Sophie rahl,GB,1.0,"ABSOLUTELY DISGUSTED by this company!!! I have just come out of hospital and am housebound. I have a family/children to feed and had NOTHING in my house to eat. So I ordered a small food shop so we had food for the next few days, which left me with £2 in my bank. Order was due at 4pm. I waited and waited, and was getting really hungry and needed to eat as I have diabetes. At 5.20pm!!!!!!! I received a email to say my order has been CANCELLED & I won’t receive a refund for 3-5 working days!!! Amazon said Morrisons cancelled it, and Morrisons says Amazon cancelle it!!! So I called up and said what do I do about food? Me and my children will now be without ANY food & I can’t order from anywhere else as I used ALL my money on the food order!!! I was offered a pathetic £20 credit which is absolutely useless as all the delivery slots had gone and there wasn’t anymore until tomorrow. So me and my family will be left hungry now for 3-5 days until my refund. Which also , they are WORKING days so could even be next week now. I have an incurable illness and am a vunerable person & have a special needs child too. I rely on Amazon everyday to deliver essentials and never experienced this level of disgraceful treatment in my life. It’sactu illegal to leave a vulnerable person without food for 24hours and the company is supposed to HELP make alternative arrangements.",2.0,259,0.9999999999719105,2.808953070143616e-11,32.90521592961536,Low Trust
