debbie harlin,US,1.0,"I purchased a Nintendo Switch eCards for my grandson for $35 2 days ago and the code never came through and kept saying pending verification.  I thought it didn't go through so I tried again... another ecard for $35 same thing happened.  I thought they were just busy and by in the morning it would be emailed to me.  The next morning it's not there so I decided to call Amazon Customer Service.  You can't call at first you have to chat...acts like a robot with robot script and asks if there was a payment problem and I answered no.  Matter of fact the night before I logged onto GameStop and downloaded the same card with no problem.  The robot then tells me they will research and let me know something in 3 business days.  So this morning, Monday, I get an email that the process has started and gave me a phone number.  I called and got a nice woman who said nothing was wrong with the payment and she transferred me to the Digital Department.  This young man said my account was locked because of suspected fraud.  I told him that it wasn't fraud I did order both of them.  He said my account was locked for 24hours and that it has been sent to the fraud department to investigate.  I asked to speak to a supervisor.  This supposed supervisor I am quite sure was not one!!!  Never once did they say I am sorry for your inconvenience...or that this has happened.  Every answer was from a script and then they ask did we answer your concerns...and I said No...they get an attitude and keep reading the same line.  I asked to speak to the supervisors supervisor and was told you can only talk to one a day???!!!!  Why I suspect he wasn't a supervisor was that he referenced and quoted the guy before who I had no problem with...I just wanted them to unlock my account now and he couldn't do it.  What I find to be hypocritical and suspicious is that when you get the phone number to call and you call it before they will talk to you... they send you a text message that you have to respond verifying through that message that it is you!!!  But through this purchase they can't verify by like text message??!!  GameStop sent me a text with a code to verify instantly and I got the codes instantly.  GameStop is not as big as Amazon, however, they must have better programmers than Amazon.  Learned my lesson...never buying digital from Amazon again.  Always go to a stand a lone store site they are better equipped and so grateful for the purchase!",1.0,452,0.9999997556169924,2.443830076082065e-07,35.070118781124584,Low Trust
