Tar,GB,1.0,"So it shouldn’t surprise you that Amazon has an incandescent contempt for you as a customer….….for our government for being unable to make them pay their taxes….And as an organisation has become almost unimaginably powerful, far more so than most countries…..….And that, inevitable as it may seem, this - Amazon - is what will replace the Nation State to the eternal detriment of Mankind.If you all stopped buying junk to fill that empty space in your lives and looked elsewhere for fulfilment then Amazon would fail and YOU would be less miserable.",633.0,92,0.9999997049340479,2.9506595211614695e-07,31.03198334555784,Low Trust
Sophie Emerson,GB,1.0,"I was, up till recently a very active and avid Amazon customer, purchasing more than I could really afford to each month on very regular basis. Usually on frivolous items ordering just because I liked how something looked, or maybe because of the rave reviews. Etc..... Anyway, up until recently I would turn a blind eye to how Amazon made their money, because it suited me to. Well no more! I am appalled at the revised returns policy, yes it's bad enough that we have to pay to sometimes return items(although I do partially understand the reasoning behind, not that I am happy about it!) but it is the fact there were no CLEAR prior instructions that annoys the BeJesus out of me! These changes, these policy instructions should be made very clear and not hidden - so that it is clear to ALL concerned so they can make a WELL INFORMED decision whether they would still like to purchase the items or not. STOP BEING SO CONNIVING!!!!!!So, although there is a silver lining, it is with sadness that I have to inform Amazon, I shall only be purchasing essential items for the foreseeable future, items i cannot otherwise obtain elsewhere! (Good reason to save my money - many thanks for your assistance and consideration of my monetary wellbeing!!!)",1.0,219,0.9999997042943005,2.957056994823404e-07,32.456548716860965,Low Trust
