Kenny,DK,5.0,I ordered two sunglasses they came pretty fast!. Quick serice fast shipping! Nothing wrong with my order! Stop buying wish crap start buying on Amazon! Always look for three stars products and up ! Theres a chance for you get a nice product and good service!!.I don’t think Amazon is bad!,42.0,51,0.9999826167061566,1.7383293843376002e-05,150.57293871040164,High Trust
Summer G,US,1.0,"I've been with Amazon Prime at least 5 years, probably more like 7 or 8.  Today I was on the amazon.com site browsing when a little pop-up window solicits me, saying... ""download the amazon app and we will give you $10 off a $20 purchase""... I went ahead and clicked the link provided within the pop up ad. It downloaded the amazom app and I resumed browsing. After putting $20 of items in my cart, went to check out, and low and behold there was no $10 credit as advertised in the promotional pop up! I called customer service and after being on the phone for over a half hour and speaking to two different people I had no choice but to cancel my Prime Membership. WHY do I want to be with a company that doesn't stand by their own words!?! They solicited me with an offer so I'm not really sure what's going through their heads right now...but apparently they need the $10 more than I do, bless  their little heart! All i can say is if they dont want to honor their promotions maybe they shouldn't solicit people with little pop up windows ....The funny thing is not only did I cancel my Prime membership (for which they will have to refund me 120...) but I will not be renewing it again in the future!!!So they lost 120 this year and 100's in future years....Overall this was more of a blessing in disguise... now I'm free!!!I won't have to pay 120 a year for free shipping which I use but a handful of times each year. Otherwise the only other service I was using was Amazon video... and between you and me it leaves a lot to be desired. Nothing that Netflix or Hulu cant do as well... if not better.",1.0,304,0.9999824915352935,1.750846470649492e-05,33.41085859766045,Low Trust
PMB,GB,1.0,"Absolutely appalling customer service. Been an Amazon Customer for over 18 years, mostly without incident although there have been some hiccups along the way.  In mid Feb I ordered a Punkcase for iphone but got a case for Galaxy S9 instead. Initiated the returns process and sent that one back and got my refund and then ordered a new one. New one came OK ... but now have recieved email saying they want to ""Recharge"" me £29.99 because   ""I didnt return the iphone case but returned a Galaxy S9 case instead""  !!   Have spent the last 26 days going back and forward via email and phone calls and no-one seems to be able to sort this out. Last straw was today when I got talking to a ""Customer Agent"" who basically said that a ""Specialist Team"" will contact me within 72 hours via email and I will have to regurgitate the whole story all over again to them for the 4th time. Apparantly then are not allowed to contact the customer via phone.  What a terrible terrible way to treat your customers in 2023.  I am on the cusp of shutting down my Amazon Prime account, scrapping my Amazon Firesticks and dumping my Kindles in the bin if they cannot sort this out.  Will update in due course.UPDATE:  So ... basically they did respond to my issue .... email stating that they have reviewed the situation .... and understand my concerns ... but thier decision is final and they would ""likely not respond to further emails about this issue""  !!!    How absolutely shabby is that for customer service !!    And they had the cheek to add that I can ""continue to shop as usual on Amazon"" !   I DONT THINK SO !!       I have now closed my Prime account, scrapped a couple of Firesticks and given away my Echo dots to family. I will Never shop at Amazon again.",8.0,319,0.9999820735262122,1.7926473787843733e-05,33.5791352468526,Low Trust
Francesca,ES,1.0,"Don’t ever use Amazon.es! Faulty items that Amazon does not want to take responsibility for even though it was Amazon that sold and delivered it. I bought some baby items well in time for the baby’s arrival. I had a quick look to see if everything was there and it looked fine but obviously didn’t put it up including a travel cot/changer as I wasn’t due any time at that point, I got it early just in case as you never know when the baby decides to come. When I did get to put it all up, there was a clip missing to hold the changer up safely onto the cot, this is something I would t know was missing without the whole thing up and reading instructions etc. I contacted Amazon and they shrugged it off saying the policy is complain within 30 days. This isn’t realistic for this sinario but they didn’t want to know. I only wanted the missing item! I didn’t want a refund or a return, I just wanted the clip which I am unable to buy separately. They didn’t care and didn’t want to know!! It’s so black and white with Amazon and will use anything to avoid responsibility and to compensate a faulty item! I might as well paid a lot less for the same item as I am unable to use the other aspects. It’s now just a travel cot. I paid €110 for a travel cot!!! Don’t bother! Go to a shop or use a different online sight!",1.0,257,0.9999816151691142,1.8384830885787018e-05,32.883701069923426,Low Trust
Izzy,AU,1.0,"I contacted the Amazon prime customer service chat option when my 30 day free trial stopped working after 2 days because it was trying to take money out of my account. Spoke with someone called Zee. Beyond angry and frustrated with the experience I had. Yes she was polite, very professional, I will give her that. But my god, no matter what I said she asked the same question over and over insinuating that the free trial not working was my fault because I don’t have funds in my card. Hun it’s a free trial!! I then was made to add a new card THREE TIMES because she did not listen when I told her I updated it the first time! She then told me my only option was to cancel the subscription and resubscribe and pay!! And that I’d have to wait on a refund which I was not going to believe after she had been extremely useless!! All of this way over one hour! She then magically fixed the issue which made me even angrier as she could’ve done that in the first place instead of insisting the only option was either update my card or cancelling and resubscribing! A simple 10 minute query turned into a one hour fiasco! Never again",1.0,214,0.9999814400342921,1.8559965707876103e-05,32.40137668028203,Low Trust
Daniela & Markus,PH,1.0,"Selling overpriced products!! 🤬😡 I BOUGHT 2 WD 4TB PASSPORT external hard drives, 95$ each!! Found them in shoppee ph for 80$ only!! Return via DHL offered! THE PROBLEM IS: THETE IS NO DHL WHERE I LIVE!! INSANE LONG INTERNATIONAL DELIVERY TIMES 😡Order #112-4446488-8299468Order #112-6360506-7617806",53.0,45,0.9999811454480948,1.88545519052008e-05,30.505709973809502,Low Trust
Lashonda,US,3.0,"I would give 5 stars and here’s why I’m not. I’ve been using amazon for several years now and they have been great! Especially with prime. Now, here recently they have started delivering packages with their blue or white vans. Every since they started,  I’ve had quite a few issues! I’ve have packages that never showed and had to end up getting my money back or have them resend it. Claiming that my house was not accessible! I’ve been staying here for over a year and NEVER have I had an issue until they started using the random people in these vans! I checked videos from the cameras around my house and it showed where these people are throwing my packages!! I wish I could post the videos!!! Come on amazon you have to do better!",1.0,136,0.9999810849000019,1.8915099998073615e-05,91.5264645435585,High Trust
Debbi Murray,GB,1.0,"What on earth has happened to Amazon?! The overseas customer service is dire! Prime has now become a rip off £1.99 for next day delivery, Amazon has become the worst platform to purchase from! Ordered a Worx grass strimmer for £108 my status was updated to ‘delivered to neighbour’ NOT TRUE we live in a gated complex with CCTV plus we haven’t been out today, no way any of our 4 neighbours was handed my parcel!! CCTV checked no deliveries today! Rang Amazon they said call back in 48 hours…didn’t take them 48 hours to take my money! I had to ask the agent to slow down as I couldn’t understand a word he was saying. Get a grip Geoff, I am cancelling my Prime subscription definitely NOT a platform I am prepared to pay for…remember if your purchase is over £100 you can always do a charge back via your credit card company in the UK! Amazon seem to be reluctant to admit they ARE responsible for your refund regardless of them saying it’s the sellers responsibility! UK law is probably different to USA law but we also have a 14 day cooling off period in the UK regardless of what the so call customer service advisor says!",2.0,209,0.9999789541482469,2.10458517531098e-05,32.345415725004926,Low Trust
