Mohamed M. Elgadhafi,JO,1.0,"I've been a customer since 2008 and these few last weeks I faced several problems with shipping. I was shocked with Amazon's customer service! Unbelievable! I have tried both online chat and emails, and you feel you are talking to a robot! At least robots analyze and provide solutions! But that's not the case with Amazon's customer service! They keep copy and paste the same answer over and over regardless of what you say or what data you provide! A hopeless case!! And of course, after all these chats and emails, my case is not resolved.",2.0,96,0.9998103149914237,0.00018968500857630133,31.086321042352537,Low Trust
Lee J,GB,1.0,"*DO NOT TRUST AMAZON*Everyone who has EVER purchased anything on Amazon check all of your bank statements very closely. Look for Prime that you have never subscribed to also for Amazon Music. When you place an order with a third party seller, they (Amazon) have a habit of ""accidentally"" signing you up to one of these subscription services and charging to ANY CARD that has been used to buy a product. Even if it is not in the name of the person who holds the Amazon account.Example! My 70 year old mother was being billed for Amazon music, she did not even know about this. It went on for months. Finally yesterday I got to the cause of it and Amazon has agreed to refund ALL 8 wrongfully claimed payments from a pensioner. That amounted to almost £80 STOLEN from a vulnerable person.They also agreed to refund the £9.99 STOLEN from my card. It only came to my attention when I used my mothers Amazon to order an item from a third party seller. When I checked my card. I had been charged £9.99 for Amazon music, as my mother's registered card was lost and had to be cancelled and replaced. So Amazon took the money without authorisation from my account. Just to add. I have now been charged £1 by amazon only a day after this scamming, thieving, fraudulent bunch of vultures ""apologised"" for stealing money. I therefore deleted both my card and my mother's card from amazon. I suggest EVERYONE does the same. If you buy anything on Amazon, DO NOT STORE YOUR CARD!!! Simply input it for each transaction. Your money is NOT SAFE!! Better than that NEVER USE AMAZON. We never will again!!Had this not happened, and I had not been charged my mother would never have known about this and Amazon would have continued pocketing her money. Along with their tax avoidance schemes. So be warned. This company openly admitted to me that the system sometimes ""accidentally"" subscribes when a purchase is made. The person who scripted Amazon's website must be a total amateur if this is what happens. So everyone get checking you statements, if you see one payment to AMAZON MUSIC or AMAZON PRIME, that you have not asked for, go to your bank (or call them) Order statements dating back to when you first started using Amazon. You may find more unauthorised charges. Also if you have elderly parents who use amazon help them check their account. Amazon do not pay tax correctly, why should they also get away with STEALING from vulnerable people.My mother's was almost £80, your refund could be more, It depends how long it has been ongoing. But every penny they have taken without permission will be refunded. And Amazon if you're reading this. ALL CARDS have now been removed from your scummy site and not one more order will be placed using Amazon. Sorry this is a long post but it needed explaining in case amazon are stealing from others. They certainly won't check their end, as long as they get their money coming in. So ensure you all check.I would love to have replies on here of anyone who checks their account and finds they have been unknowingly charged. I know for a fact amazon do it frequently, my bank told me this and even said they refund people OFTEN. So there is a good chance of you being owed and I would love to hear about your situation.Thanks for reading.",56.0,585,0.9998095407029425,0.0001904592970575214,36.571497165638064,Low Trust
Cara Dschaak,US,1.0,"If I could leave a negative star rating, I would. They have MAJOR PROBLEMS with their system! I had ordered a CPAP pillow last week, paid for it, received it with absolutely no problems. Then three days later I received an email telling me my payment was declined. Of course, I was confused to what was going on; I  didn't have to dig very long to see that a completely different order of the same CPAP pillow, made on my account with my name, and the reason they were saying my payment declined was bc they had used a credit card (marked as the default card for some reason) I had on the list of cards I've used in the past that no longer worked (I had closed the account a few months ago); this ""order"" even had an entirely DIFFERENT ORDER NUMBER! This is NOT a case of someone anonymously trying to scam a free CPAP pillow; this is a case of THEIR SYSTEM making a random second order for some strange reason, and even tried to collect payment for it a SECOND TIME! And no, I of course did not authorize or was even aware of this! Actually, this has happened twice before, and I of course contacted them immediately and explained what was going on; the customer service rep didn't know really what to say or do about it, as she is just an employee earning a paycheck. But she would not let me speak to a supervisor or anything! She did not do anything about it, and how is a person expected to feel safe shopping on their site when they make random multiple orders at the person's expense? All I can say is I think IT'S A VERY BIG DEAL, and I'm not done making ""noise"" about it either! I hope everyone reads this, bc it's bad enough with all thieves and scammers out there, but you also need to worry about these huge shopping websites (Amazon has been around a long time and they're supposed to guarantee that you're safe) making random repeated orders and taking your money, probably hoping you won't notice? They've gotten too big for themselves and something is going on with them! I'd watch out with Amazon if I were you!!",6.0,381,0.9998074729100256,0.0001925270899744147,34.283322372446,Low Trust
Heart Breaker,US,3.0,3 stars is being generous right now! I am so disgusted with these people I could scream!I will summarize to the best of my ability. They are playing games with the way they bill things out and being denied. When they originally debit my card for the total...that amount is set aside for them for up to 10 days. Then they have to finalize when they ship. They are changing the information or something when they finalize resulting in a denial. So I was forced to put money onto my gift card balance and shop that way. Which by the way is taken from my debit card IMMEDIATELY WITH NO PROBLEMS. So I purchased 2 pair of leather boots for work but returned them both. I started looking elsewhere for boots until Amazon informed me that I would NOT be getting my money back!! They put it back on the gift card but will not give me a refund to my debit card. Which now means that I have to save up that money AGAIN to buy boots somewhere else.Being that they were attempting to bill the WRONG DEBIT CARD they were also denied and since have suspended my account. After being on the telephone for at least 3 hours and 4 representatives I have been informed that they are going to KEEP MY MONEY! They told me that they cannot reinstate my account... that I have to sign up all over again. But they WILL NOT transfer my credit balance to the new account and they will not refund it to my debit card! EVERY BIT of this is THEIR FAULT. I don't know what kind of SHADY AF accounting practices they have but it is what has caused ALL of this chaos. And as a result I have to be the one to pay for it. They have me so mad that I told them that I will not be doing business with them any longer so now they HAVE to refund my money. THEY WILL NOT! This is truly unbelievable!,4.0,343,0.9998047962619827,0.00019520373801729107,93.85720830804499,High Trust
Mary Grace Parde,US,1.0,"My android phone broke, had to get new phone with new number. Got locked out of my Amazon account. Their customer service was terrible! They wouldn't help me regain access and I was a huge user of their products with numerous subscriptions. They treated me like a criminal, wouldn't help me regain access and said I failed their security tests when they asked me questions about my last orders and I couldn't remember exact details, but had already confirmed charged amounts, account information, credit card numbers, etc. It was the most ridiculous experience!! I could hear them taking pleasure in telling me, ""Sorry, you failed to answer the questions to our satisfaction...."" I wanted to reach through my phone to ring their necks! I already spoke to one, gathered needed info, called back and they threw another ridiculous question at me!! Closing account and credit card. They suck!! 😞",3.0,149,0.9998045152388285,0.00019548476117148272,31.68111467552352,Low Trust
Jack L,US,1.0,Beware!!!Amazon marked down an item and did not advertise it as a Prime Deal or one Day sale the next morning it was full price!  Customer Service said there was nothing they could do about it!!!!,2.0,36,0.9998024643345396,0.00019753566546043544,30.413690580244417,Low Trust
Robert Drake,US,1.0,"The return process is a rip-off! I bought something and it was much larger than expected.  I wanted to return it.  During the process, I had a couple of options, first print my own return label in which the charge was over 13 Dollars!  Expletive (I can't use bad language)! 13 Dollars to print your own return label!!! The second was just to drop it off for free at the UPS store.  I had used the latter method before and it took well over two months to get a partial refund.  I never got a full refund.  Calling the service center took such a long time on the phone with someone who barely spoke English. On my current return, they said it would take over a month to ""process"" the return!  Expelitive! In years past, I would get a refund once the item was scanned in at the UPS center.  Why are they holding my money for so long?!  I have been an Amazon shopper for years.  I think that in the future I  will be looking to other online retailers.",5.0,181,0.9998009561502523,0.00019904384974767098,32.04023822726024,Low Trust
Paul Hensel,US,1.0,I'm giving Amazon a ONE Rating for poor customer service. The simple fact is that I have called numerous times over a month and half with the promise of rectifying my account that has been hacked. They have not returned one phone call they have asked me to wait 24 - 48 hours to receive. I have been unable to order anything because my account is closed down and the Prime Membership I paid for is Gone!!! I am waiting and am NOT HAPPY!!!!!,1.0,84,0.9997885091378639,0.00021149086213612112,30.95280673604006,Low Trust
Brian Lehman,US,1.0,"I made a purchase and amazon FROZE MY ACCOUNT saying its suspicious activity... Buying online from amazon i thought was the point but instead of CALLING MY REGISTERED NUMBERED ON THE ACCOUNT its been froze for over 48 hours. I sent in 4 documents of proof, 2- 30min. phone calls and still nothing! Meanwhile doing so crashed my deviced (amazon fire) lost ALL MY INFORMATION i cannot access 5 accounts now all frozen from this! Cant register this cause accounts froze, cant access other accounts from a unregistered location and device!!! NOW 600 I LOST WHO IS GOING TO PAY ME BACK AMAZON!?!?! Also ""alex"" a supervisor on a recorded call admitted and said it was their mistake and amazon will reimburse me for at least the cost of my purchase.",1.0,131,0.999786249636554,0.00021375036344595255,31.480121057151543,Low Trust
Ife salami,IE,1.0,"if i could rate 0 stars I would!! i am normally a happy customer of amazon but as of lately i cannot trust this website! their currency exchange is completely exploiting and i recently purchased an item that was supposedly “refurbished,” yet it did not even work! i am DISAPPOINTED, OUTRAGED AND UPSET to say the least!! not to mention, their AWFUL customer service! i now to pay for shipping to post back my item and had previously paid for shipping that i will not be getting back! ANGRY CUSTOMER HERE.",3.0,91,0.9997851167827683,0.00021488321723173165,31.031495703205948,Low Trust
Jenn,GB,1.0,AMAZON order 206-8734269 -5562714If I could leave Zero I would 🤬Amazon are fine when all goes well .We assumed all goods came directly from Amazon… WRONG!!They continue to buy from SCAMMERS!!And ignore customer concerns..Hoping you will go away ..We bought a rug from Amazon  27th September 23 .. when it arrived it was a different colour and quality from the sales picture….So thought ah it’s ok …It’s  AMAZON ..Returns are easy ..WRONG!!!!!🤬🤬🤬🤬 So ..You buy the rug through AMAZON…You dont return to AMAZON but to an empty yard (see photos in TRUST PILOT) to a company called VICEROY BEDDING…..The return is not through the seller (AMAZON) but a 3rd party (VICEROY BEDDING) with completely different returns arrangement from what you are used to with AMAZON .🤔🤔🤔🤔.. is this legal ?VICEROY seem to be a front ..A made up company..(See other reviews on TRUST PILOT)You then try and seek resolution with AMAZON…Nearly 4 months VICEROY.. and AMAZON BOTS turning us around in circles ..No refund despite goods being returned..Look at trust pilot pics of depot…😳So has anyone from AMAZON actually checked VICEROY out ?Do they comply with Modern slavery Rules…Something is seriously wrong here and AMAZON are doing nothing..ALL Potential AMAZON customers should not buy goods unless directly stocked by AMAZON..Or better still buy elsewhere..Be warned ..CMON AMAZON sort this out please ..,24.0,222,0.9997840390361045,0.00021596096389553399,32.50098312951839,Low Trust
Susie Melo,US,1.0,"Amazon customer service has plummeted over the past year or so.  Now they are making returns harder and charging if you use UPS.  They are also requiring a copy of your ID which is unacceptable!! They claim they need to identify us but they don't seem to need that to take our money!!  That is invasive and opens us up to identity theft in the event they get hacked like everyone else.  I will never give them this!!!  To make matters worse any phone call to customer service takes far too long.  Now, after you've spent 10-15 minutes with a customer service rep they often say they need to transfer the call and you sit in yet another long queue waiting for that person to help and they are less inclined to resolve problem easily putting the burden on the customer.I recently ordered 2 gallons of fuel stabilizer.  After multiple emails that it had been delayed, I called to cancel the order because I was leaving town.  They said they couldn't, but as soon as they could locate te product they would refund my money.  Then, I got emails saying the product ""was likely delivered on December 2nd"", when it wasn't.  They still would not refund my money.  They said I had to wait until after December 12th - almost 2 weeks and I would have to call back and go thru the process all over again.  Finally, after 4 phone calls and over 2 hours of wasted  time, they refunded my money for ""their"" mistake.  Yesterday, I received a $16 item that was not as described online and they wanted a copy of my drivers license or ID.  Well I told them to take a hike.  Instead of placing my next order on Amazon I bought several hundred dollars worth of goods between Walmart and Home Depot and even saved money!!  I will be cancelling Prime and using Amazon as little as possible in the future.",4.0,327,0.9997829632495016,0.00021703675049844495,33.6788271600151,Low Trust
CeeCee,US,5.0,"I order the  book called The Molding of Him AUTHOR is George K.L.Smith. Amazon was right on time with my book. When I received my book I couldn't put it down it was sooooooooo good! I was delighted to see a Man put out a positive book for us sisters to read. George book was so good I didn't want to put it down.  George gets straight to the point, I love it! I really enjoy his questions he has you ask yourself after each chapter! God is so good! Thanks for this book George  K. L.Smith I have taken your advice and I have start using your ideas on communicating with my mate! IT WORKSSSSSSSS ! THANK YOU GEORGE K. L.SMITH I REALLY ENJOYED YOUR BOOK, I CANT WAIT FOR The Molding  of  Her! I  have read this book twice now and it got delivered on April 6,2020!",1.0,149,0.9997827748967454,0.00021722510325461464,151.68220169262767,High Trust
