Althea,US,1.0,"ONCE AGAIN; MY PACKAGES WERE DELIVERED TO SOMEONE WHO IS NOT ME!!! I ORDERED SODAS (HEAVY WEIGHT, RIGHT?); YET I ACTUALLY RECEIVED SOMEONE ELSE'S SMALL LITE WEIGHT PACKAGE.... AND OF COURSE THERE WAS NO KNOCK ON MY DOOR NOTIFYING ME OF THE DELIVERY!! ARE THEY AFRAID THEY MAY HAVE TO INTERACT WITH THE PEOPLE WHOSE ORDER THEY MESSED UP??!!!THE TOPPER WAS WHEN I WAS TOLD BY CUSTOMER SERVICE TO JUST KEEP THE PACKAGE THAT WASN'T MINE.... I ASKED HER WASN'T THAT ILLEGAL AND SHE MUMBLED OFF SOMETHING. I EXPLAINED I WOULD NOT DO SUCH A THING. I ALSO ASKED WHY THE DRIVER COULD NOT JUST RETURN?... ONCE AGAIN I GOT THE COMPANY LINE........I'M SURE YOU'LL BE HEARING FROM ME AGAIN BECAUSE IF NOTHING ELSE; YOU CAN BE GUARANTEED THAT THIS IS A REGULAR OCCURRING PROBLEM FOR ME WITH AMAZON DELIVERY DRIVERS AND CUSTOMER SERVICE. ",6.0,144,0.9997410465583899,0.00025895344161008804,31.628202859966088,Low Trust
Customer A,US,1.0,"AWFUL. REALLY GONE DOWNHILL. This happens a lot lately. If I have 1 problem, suddenly I have 10. Customer Service is embarrassing when before I would've said they had the best of any company. In 7 days Amazon has screwed up 5 out of 6 packages; resulting in 4 calls totaling over 2 hrs. (so far...) that STILL has NOT completely resolved issues (still don't have items or my refunds...). The really weird part is that each problem was different; but the WORST part is that Customer Service (for the most part) has been HORRENDOUS causing situations to escalate! I worked in Customer Service for years & it's really quite simple... Admit you're wrong, apologize and RESOLVE issue (and when company ROYALLY screws up, like in my situation, you proactively offer compensation to show you value your customer). PERIOD. What you do NOT do is talk over customer, cut them off, continually place them on hold, transfer them & ask them to repeat their story again & again only to have it repeated back INCORRECTLY again & again; IF something does finally get resolved DO NOT USE THE WORDS ""as a 1 time courtesy"" --ahhhh....THAT IS SOOOO RUDE TO SAY THAT BASICALLY YOU ARE DOING ME A FAVOR BY FIXING YOUR MISTAKE! WORDING MATTERS PEOPLE. Also DO NOT ARGUE W/ THE CUSTOMER OVER THIS! I mean MY GOD. ARE YOU SERIOUS?? Also enough w/ the fake ""ahhhs"" like you're soothing a baby. TRAIN YOUR INDIANS IN AMERICAN WAYS PLEASE. THESE METHODS ARE RUDE IN OUR CULTURE. THIS IS NOT EMPATHY. IT IS CONSIDERED PATRONIZING, RUDE, INCONSIDERATE OR JUST PLAIN NOT PAYING ATTENTION. Issues TOTAL in 7 days: 1. Wrong model of phone case sent resulting in return. 2. Received EMPTY package (CLEARLY open where the flap wasn't put down correctly at top and my items slid out somewhere during transportation/delivery; you could see in the pic that Amazon took of the delivered item in front of my door that the package was wide open, LOL! Called & 1 rep offered refund AND free replacement immediately (very nice & good at his job); however NEXT rep talked over me, cut me off constantly, repeated herself & used my credit resulting in a callback 2 days later to ANOTHER rude rep that argued, talked over me, cut me off, blah blah blah for 45 min. to then FINALLY ""do me the courtesy"" of returning the credit... 3. Different phone case ordered, arrived in my city at 7:30 am, yet by 8 pm (guaranteed delivery by 9pm); called Amazon & they said they had no driver so they offered a $5 credit & promised it would be delivered next day (ok, no problem) yet when didn't arrive next day I checked & it looked like package was delivered through app yet when I clicked on ""tracking"" it said item shipped to another state at 3:50am (??) and then BACK to MY city/state at 3 PM where it was then supposedly ""damaged"" and shipped back to seller... (do WHAT???). HOWEVER when I called Amazon THEY said item showed ""on hold at shipper"" and they didn't know why, so they marked it as REFUSED BY BUYER!!! (so now THAT'S on my acct. along w/ fact that I don't have my product or refund...) 4. The SAME day that my phone case was supposedly ""damaged"" I was supposed to receive a bath product but it was ALSO supposedly ""damaged"" & shipped back to seller... (when I tried to ask Amazon about the refund re: this product they were ""having computer issues"" after I'd already given tracking numbers multi times, been on hold, xferred around, explained story over & over... so they couldn't tell if refund was issued... 5. An item I ordered FIVE days ago (also on same day I ordered 2 other items separately w/ no problems, BTW) & scheduled for delivery tomorrow, SUDDENLY shows that I need to ""update my payment method"". Do WHAT??? I have the email confirmation from FIVE days ago and after 100's of orders I have NEVER had Amazon wait FIVE days to charge for something... They just DON'T do that... ALSO there is a GC Balance on my acct. that is technically my 1st payment/default payment option anyway, but for some reason REFUSES to allow me to use it for this $6. They had NO explanation for this and just kept saying to ""check w/ my bank"", LOL!! THAT IS NOT THE QUESTION. WHAT IS GOING ON AMAZON????",1.0,749,0.9997378680246145,0.0002621319753854934,38.414676985757495,Low Trust
mr vytautas markevicius,GB,1.0,"worst site to buy somethink ,i had enough with them any item you buy its very very bad quality !!! i was reading reviews before but now i know all of them is fake !!!",75.0,35,0.9997369187259272,0.00026308127407281834,30.405750810759162,Low Trust
Bex,NZ,1.0,"Your delivery drivers in Florida are little more than dump n dash drivers!!!At the complex I work for they literally just get the package out of the delivery vehicle scan it and toss it anywhere - never actually deliver to the receivers apartment, they don’t even have the courtesy to come to the office so we know there are parcels for our residents, the team just randomly stumble upon randomly deposited parcels around the grounds of the complex - lord only knows how many we don’t find that get misappropriated by non residents!I know the issue is not our building as now other parcels are randomly put by the lift doors or stashed near the storage units, ONLY those coming from Amazon.Perhaps a team building event focused on orienteering for the delivery drivers might be an idea so they understand the importance of getting to a specified area rather than just in the general vicinity!!!Sort it out please!",1.0,158,0.9997365207399481,0.0002634792600518798,31.785467849710393,Low Trust
Mike Robinson,GB,1.0,"I’ve been with amazon for years & spent thousands! But this last few months have been beyond a joke! Has Mr bean taken control? Parcels left on the street! App says “handed to the occupant” WHAT!? I’m 5 miles away and you can’t be bothered to use a ring doorbell?? After that experience I started using my parents address for delivery…today I’ve had a wrong order £180 spent and got a box of plasters!???  An hour later trying to fix it & end up with rude customer support talking over me, clearly going to make a loss  and still no further forward! Personally I think they have become to automated for their own good! & have forgotten about good customer service! Guess who won’t be renewing prime this year….",2.0,129,0.9997346866289627,0.00026531337103730124,31.46026510769937,Low Trust
Desiree Brown,US,1.0,"Oh where to start.First the customer service is a JOKE. Can barely speak a lick of English and most the time have an attitude. The past few times I've ordered from amazon I've had issues. I ordered a phone and it didnt work. It said 'unlocked' and it wasn't. Took them 3 months to send me a return label!!!!This week I ordered something twice by accident, the representative told me i could just write the words ""return to sender"" to get my refund back (the double order was honestly my own mistake). I got an email claiming since I wrote return to sender and it got sent to Amazon's warehouse, I wouldnt receive my full refund because I didn't have a 'return label. I was told i had to pay the extra fees for amazon to return it. Yet the representative I spoke too was the one who told me to write that on the package. I also ordered 2 tablets for my kids for they're easter baskets. The same I D I O T who told me about the labels told me the item looked fine, the payment was accepted etc. Again, I got an email claiming the payment was declined. And They claim my payment never went through, yet my bank statement said different. A purchase of $49.00 and i had over $200.00 in my account, how did it get declined? My bank statement shows the exact time and date when the money was taken and it clearly says amzn (they shorten most the words lol)Amazon is like walmart, they seem to hire anyone off the street and dont care about customers, they only care about being competitive to other stires instead of the customers. So now I'm out of almost 50.00 because the employees heads are so far up they're asses. I'll stick with EBAY! I've used them for a good 9+ years and only had one tiny issue that again my own fault and they fixed it.Thats 2 places ill never shop again, walmart and Amazon If you want good quality...Amazon isnt worth the hassle!!!!",1.0,349,0.9997300552775764,0.00026994472242358736,33.928247656760554,Low Trust
Nicole Bailey,US,1.0,"Dont get me wrong Amazon USED to be one of my favorite places to shop until I found out Prime does NOT mean 2 day delivery more like 4, which is even more crazy because it's a membership IM PAYING FOR that they definitely get their money for! Then the non-English speaking, insensitive representatives dont know no more than you do and their attitudes is HORRIBLE. I'm not spending any more money with them I'll go to the store first. And although their a big company that wont do anything about this I hope this helps someone else with NOT spending their money here. EBAY HERE I COME!!!!!!!",2.0,108,0.9997217581544122,0.00027824184558777887,31.22535348319358,Low Trust
James,GB,2.0,"Was a very good site until the recent 18+ verification policy was bought in and now if you order anything that is 18+ you will have to wait in all day to receive your package so you can provide id( identification for a parcel, have you lost your minds?! ) completely defeats the object of having prime as parcels are delayed due to this issue .I will not be buying another 18+ item from amazon and will be reducing my usage of it due to this issue . There is no need to provide Identification as I have ordered the item from my account which I pay for myself , and the package is addressed to me no one else therefore it is my responsibility not Amazon’s .... what a shamblesAlso a side note . Amazons customer service is appalling the staff are not helpful and quite frankly don’t care and the lack of English speaking staff just says it all . The amazon system is down and now and I am unable to even contact amazon about my account ..... what is going on !!!!!!",54.0,186,0.9997168383137057,0.0002831616862942754,62.10052936866693,Medium Trust
Amanda Connick,IE,1.0,"Absolute scam... cancelled my membership because money was taken out of my account every month and never used Amazon prime, I requested a refund, instead of giving me a refund they took €88.67 out of my account with out my permission, when I emailed customer service, they replied with asked for a charge ID and they would be happy to refund me. I questioned what the charge ID was and they did not explain what it was... they wanted me to contact them AGAIN, which I did and no response.  I am still waiting on my refund and still not getting any sort of help from customer service. No customer service number for Ireland to deal with complaints, absolute joke!!!!!! I did not sign up for Amazon prime!! It was an app on a phone that I purchased and somehow got my bank details",1.0,144,0.9997127978945246,0.0002872021054753926,31.629615293159354,Low Trust
