Becky,US,1.0,"Terrible terrible customer service today!! Have not experienced that in all my time w Amazon....boo!!!! To bad your company can’t get that piece right. We (the customers) helped build your empire, treat us right. Solve the problem or fix it. Not that hard of a concept. Don’t offer me 10% off of a fire stick remote when YOU deemed it defective! Purchased six month ago and it’s defective....that’s on you. I know a remote is small but the point is I paid for it once and it’s defective.....it’s the principal of the thing",2.0,93,0.9997019961861923,0.00029800381380773455,31.058085832866496,Low Trust
evu lix,DE,1.0,"DONT buy gift cards, they steal your money!!! Contacting their service doesn't help at all!!!I'm disappointed in Amazon. I have never experienced such a bad experience with any company in my life! I wanted to make a gif for my boyfriend who lives in another country. His birthday was coming soon and I wanted to surprise him. Because I was saving up money and they weren't in my bank account I decided to just buy a gift card. I made my order for a gaming monitor selected as a gift.Everything was going well till I got an email saying that my account is on hold. I tried to call the service multiple times in German( because I bought it in Germany) and English. I have over 30 calls with Amazon service. The situation didn't get any better, I also didn't get any emails. The ones I sent get deleted or I get a response from their system, not a human! When I log into my account I get a message to check my email and I can't do anything else except log out. I have checked in other categories such as spam or archive... The only way to contact them is to call them.Throughout the call, I got different answers every time. After every call, I have to wait more than 72 hours and contact them back, wait again, the same thing over and over again. I even got asked multiple times for proof of the bought gif card with photos showing the receipt and the spend amount. Others said that I have done something against their terms of policy, although I have read them and explained that I haven't.Overall I wasted a big amount of money, didn't get any support, wasted hours trying to explain my situation to people who don't know what they are doing, destroyed my moods multiple times, and didn't surprise a special someone.",4.0,318,0.9996963781950743,0.00030362180492571333,33.58220296349362,Low Trust
Martin Jones,GB,1.0,"Been a good and loyal customer of amazon for year's but now in the UK I must think twice!! Customer service is not available they simply don't have it, or understand what it is! This year alone I've ordered over 300 times, I'm a prime member? And I'm now treated like dirt!! Goods not delivered? But they take the money!! Getting it back is painful, I've simply had enough, I'll now shop elsewhere very very sad",40.0,76,0.9996876858278777,0.0003123141721222966,30.868111502212397,Low Trust
Janet Skipper Wise,US,1.0,"If I could subtract stars I would. Beyond frustrated!  Amazon took my $750 and did not deliver my lawnmower. In order to receive a refund,  I have to return the product.  I DO NOT HAVE A PRODUCT.  Never delivered. The stupidity of customer service is shocking and the refusal of a refund is legally shocking!!  Stay away from AMAZON!!!!",1.0,59,0.9996853411701035,0.00031465882989645255,30.677538886531273,Low Trust
Christi White,US,1.0,"What the hell has happened to Amazon?! They used to have the best customer service, now it’s gone to hell. I recently purchased an expensive watch from Amazon and they sent me an EMPTY WATCH BOX. I called to report the issue, thinking that just maybe they would be able to check their cameras and do their own due diligence since clearly someone in their facility had stolen the watch but instead, they tell me I’m the one that needs to file the police report and once I send them a copy of it, they will decide whether or not a refund will be granted! Yes, you read that correctly. I paid for an empty box and then they will decide if they want to give me a refund! I know this sounds crazy because it is!!! Nonetheless, I filed the police report and submitted it and to my surprise, I still got kickback telling me that my police report is invalid. It’s a legal document from a police department. How much more valid does it need to be?!! Unfortunately, I’ve spent almost a week of my time trying to provide them with everything Amazon needed in order to receive my money back and it’s still not enough so it looks as though I’ll just have to refuse the charge since they did not send me what I paid for. In sum, I did not receive what I paid for and in theory, I should be filing the police report on Amazon. They stole my watch and/or they are stealing my money…however you want to put it. It’s disgraceful and they should be making every bit of effort on their end to get to the bottom of this because clearly they have a thief in house.",1.0,296,0.9996775515061083,0.000322448493891736,33.336369199792735,Low Trust
ELLIE SMITH,US,1.0,"If I could leave zero stars I would. Amazon has now entered into the new world of zero customer service sadly. They removed the option of print your own label. So now you are using your own time and gas to drive to one of the Amazon return sites which are 25+ mins one way from me. $7.99 to have UPS box it up and ship the return back --that is 30 mins 1 way. Basically, Amazon is driving customer into Kohls, Staples, Whole Foods and UPS the stores THEY choose to business with!! Then they present it as trying to keep trucks off the road. Who cares if its a truck or my car. The truth is they are saving a TON of money by inconveniencing their customers!!! A return took me 1 min, put it back in the box or bag it came in, print a label, slap it on and drop it in a UPS drop box --any time of the day or night--even midnight if needed. The box is 1 min drive. Now I have to chat with an Amazon representative they email me a label it takes about 20 mins of my time. So RIDICULOUS and beyond maddening!! So happy Amazon is using their customers to save money. Is Amazon going to pay for gas and time for their customer returns to the stores they do business with?????? I do not choose to drive to any of those stores. I was a HUGE amazon customer HUGE-- I am done now--I can not take it anymore! ",1.0,260,0.9996766563453282,0.0003233436546717927,32.93260016086034,Low Trust
Jamie Valenti,US,1.0,Normally I have no issue with Amazon. Sellers have been good. Fast shipping. But my last order. They have processed and cancelled the payment over 9 times. Spoke to Amazon they are less then helpful. Telling me it will go back in my account 5-10 days. Luckily my bank is great and issues me back the over charges leaving one pending to clear. But then the next day they put in 4 more. That makes my car insurance payment bounce. Go to the bank put in money to clear that payment. Bank again gives me my money back leaving one pending. This morning I wake up to 3 charges. Wft is wrong with Amazon. All you need is ONE authorization. Not 9. That’s over 1400.00 you have pending for a 164 payment. And there remedy is to offer a 10.00 Amazon GC. Really?!?!  Do better Amazon the worst customer service there is!!!!!!,1.0,152,0.9996723635914699,0.00032763640853006315,31.721373407639064,Low Trust
Lisa Barrett (lisebrrtt),GB,1.0,"Ordered a lens on Friday for my husband it was £669 very good value and was supposedly on sale with Amazon.  It was due to arrive on Sunday.  Sunday morning I received an email informing me that the lens had to be cancelled due to unavailability and that it would take 1 - 2 business days before the money would go back on my account!! I went into Amazon where the lens was showing as still having 6 available. I finally contacted Amazon by phone, asking to speak to a Manager, there was a definitely a language barrier, I found it extremely difficult understanding what they were saying, with at least 2 customer service reps speaking very bad English, and did not understand what I wanted and basically just put the phone down on me.I could not get in touch with a manager at all, despite trying for over an hour, finally I used the chat option. I was put through to someone who said he was a member of the leadership team, who told me the 6 that were showing available, were already pre-ordered, (which is surly rubbish, as if pre-ordered surely they shouldn't show as being available).  I said that I had ordered these on Friday and if they weren't available, why had they taken the money for these out of my account?  He was not able/refused to answer that question.Earlier this week I had a generated email from Amazon, telling me I was cancelling items and if this continued they would not refund me.  When I got in touch with them about this, they said it was automatically generated email.  I pointed out that what they were saying about refunding was illegal and that, in my case, it was they who were cancelling items not I.  This is all very strange isn't it?  I have attached a picture of the lens, this I uploaded at 11.36 on Sunday 5th November, so you can see for yourselves it is still stating 6 available (NOT 6 PRE-ORDERED).  Again the 6 lens are still showing as available at 17.26pm and again at 17.50pm on Sunday 5th November.  I have taken a snap shot and can share if required.  This is very frustratingSeriously considering closing all my accounts with Amazon, having been with them for many years the level of customer service, is now non existent!!!!!",65.0,395,0.9996701009091722,0.0003298990908278121,34.44722967131088,Low Trust
