Star Dazer,US,1.0,"Placed an order, items being sent in 2 shipments both from Amazon delivery drivers. First shipment marked delivered to mailroom, no picture. Should’ve been to front door. I run down to see it’s not in there. See Amazon driver and he tells me he didn’t have a delivery for me. Call customer service and they say it was marked delivered by mistake and I’ll get it with 2nd shipment. 2nd shipment marked delivered but doesn’t say where and no picture. It’s not outside. I call Amazon and receive terrible customer service so fuming mad I drive down to the Amazon HUB customer counter. Spoke to 2 supervisors who looked into it and found that one shipment was delivered a mile away, completely different apartment complex. The other, they say they have no idea what the driver did but delivery wasn’t actually attempted. They could see this by looking up the GPS history. I now drive to the “wrong” address where they told me it was and spoke with leasing staff. My packages were not found but they did find several packages that belonged to people at MY complex, a mile away. I called Amazon customer service and explained all of this for the 10th time. Amazon then emails me a questionnaire to file a report for them to look into it, I gave them everything they asked for. They respond with, NO refund NO replacement, basically you’re SOL! So, I’ve spent hours of my time and not even to mention aggravation dealing with them over this. I had to file a dispute with my CC company. To add insult to injury I get a WARNING email from Amazon due to “too many” packages reported missing. They are threatening to close my account. Wow!!! They think they are so big and successful that they can now treat their customers like dirt. I’m deleting their app, deleting my handmade seller’s account, F them, horrible company!!!!",10.0,323,0.9996524014238617,0.00034759857613830825,33.64048705163361,Low Trust
