Steve Houston,US,1.0,"Today I tried ordering about $32.50 in small lightweight merchandise from Amazon.com; before the check-out i opted for the Prime Membership 1-week trial for $1.99.  However, when I attempted to complete my order, Amazon had the unmitigated gall to try to ADD another approximately $34.00 to this order; instead of the free shipping which I would expect from paying for the 1-week Prime membership.  Of course I immediately cancelled this order; and further, also immediately canceled the Prime 1-week trial membership.  THEN I checked my bank account to find out the AMAZON had gone into my account and taken about $2.12 for the BOGUS Prime trial they just attempted to SCAM me out of with OUTRAGEOUS shipping charges which under any other circumstance with any other business would have been possibly about $10 maximum.  When I had to waste my time calling Amazon Customer Service, first the phony computer voice put me through HELL... insulting my intelligence and taking several frustrating minutes of my time before finally transferring me to an agent--who additionally attempted to waste even more of time running me around in circles ALL in order for Amazon to credit my account for the $2.12 cents they SCAMMED me out of by adding on about $34 in BOGUS shipping charges which was in complete and stark contrast to what one expect from Prime's FREE shipping pledge.  BEWARE OF THIS AMAZON BAIT & SWITCH SCHEME!!!!!!!!",2.0,236,0.9996267178162352,0.00037328218376475597,32.66588788933406,Low Trust
chris,GB,1.0,"Another Amazon Prime classic delivery gaff! They used to be really good with deliveries but have steadily gone down hill and are actually worse now I'm paying for Prime! Two deliveries due today, one turns up without issue and the other is marked as attempted delivery but ran into an issue! Two orders 30 minutes apart and one gets to me and one doesn't. This is starting to become a habit with Amazon! Will I get a refund on my Prime, definitely not and never get anything back from them when there's a blunder. I can feel Prime getting cancelled now!!!!",13.0,101,0.9996196374756465,0.0003803625243534725,31.15194016772076,Low Trust
Iri N,GB,1.0,"If there was an option I would have rated their customer service ZERO! With the following, I want to warn all the Amazon Customers: PLEASE DO NOT PURCHASE GIFT CARDS! I did receive a gift card, it was sealed, when I tried to claim it, there was an error, therefore I could not claim the value/money on the card. I have tried everything and contacted 3 different Amazon's customer service in different Regions. They said they were unable to sort this issue.No explanation, no refund, although I did provide them with all the details required and despite the fact that I have been a loyal customer since 2009.  I finally tried to review the product on their Reviews page and, I was not allowed because I did not earn the privilege?!?! Scum! PLEASE REFRAIN FROM PURCHASING GIFT CARDS FROM THIS THIEVES!!!",11.0,141,0.9996195018163425,0.000380498183657485,31.600628947320843,Low Trust
Vitalie,GB,1.0,"Samsung S20 Plus 5GORDER # 204-2172993-2603509The seller PixelDirect is a LIAR and clearly breaking the law by misrepresenting!If you don’t want to waste your precious time – AVOID !!!On the 9th of June 2022, I bought a renewed smartphone - Samsung S20 Plus 5G, on amazon.co.uk which was sold by PixelDirect.Important to mention that this is a used phone, as you could easily notice the dirt which accumulates with time into the small holes of the phone.Under the section ‘’What’s in the box?’’, was listed a list of accessories which were missing when I received the product (the delivery was late as well).I contact the seller, he replied to me that renewed products are not coming with accessories.I sent him the screenshots when I placed the order and where it clearly said what was supposed to be in the box and that ‘’All Amazon renewed purchases will come with accessories that may not be original but will be compatible and fully functional’’ and asked him to explain that.His answer was that this applies to new items, and that renewed items are not supplied with the accessories. Also, he asked me to return the product for a refund. Their address is Pixel Direct (Amazon Return), 353 Hoe St, London, E17 9AP.That is a clear misrepresentation which is against the law!He wants me to send the product back, but what about the inconvenience and all my time wasted for moving the information and all the apps from the old phone to the new one and that I have to repeat the entire process again to be able to send the phone back?Who’s compensating for all the distress?!At this point, I called Amazon Customer Service. The assistant had a look at it and confirmed that the product must have the accessories listed on the web page.Her answer was that as the product was sold by a 3rd party seller, there is nothing she can do.The BIG question is Why then do you allow such sellers to be on your platform? Are you not responsible for the misrepresentation on your platform?I asked the assistant to connect me to her line manager/supervisor and she said that she cannot connect me with one, but that they will contact me in 48 hours. That didn’t happen.Shame on you amazon.co.uk, your customer service is becoming worse and worse. Such experiences are showing you the real face of the AMAZON.That proves that your platform is the perfect place for dodgy sellers and scammers!AVOID !",4.0,415,0.9996180352285952,0.0003819647714048413,34.674173953657174,Low Trust
William,US,1.0,"I have had an Amazon account for many years. I had my ID and password saved so I can just click my account one time and log on. However, Amazon made an 'update' to their log in protocol and now I have not been able to log in to my account with my known password for over a month. I have books that i've written and published on Amazon KDP that I can not access now because Amazon login procedures no longer work. I have contacted the Amazon support phone number 5 times now, they tell me the same thing, call back again and talk to another agent!When the log in page tells me that my password is not correct, I try again and again, then I try to 'reset my password'....but I can not do that because it shows an old phone number that it will send a code to so I can reset my PW. But that number is not used now, I have a new phone, new phone number. I can not log in to change the phone number!Amazon 'support' will not help me.....they asked me security questions which I answered correctly...then they asked what items that i've purchased in the past from Amazon. I tell them two because it's been so long, that I can not remember a third item. Then the 'agent'(who can barely speak English) tells me that time is up. I tell her that I now remember the third item, she is rude and tells me that i'll have to call back on monday and talk to another agent!I have had this problem for about a month now, I can not log in to my Amazon account, I can not log into my Amazon KDP account where my published books are. I can not get any help from Amazon 'support' at all!. Amazon Corporate WILL be getting a nasty letter or e-mail from me on this one!This is no way to treat an almost 15 year account holder!!!",7.0,335,0.9996178467558883,0.000382153244111727,33.77681938402275,Low Trust
Ste Cm,GB,1.0,"2 weeks of delivery hell!!I have had several orders that have gone missing or got damaged. Over the last 2 weeks we have noticed a pattern developing. If the package is sent by a third party (DPD, YODEL, XPD, MY HERMES EVEN ROYAL MAIL!!!) it arrives on time/early. If its being delivered by amazon logistics, it gets lost being passed between depots claiming its at the wrong depot!I have had every excuse from my address is wrong to its been deactivated (customer service won't explain that one to me) I get reassured every day the parcel is coming and they've fixed the issue but 2 weeks on and it's the same thingCustomer service is horrible, rude and incompetent, based nowhere near the UK and therefore have no idea what they are talking about. They tried saying the driver was parked outside my property when he said we weren't in and then later confirmed he was over 20minutes away by car!! Definitely not parking distance for delivery.They are not signed up to an ombudsman service but yet deflect complaints to the ombudsman service to which they have no obligation to act upon their decision. When you raise a complaint its filed as an internal matter as such you never get a resolution and the ntry and fob off their failure to deliver with a token monetary compensation of a 10 pound voucher..... Which if you use you have to complain about because the item doesn't arrive and as such the vicious cycle continues.Amazon themselves can not deliver. It would be quicker ordering off wish/joom",4.0,263,0.9996167468853707,0.00038325311462927836,32.96924678360583,Low Trust
Steve Lemon,SE,1.0,"Recently bought a Kindle Fire HD from amazon.com as I was unable to order one from amazon.co.uk (for some reason, unless you live in the UK, amazon.co.uk don't want your business or your money when it comes to the Kindle, despite the fact that I live in another EU member state!).  The gadget was sent to me quickly from the USA and almost as soon as I received it,  I started to try to download apps to customize it to my specification.  However, I have now found out that because I do not live in the USA or have an American credit card, I am not even able to download some supposedly free apps!  Huh?  Surely the World Wide Web does what it says and is not supposed to be geographically  restricted by amazon - or anyone else for that matter!  Why was I not made aware of these restrictions before I bought and paid for my Kindle?  Turns out that I have paid a large amount of money (I had to pay extra tax because I ordered the Kindle from the USA!) for what is nothing more than a glorified e-reader.  What a waste of money!  I would have been much better off just buying books and using my PC for everything else....! Beware if you are considering buying a Kindle from Amazon as you may not be able to use it for anywhere near the amount of things you thought you would! It's a shame, too, as it's a great little gadget, but only if you can utilise it's full potential!",33.0,263,0.9996157216982732,0.00038427830172682587,32.96929804296071,Low Trust
