chygill,GB,3.0,"Amazon is a very good service, however I can find nowhere to report a discrepancy between the comment the delivery driver made and the actuality! The comment read “handed to resident”. Not so, we were in and listening for the delivery - having tracked it. But no ringing of the bell or knocking of the door, just dumped.I’ve tried to find a place on their web site to report this - it’s not the first time - to no avail!! Sad really as parcels they send by Royal Mail or other service always come with a ring or knock!! Making this a reliably, safe delivery. That’s really is my only complaint about an otherwise very good company!",51.0,117,0.9995404184949995,0.00045958150500047257,91.33537391540705,High Trust
Robert USA,US,1.0,"Third party sellers on AMAZON.com do not have to disclose their true, actual identities. They come up with a pseudy-name, a fake name. A third party seller only needs a pseudy-name, a working email address and a bank account. That's it! AMAZON has no idea who these people are in reality. Nor do they care either! Its a scam! And there are millions of them on-line, doing business under the AMAZON domain name. Its an unfair market  advantage since American businesses need to incorporate (usually this is a good idea for legal reasons), pay taxes and fees, file tax returns, file for business licenses, etc. AMAZON and the millions of third party sellers who transact business under the AMAZON domain are scamming the US economy and the American consumer! If these AMAZON third party sellers get into trouble with AMAZON, they only have to change their fake business name and get a new email address! AMAZON knows this too! It is a cycle of perpetual chaos and insanity!  The largest population of third party AMAZON sellers are in CHINA and AMAZON protects these sellers at the expense of the American consumer - crazy! :(",10.0,194,0.9995380124295633,0.0004619875704366949,32.199207062201026,Low Trust
Dave Galloway,GB,1.0,"Just had the WORST ever customer service experience in all the years I have been a loyal Amazon customer!After being passed around customer service associates four times on chat and then speaking to an incompetent manager, I am still at the point I started at.I purchased an item from Amazon on the Prime day. The item ended up faulty, not fit for purpose and was immediately returned.The item was sent back on the 20th July 2022.Item received and signed for by an amazon associate on the 21st July 2022.On the Amazon APP it was still showing as ""item will be refunded when we receive the item."" Bearing in mind, I have the UPS tracking number which states delivery date 21st July 2022 and the person that signed for it.Used chat and spoke to someone and they said that they would sort the problem, not to worry.22nd July 2022, still showing ""we will refund when item received."" Even though the associate assured me it just needed to be scanned in and the refund would be  intimated.27th, six days after they received the item, it is still showing as ""we will refund when we receive the item.""The last associate I spoke to today, said he can not do anything, it will be 14 days! 14 days to start the refund? That's 14 days, plus the 5-7 days for the refund to be paid. That could be up to 21 days.The associate then said ""is there anything else I cam help you with?"" Just as I was copying and pasting a chat section from the first associate, he cut me off! How UNPROFESSIONAL!!!!!Disgusted in Amazon's customer service over the last seven days.I'm about to email the CEO and contact my credit card company.Supposed to be relaxing and recovering from an illness and now I'm worse than I was before I purchased the item from amazon.",14.0,312,0.9995362017500757,0.0004637982499242632,33.52290948624832,Low Trust
Derek Al,GB,1.0,"It's just problem after problem after problem with Amazon lately. Some of my deliveries just vanish and are untraceable, terrible customer service, same responses time and time again like you're talking to a robot or a broken record. The delivery drivers never buzz the correct number, when they say sorry the item is late it basically means its vanished and they have no idea where it is, then tell you that you have to wait for roughly another 5 days before you can ask for a refund. There is a reason why people pay for prime and want there deliveries sent the next working day, because they need them for upcoming events or plans etc, but they don't care about you,who they hire or how much they pay there staff. All they care about is taking your money!!! Terrible service, probably one of the worst I know!!!!!",3.0,147,0.9995333001901427,0.0004666998098572517,31.672241328126066,Low Trust
Laura,GB,1.0,Will be cancelling my prime after your recent music app changes. I want to listen to what I choose not what you decide to choose for me!!!! Shuffle is sh?te!!!,22.0,30,0.9995330611372581,0.00046693886274185026,30.35985844061326,Low Trust
