Kate,US,1.0,"WHATEVER you do, DON'T accept an invitation to upgrade your personal Amazon account to business!  It's a scam so that you lose your video library and can never use it again!!!  No entertainment and they don't tell you when they make the offer!  I have spent 3 days on customer service calls and the answer is ""You can't fall back, you can't have your library, you are screwed.""  BEWARE!  Great for personal accounts, don't EVER think of becoming business attached.",3.0,80,0.9976944577290177,0.0023055422709823414,31.012641106818883,Low Trust
Monica Santillana,US,1.0,"I’m given 1 star because I can’t give it 0. It’s unbelievable Amazon at this point doesn’t have any representative available for questions or concerns regarding the orders.  I know we are living difficult times but a company as Amazon should be more careful about its customers. I don’t know how can I get help to fix the issues. I tried calling and the chat but I didn’t get help. I decided to tell my story because my experience could help to somebody else. If you are going to buy something in Amazon, think about it twice or three times before you do it. On last Sunday I made a purchase of 2 items; unfortunately 20 min later, my husband came home with no good news and I realized I shouldn’t expend the money in those purchases, then I tried to cancel the orders. It’s funny how fast according with the sellers, those orders were already shipped (really?... On Sunday? And why? If they weren’t an essential items) and the money was instantly taken from my bank account. The only option I saw was to return the item (Non sense! I’m supposed to have the option to cancel the purchase!), any way I filled it out the form and I explained in a message everything about my situation (keep in mind! 30 minutes after I made the order). I received a confirmation from one of the sellers saying my return was approved, obvious I thought my refund will be ready in the next week and they won’t send the item. For my surprise today I received the item and now I have to print out the slip for the return. At this point I’m out of ink on my printer and libraries are closed, so I have no idea what I’m gonna do and no! No money to buy the ink. Oh! other surprise... on my account now I have a pending charge of $9 for restocking. For the other item I haven’t received any response, the seller is supposed to answer today and if they don’t do it, I have to fill another form. Obvious I had to do the same return process, filling out the form instead of cancel the order (cause they don’t give that option) and I sent 2 messages explaining about my situation, but so far my money is not in my bank account and I need it. It’s frustrating! Where’s the Amazon’s Customer’s Service? Why there is no representatives trying to help customers? Unbelievable!",1.0,420,0.997686538776237,0.0023134612237629693,34.82683402585444,Low Trust
Brian,US,3.0,"Two months ago I would have given them 5 stars. I have been an Amazon Prime member for a couple of years now. I have always loved this company and web site.., and then came covid-19!!! I am not complaining about the slower (much slower) shipping... we all have to adjust to aid each other. What I am talking about is their product line & what they have aided Chinese companies in doing. For instance: I wanted to find “hand sanitizer.”  If you go to the other well-known ‘brick and mortar’ sites you will find it marked, “Out of stock” and there will be no “cheap” substitutes. Amazon owes it to their customers to maintain some quality control. Instead they are stocking many, very many substitutes that did not exist before. Also, they have allowed the price on “junk” to go through the roof. Read the review, the comments on these outrageously priced & newly appearing Chinese made hand sanitizers. It is absolutely nothing but a rip-off. Amazon should start listing items as “sold out” & stop aiding these companies with no quality control in flooding our markets with overpriced garbage. It is Amazon’s good name that will suffer. We expect Amazon to do at least a little policing of the products they sell, and prices that have quadrupled in a month’s time. I hope the Amazon name will mean as much “post” covid-19 as it did “pre” covid-19!!!",3.0,239,0.9976491563487593,0.0023508436512407194,92.79841711245547,High Trust
Jeren Connell,US,1.0,"Tried to order tires from Amazon as none of my local retailers had the size I needed and I had a bad tire that needed replacing on my vehicle. Wait a week for the tires to arrive, they finally get here and I was sent  not only the wrong type of tire but the completely wrong size! I ordered a 17"" tire and was sent 16""! I call Amazon to address the issues and their excuse was they were out of the tire I ordered. So maybe try calling your customer and making them aware of that instead of charging them $400 for a completely wrong tire that I can't even use! Now I am still stuck without a vehicle, short $400, and waiting for a driver to be ""in my area"" again to pick up the tires before I can even begin to get my money back! Talk about horrible customer service! Oh and the tires I ordered retail for almost $100 a tire, the tires I was sent retail for half of that yet I was still charged the full $400!",1.0,183,0.9976363121498193,0.002363687850180707,32.17090452711363,Low Trust
Frankie Pedelty,GB,1.0,"First of all they hire anybody with no interview as long as you have a right to work document & If you value your mental health stay away. i ended up on anti-depressants and propanol for anxiety and did CBT because of amazon they dont care at all, my mum was extremely ill and i was given a disciplinary, due to taking dependancy leave to care for her, which is a joke! thats what it for! i have endometriosis which is painful and i have to go to toilet more frequently and i was told i couldnt spend more then 8 minutes in the toilet! its a joke! and even better it was a man who told me i couldnt go to change my sanitary product. against humans rights am i right? & also sexist, which amazon promoted him to manager a month later. so it was swept under the carpet. even my CBT woman who works alongside amazon said how bad they are treating me, i had numerous sicknotes from my doctor due to my mental health being so bad & amazon didnt care! they offered no support and made me worse and worse, just kept being brought into meeting being told i need to do better & basically get on with it when mental health is a serious issue and wonder why people commit suicide, which i also attempted while working there because they wouldnt listen to me and they treat you like a number not a human being. you are easily replaceable, the staff turn over is ridiculous. Please Please AVOID!!",1.0,264,0.9976334721661889,0.002366527833811083,33.0796275694808,Low Trust
