Betty Davis,US,5.0,"This person,  that created AMAZON, is just a brilliant person that is making our life so much better. Thank you Mr. Bezos, especially for choosing all the best employees, (You and Apple are the greatest). I returned  an item today, because it was to heavy for me, nothing wrong with the item, and I went to your drop  off  facility, (first time,) in DC. I was so amazed by the cleanest place ever,  I was even able to use the Ladies room,  that was  spotless,  everything was available to the public, in order to seal and wrap the package BRILLIANT, if I was tired, I could rest on a nice clean grey couch, and drink my coffee. Thank you soo much. AMAZON.  I hope we all will respect those places, as they trust us !!! And we trust Amazon. After a few hours I received credit for the returned Item. Can it get better then that??? love it!!!",2.0,158,0.997120661846639,0.002879338153361055,151.91626079437583,High Trust
Terry,US,1.0,"Crap, crap, crapI contacted Amazon Customer Service to ask about a package I ordered myself for Father's Day.  It has not arrived even though it says it was delivered.  The morons on the chat told me at first to contact them on June 24th to ask about the package.  I cannot travel back in time to contact them.  I actually had to remind this Genius that today is June 30th.  After I had this little interaction, it took this moron 15 minutes to look up the info on my package when he said it would take two.  Then this genius told me to contact them tomorrow (July 1st) because their 'system' could not help me.  WOW!!!!!!   DO NOT use amazon for ANYTHING.  Consider yourself warned.   Oh, and I spent an hour on the chat to get NO customer service",1.0,139,0.9970794068859624,0.002920593114037584,31.705199594008104,Low Trust
Leo P,GB,1.0,"The worse Amazon customer service that ever had seeing, I'm still waiting item collection, It's a shame  and completely frustrating, is the same to talk with an operative than supervisors or a manager no different at all, nobody solve your problem, absolutely incompetents.First, they sent a scheduled for 1 of March, as it was expected nobody arrived, after 40 minutes waiting over the phone plus 4 Amazon persons they sent a gap of 12 hours for a business collection 12:00am to 11:59pm, is a real joke, who will pay for your wasting of time?,  I'm sure that the seller don't know about the situation.AMAZON CUSTOMER SERVICE ............LESS 5 STARS!!!!!!",1.0,109,0.9970389229419729,0.0029610770580270618,31.370712293731412,Low Trust
DLP3,GB,1.0,"If I could give minus stars that would suit better. I have amazon prime and expect it delivered the next day but amazon delivery drivers for my area refuse to deliver to a new build estate as he says he doesn’t have appropriate insurance to drive on a new build estate. Amazon need to employ drivers that CAN do their job!!!!! A lot of people on new build estates will be ordering new things for their new house, it’s ludicrous Amazon would employ driver drivers unable to fulfill this! Amazon have said they can’t change the delivery company...prime canceled and back to eBay and else where for me.",18.0,108,0.9969778084863824,0.0030221915136176003,31.36255096659507,Low Trust
Jeremy Hetrick,US,2.0,"Ive Used Amazon Several Times, Every Order Ive Ever Placed There Were Issues. I Do Give Them Credit For Refunding Me After Delivering One Item To Wrong Address. Several Orders Never Received, One Order Weeks Late, ALL ORDERED PRIME! What Does That Tell You, There Business Model Is A Complete Lie! Don't Write Checks Your Ass Can't Cash Amazon! The Business Has So Much Potential too, What A Shame!EDITED: So the moral of the story here is simple. Don't Lie! I just don't like being lied to! You can have the best product in the world, though if you lie about it's or the businesses potential, delivery time, expectations, it's a game buster!I also want to stress that Amazon customer service has always been a pleasure to deal with. They have also always made good on any inconveniences. Just the BS that totally kills the experience, Ill stick to local businesses, even if it does mean paying more.",1.0,158,0.996961316509617,0.003038683490383054,61.92422806122695,Medium Trust
Tee,US,1.0,"I've been an Amazon Prime member for years now. A few months ago they placed a note when I went to place a review that there had been ""unusual reviewing activity, all my reviews have been removed and I will not be able to place reviews anymore."" I called to get this issue taken care of, they sent me a link to their review guidelines. I read them and didn't violate One rule! I use reviews to let other know about a product and also to ask questions. Asking questions, I'm no longer allowed to do either. So I called Amazon back again a couple of months later. I thought this time the issue was taken care of, NO it isn't!! So I emailed them. No response from Amazon at all!! Amazon Prime will be $139 when my membership is due again. If I can't have use of ALL the perks, including placing reviews & asking questions, then either Amazon can lower the cost of my membership or I will drop it! I heavily rely on being able to ask questions in making purchases so I don't buy & have to return. Because Amazon doesn't seem to care at all about fixing my issue, I can only give the one star",8.0,211,0.9969232787096406,0.0030767212903594077,32.52063359676699,Low Trust
