Sania Rahman,CA,1.0,"My first experience with #Amazon is horrible! I dont know with this level of service how they became such a popular site!!!I received an email gift card from my office as my farewell gift on October 8th, 2020. After that, I opened an account on amazon.ca as I am living in Canada. Then I checked my amazon gift card on an email that I received, there I have seen a gift card redeem option on my email so I redeemed my points and it said it is added to my account. Then I ordered a few items from my account using my gift card balance. Amazon also confirmed that order by email. After a few hours, I received another email saying something suspicious happening in my account so they froze my account. The email says to activate my account i have to reply their email with details of my gift card. So I have replied the email using the order number of my gift card and a screenshot of that email. Though I replied to the email still i was receiving the same email multiple times and I replied two times to those emails with all details, nobody returned to me with any solution! Then i called amazon customer service. They took all notes and told me they wanted to make sure this is me, they have taken my address details and phone number and told me I will hear from them within 3/4 days. I was waiting for thier email or phone call, nobody contacted me and my account remained on hold. Then after waiting gor 4 days I called again to thier customer care and repeated the whole complaint process that took around 40/50 minutes. This time again the customer care gave me hope that they are going to solve it. The customer care agent told me the problem my account is on amazon.ca but for redeemed points and purchase they used amazon.com id as i was doing it directly from my email gift card. Then i asked how is that possible, as i never opened account on amazon.com. His reply was the system doesnt require a new account, it just used the same information i used for amazon.ca, as my gift card was from amazon.com. Since then it's been more than 5 days I am still waiting for thier reply and my account is also on hold. I cannot use my account anymire. I dont know whether i will be able to get back my gift card money which is 225US$. I just want to use my gift card, hopefully i will never go for amazon shopping in future and will not suggest anyone.I have no idea what kind of service it is!?Sania RahmanCanada",2.0,457,0.9876530676281139,0.01234693237188611,35.743538430147865,Low Trust
John,GB,1.0,"How come Amazon US is so incompetent? In comparison to Amazon UK, they take weeks to ship (if they can be bothered) then when you contact customer service they don’t give a crap either! Lazy company! Unreliable! You would think for tax dodgers they would be able to get something right, but no!",76.0,53,0.9876301535833871,0.012369846416612873,31.212995966371864,Low Trust
Alex Smith,GB,1.0,"Amazon is a SCAM! Avoid at all cost! If there is an issue with your order, there will be ZERO support apart from excuses! Placed an order on 3rd March, today is 6th April, item still not been despatched! Tried to cancel the order, not possible! Tried to contact customer service, they advised that they can not cancel the order either, spoke over chat and phone, no one could help or at least explain what is going on and what is the reason for order still not been despatched or the reason why they can not cancel it... Unbelievable! Will be reporting to Trading standards and contacting my bank to get my money back... Now it makes sense why Amazon not accepting Paypal...  Use EBAY, so simple and no issues with refunds if there are any problems....",6.0,137,0.987579050604929,0.01242094939507099,32.157783308228026,Low Trust
