DJ Savage,US,1.0,"Amazon is a crooked company.  Once upon a time, it was amazing for people in rural areas like me.  We used to get things quick, and usually in the 2 day shipping time.  However, that number has grown from 2 days to at least 10 days, and now cost more to have the Prime membership.  I needed something quick, and realized how slow they were now, and received something from Walmart in 2 days, and do not even have an account with them.  Amazon is too big now, and needs to realize that they have hurt the rural areas, even though they do not care.  I finally cancelled my Prime account, and realized that I did not benefit from it.  I still have money in my account for returns, and they will not refund it.  They tell me that I can use it towards another order from them, but refuse to use them for business.  They steal money, and will not return it!!!  No wonder Jeff Bezos is rich.... he is a thief!!!",1.0,173,0.9856216810377734,0.014378318962226633,32.65946558355721,Low Trust
BUI,GB,1.0,"ZERO stars! for the worst customer service ever experienced.  After making an initial complaint re the damaged item, I was forced to hold several times and and passed through a stream of incompetent individuals, who asked me to repeat my complaint - it was akin to torture! Essentially, every single one of them did nothing to help and two of them thought it fine to talk over me and then abruptly cut the call. In addition, I received contradictory advice, hence asked to speak to a manager, talked to someone who claimed to be, asked re his name - he stated it would be in the email - subsequent email had no relation to the actual complaint, that we discussed at length, and he omitted his name! Talked to 16 Amazon staff in total! Then I wrote to them, sent images through, message came back - we cannnot accept images... Conclusion: Amazon is beyond unprofessional with incompetent staff, who appear to revel in wasting their customers time! Their badly packaged goods policy is incomprehensible. Hence, I intend closing my account, based on Amazon's complete lack of respect for a legitimate customer complaint.",6.0,192,0.98549882521424,0.014501174785759963,32.878732323135445,Low Trust
Brent,US,1.0,"I made a purchase last Monday on Amazon for a glass-top desk and a leather desk chair. I canceled the purchase no more than 20-30 seconds due to them being the wrong items. I intended to go forward with the same purchase but different items but the policy states 3 -5 business days before the money is returned to my debit card. On the 3rd day I contacted Amazon asking where the refund is because the items I canceled weren't even in my list of purchases. Amazon kept asking me for the order number and they weren't listed to get the item number! So they asked for the card number I used to make the purchase. Some magical reason, neither Amazon nor Chime bank can tell me where or how or what about that purchase. It's non-existent to them. But clear on my bank statement. It's been a week and still no sign of my refund. I've called Amazon countless times. Chime too. Today Chime had to start a claim to investigate where the money is and to give it back. How sad is it that they large corporate businesses can't handle their own customers money. They don't really care either because it's not them at loss!! Now I have to wait who knows WEEKS to get my damn money back from these 2 idiotic and ridiculous companies and I needed those items to start school tomorrow!! Never again Amazon, and Chime can definitely kiss my ass!",18.0,247,0.985319143750017,0.014680856249983054,33.50465414171956,Low Trust
Shalanie Rodriguez,US,1.0,"I bought multiple items from amazon and 4 items stated that delivered, they even took picture on where was left but it wasn’t there. I called the customer service about it. They refused to refund me 3 itmes which is more expensive and only refund me with 1 that only cost $8.99.Please be aware buying from amazon from now on! Because they said that there’s a specific items lost they can’t able to refund or replacement. They said that certain items have the policy of risk of lost and won’t be able to refund or replace them. So everyone who’s buying from amazon be careful because you gonna lost your items plus your money! All they can say is Unfortunately! And hang up on you because they don’t wanna deal with your frustrations! No matter how many times you keep calling them back. If amazon was great before well now, not anymore because they only care about your money and not the customers. It’s not customer’s fault for lost items but the customers are the one suffering and amazon customer services or amazon itself doesn’t care! Amazon can’t be trusted anymore!",1.0,191,0.98529575875532,0.01470424124467995,32.87766859616557,Low Trust
ANDREW DAVID MERRICKS,GB,1.0,"Purchased some Parker Pens from a Amazon Market place seller trading as Abbeyshake who are ownded by Galaxy Wholesalers spending 2 lots of £1,199.90 and £839.73 . unbeknown to me they didn't have the pens advertised so instead sent me two crappy calenders instead supposedly to  keep their Amazon rating ! They even had Amazon in on the fraud as they collected the items as part of prime delivery . Both address labels had the correct weight of the original order yet the calenders weighed far less and the picture on delivery did not match my order . As anyone knows Amazon Customer Services are very difficult to connect with and communicate with but through constant messaging I have got most of my money back ! Despite being Fraudsters this is of no concern of Amazon who were quite happy to go along with this ! Abbeyshake Customer Service is a Abysmal run by one Obnoxious pathetic excuse of a human being called Alex who cannot even add up even when he takes his socks off ! The callenders are so rubbish that I couldn't even wipe my behind with them ! BEWARE OF BOTH BUSINESSES !",13.0,197,0.9851920442332529,0.014807955766747094,32.95015662176416,Low Trust
Mr Richard Castle,GB,1.0,"So many problems with Amazon these days. Delivery company used is awful, numerous not in stock cancellations but only after payment has been taken from your account and then wait ten days to get the money back.. How nice of them!Yesterday, my wife who does not have access to my account switched her machine on and all of my searches appeared for her to browse through!!! Imagine the scene if something naughty had been there....Then, I could not sign in to amazon on any of the win10 machines. I was told to get the number from ***555 message and then enter it. Why?Follow that with Amazon demanding a new password and then another number obtained from ***555 which could not be found for some reason and that as they say, was that. Enough!Literally dozens of problems in the last 2 months and as usual nothing but a machine to answer you.How I pity the poor people who have to work for this company.I have one outstanding order that may actually be delivered and then bye-bye Amazon.Finally, if you suffer from amazon's disease, just go elsewhere. It is the only way to make them realise that they have got it wrong.",25.0,200,0.9851434599834218,0.014856540016578212,32.986236984003334,Low Trust
