Sherri Root,US,1.0,"If I could give you a stars I would. I am not sure how Amazon delivery services cannot read an address. I'm going to assume that they use GPS location when they're delivering products. So how do items get delivered to a completely wrong address not even the correct street. I have no idea where my items went. But I have a picture and according to Amazon I can ""check to see if someone else has it""... Well I shouldn't have to. That's why I pay for Amazon prime! Worst part is, the items today are things I really needed this evening!! Ugh!!",3.0,103,0.9846937950462187,0.015306204953781322,31.920666389023893,Low Trust
Magdalena,GB,1.0,"I would really like to give 0 stars! Can Trust Pilot consider adding this option? Absolutely terrible company. Customer service doesn’t exist. I contacted them to get a refund for the order that hasn’t arrived and probably was lost. When I want to cancel it now or get refund Amazon won’t allow me to do that! It keeps transferring me to the same pages, no contact with customer service or the seller! Absolute nightmare! As soon as this is resolved I’m removing my amazon account. They are a joke!",19.0,89,0.9846615683587326,0.015338431641267358,31.765239024575987,Low Trust
Mohammed Shahin,EG,1.0,"First of all the device is working well until now Except it's going too hot on Linux (Amazon technical representative told they will contact me for this issue but they didn't), I've used it for approx 1 month for software development (I'veen't tested gaming on it yet).The bad review because of how Gigabyte and Amazon dealt with me after I purchased the device with a promotion stated on the title (Free RAM) without warning that the promotion is only for US and Canada residents only.For me as an International shopper, I've been fooled by both Gigabyte and Amazon as Both refused to give me the promotion even it's their fault, not mine.Amazon always tells please contact the manufacturer.The manufacturer ""Gigabyte"" responds first time after two weeks to provide them with details which I've provided already alongside with my invoice, then after resubmitting the same information, they replied again after another two weeks that the promotion is for US and Canada resident only!!!!   Really???!!For Gigabyte and their worst support I've ever seen, I'm not going to purchase their products again of course.I'm not happy at all with my purchase, As I hate to be fooled this way by both the companies.But, unfortunately, I can't return the device because I need it for my work, and also because it's pain to return an international shipped item.The first time to deal with Amazon and the worst experience I've ever had with online shopping as they fooled me with the promotion and not follow up with my technical issues.",2.0,255,0.984585547107368,0.015414452892631991,33.63107037317899,Low Trust
Marte Paramo,US,1.0,Amazon are crooks. They closed my account that had a $50 dollar gift card on it. I've called several times without any feedback as to why it was closed. I've been promised that someone would contact me many times. Wht is it ok ro keep my money. Doesn't Amazon have enough money w/o stealing mine. Crooks!!!!!,1.0,56,0.9844974645600508,0.015502535439949172,31.403281567286296,Low Trust
Mary Jones,US,2.0,"Amazon has gotten so bad! Deliveries not on time if they come at all! I paid extra to have something delivered same day and of course it didn’t come. Customer service sucks and will not refund you even tho the package never arrived. They keep telling me my package is out for delivery when according to their app it’s NOT!! I am done with Amazon! The Prime is awful now, you basically have to pay for everything on it, it’s just not worth it anymore. ",2.0,85,0.9842305456733604,0.015769454326639565,61.74192195918111,Medium Trust
1muflon1,NL,1.0,"I tried to purchase a kindle version of a book which showed on amazon.com priced at $61.76. So I decided to buy it with one click, I wasn’t logged in so I logged in and immediately clicked on the buy with one click button as I was not expecting logging in will have any effect on the order.Afterwards, I received in my email invoice with a completely different price than the one shown before ($81.59). When I brought this to the attention of amazon customer service they told me that is just a normal change in price across the time.However, then I noticed when I log out price drops back to $61.76. Every single time I log into my account price becomes $81.59 and every single time I log out it drops back to $61.76. I tested this about 8-10 times and even recorded one such attempt in case they change it later so I can bring this issue to the attention of local authorities and lawmakers because if this is legal it definitely should not be in the future.I am appalled by this for two reasons:The practice itself is incredibly deceitful. In fact, since I did not notice the change in price right away and at amazon.com you buy kindle books with one click I purchased the book at an increased price and now wasted my time going through the return process. Furthermore, I wonder how many shoppers might never even notice this happening and literary get scammed by amazon - I doubt that any customer expects the price of purely digital good changing after they log-in, and hence many might not check.Customer service laying to customers. When I wrote an email about this to the amazon customer service their reply was that Amazon prices change with time and tax rates might be different in different states.However, the price changes every time I log in log out - hence clearly the price is not a function of time but a binary function of whether I am logged in or out of my account. Claiming that’s changing with time is incredibly intellectually dishonest as the fact that the price is still even of the time of this writing shown to be $61.74 shows that at least today the price was completely unrelated to time but depended solely on my logged in/out status.Furthermore, this cannot be explained by taxes because when I log into my account the pre-tax price is changed as well! In fact from the order summary from my accidental purchase, I can see that the pre-tax price I was charged was $67.99. That is higher than the post VAT price shown before I log in.This is really low! If amazon sets different prices based on the login of a customer they should at least be transparent about it and put a big warning sign under each price! Furthermore, they should at least transparently say that price depends on the customer and not time as is the case here!All future customers of amazon should be beware of this practice! You might get billed completely different price than the one they pretend to offer!",1.0,524,0.9841785602066383,0.015821439793361702,36.66880614558507,Low Trust
Pui Ching Ho,HK,1.0,"The page of Crystal Flash Sales stated that total 6 boxes surgical mask, each order contains 300 pcs at customer questions. Is that cheating? Besides, items weight of product information mentioned that it’s 5.19 pounds? All of the above wordings are cheating consumers!!!!Though I requested for refunding and returned the product for long time, no refund up till now, is it reliable for purchasing items in AMAZON?!",1.0,67,0.984135849487416,0.015864150512584052,31.544749869992632,Low Trust
Alan Jenner,GB,1.0,"Made an order beginning of March, delivery date 25th march. Email then stated ""we will contact you when the item is available for dispatch"" I thought this was odd but, ok.It is now 20th April, no further communication at all from amazon, I check my order status & apparently my order doesn't exist. Now i've got to chase them to see whats going on & make sure i get my money back.What a great way to treat yoir customers.Update 26th April,I finally managed to get hold of customer service, very nice lady that unfortunately hardly spoke any english... she didn't have a clue what was going on, just kept repeating whatever i said to her. COMPLETELY USELESS! I evemtually told her to close mY account.Today i received an email asking if i am interested in EXACTLY the same item at TWICE THE ORIGINAL PRICE!!!!WHAT AN ABSOLUTE RIPOFF,DO NOT USE AMAZON UNLESS YOU WANT TO BE SCAMMED.",4.0,156,0.9840711432364377,0.01592885676356226,32.54630262505416,Low Trust
Leti C,US,1.0,"Dear Amazon, do not promise delivery dates, if you cannot get a package at destination ON TIME!Maybe you were great ""ONCE UPON A TIME"", but not anymore.You raise the membership prices, but do not raise the bar for your poor customer service.Also, I had 2 incidents today:1: the promised delivery by date that never arrived2: a package I sent to my daughter in college. I asked her today if she received it, and I guess it wasn't delivered. Well guess what? YOU KEPT MY MONEY!!!! Really? Do you need to steal my $ 50.00? REALLY?Upsetting: Amazon used to be.. but not anymore... you are Amazing, but for the wrong reasons.. stealing from us..",8.0,113,0.9840003028562195,0.015999697143780467,32.067511497682574,Low Trust
p fisher,GB,1.0,"I informed these reprobates that I WOULD NOT BE IN as I was going to visit a sick relative, they told me they were going to send a OTP, I told them I could not receive it as I was travelling a long way on the underground, their reply was don’t worry we can text. I pointed out I can’t receive texts EITHER!!They said parcel was on its way so couldn’t stop it. I pointed out I WOULD NOT WANT IT as, I had PERMANENTLY CLOSED my account!The driver came whilst I was out and failed to even follow my settings info that said to deliver to a specific neighbour if I was out, since then my account has now been deleted",90.0,122,0.983961735529014,0.016038264470985997,32.1703933132857,Low Trust
Craig Wells,GB,2.0,"Well done Amazon....NOT!! Every other time of year you send me a parcel its the smallest item contained in a box I could fit in. Today, you manage to deliver two of my wife's Xmas presents, not in boxes, so now she knows what she's getting. Thanks!!! Clearly I'll keep ordering from you as you manage to deliver most things next day, hence the two stars, however, maybe a bit of thought at this time of year wouldn't go amiss.",2.0,80,0.983896750648398,0.01610324935160201,61.702526460849874,Medium Trust
