Ania Lightworker,US,1.0,"Sucks soooo bad now. I have never ever experienced such horrible customer service. They are obviously 3rd party from India. Go around the world not to refund me my own money it is absolutely so crazy to me! I have never ever gone through this and I have been a prime member forever. I mean I was on call for hours, getting hung up on, lied to…this is absolutely rediculous!!!",1.0,70,0.9781897090309375,0.021810290969062507,31.87570804256417,Low Trust
Lafaye Pierre,FR,1.0,"As many customers, seemingly, I've been charged for Amazon Prime ""avantages"" without any agreement of my part : 49€ improperly withdrawn from my bank account !! I managed to have them reimbursed in few cliks but the process is disgusting ! To much power leads to the worst behavior !! I used mine and deleted my account, for ever...",2.0,59,0.9781875065502156,0.02181249344978442,31.752430617525672,Low Trust
Andy Lambert,US,1.0,"I ordered a bottle of dandruff shampoo. Around $8.00. and paid with my Mastercard. It came in on time. However, 2 weeks later I received an email from Amazon saying ""your package is on its way"" huh? Could return it but it was made too complicated the way they wanted me to return it. A square postage paid label was issued and the instructions said to return it by putting the square label on a round bottle.They had sent me a second bottle. I put it away to keep and they just had to bill my card on file.They didn't do that. Instead I got an email from Amazon saying "" if you don't pay for the second bottle by (such a date) they would charge me a late fee of $94.00!!!!I didn't want that hanging over my head so I paid for the bottle I never ordered. Around $8.00. No big deal. I received an email from the bank they use to charge credit cards and they confirmed they received my check. I wrote them a check instead of them taking the funds from my credit card.I decided to cancel my credit card but Amazon wouldn't let me. A pop-up came up and said that Amazon requires a credit card so to cancel the card I had to cancel my account.I let it sit as I figured I might buy something later.A couple of weeks after that I received an Amazon credit store card. Only good with Amazon purchases. It was for $600.00! I never asked for this card and if and when I decide to buy something. I didn't know wich card they would bill.When you buy something on credit. You are asked at checkout which card you want them to use.I picked my Mastercard on file. At the same time I deleted the $600.00 card. I did this because Amazon has a reputation of double billing. (Read the reviews). So I immediately locked my Mastercard and had my bank issue a new card with a different number.This at least invalidated my Mastercard and would be denied if someone tried to use it for nefarious reasons.After a few months went by I decided to cancel Amazon completely. Wouldn't you know it had been so long that I had forgotten my password.So I used my email address and pushed the ""forgot my password"" button. That resulted in my receiving an OTP number.I typed in the OTP number and it took me to a site that had further requirements to make sure it was me. ""Okay"" I said and I've used 3 different phones over the years.I had to check off my current phone number and nothing happened.My second option was to click on myLG G6 phone. Click? Nothing. I hadn't had the LG 6 for years so that did nothing.My next thing they wanted me to click on my Samsung SE. I haven't had that phone in a long time. I had sold it.That didn't work.The only phone I have now is an iPhone.Wich wasn't listed. So I'm stuck. There's no number to call Amazon to talk to. Even if there was they would not give me my password back. If they even knew what it was.It was a vicious cycle I couldn't break.I tried all the passwords I could think of.Nothing.I was determined and finally I got a page that had the option to ""cancel your Amazon account"". I had found my old password.I scrolled down to ""cancel your account"" I clicked on the bar and it asked me why was I canceling my account. I just typed into the ""I no longer want an Amazon account""Another page popped up with the option to change my mind or ""confirm cancellation""I hit ""confirm cancellation"". Done!Another page pops up and asked for my username and password. I just closed out of the page.This morning, while checking my email I seen a ""you haven't finished closing your account"" message from Amazon.I clicked on it and it started the whole process again. I just deleted the email. It didn't really matter because I had changed the card anyway rendering the Mastercard invalid. I counted six Amazon emails. I blocked them out. So for those who are crying that Amazon closed your account. Count your blessings. They did you a favor. But they still keep your credit card. Don't forget to delete it in the app website if you want nothing more to do with Amazon. Too bad, I had a good relationship with them innitialy. Just wanted to say that you can't ask Amazon to close your account in anger because you feel stiffed by them as they will not close it. Some people here are saying ""close my account"". That means nothing to them. They've been known to charge over and over and renewal accounts will still be charged even know you tell them to stop. You have to do it on your Amazon website. Just follow the complex account closure instructions.I eventually locked my credit card immediately and ask for a new card with a different number. That will render your card invalid and any charges will be denied. Good Luck as they make you jump through hoops to cancel.UPDATE: 12/25/2021 have not been contacted by Amazon for over a year now.",8.0,882,0.9781636033719766,0.02183639662802339,40.98525785720039,Low Trust
Paul Webb,GB,1.0,"Become an awful company during this lockdown, unprofessional and complacent!Their policies have gone out the window for the customer, 4 disputes and 2 weeks to achieve a refund, on top of that I was lied to twice that my refund had been processed, which a Manager actually admitted to after a huge argument. Have cancelled my prime, and will not be renewing with this awful company anymore, the film site is rubbish, Netflix is the better option, Amazon music is a compete rip off, you pay £7.99 for Prime, then the thieving CEO of this company wants another £9.99 to get all the music, well guess what you get better music on Spotify for less money and as for shopping, everything is cheaper on Ebay and gets to you just as quick. Plus any problems you're refunded with no issues. There's definitely life without Amazon!!!!",5.0,145,0.9779360349872709,0.022063965012729114,32.72967048843791,Low Trust
Rick,US,1.0,"I ordered this printer 4 days ago with a 2 days delivery from Amazon at a good price (-21% + 50$ added discount). I am a loyal prime customer since 8 years, at least, with a lot of purchases.TBA307871694897As I was supposed to provide the 1-time pin code to the driver for delivery of this amazing printer, and the tracking was showing delivery between 2pm and 4pm initially,  I had organized my day to stay home.At 4pm , I was ""next stop"" on the map and the driver was 2 blocks away from my house. At 4.30pm, not seeing anybody, I checked again, the driver was still at the same place and the delivery moved to 7pm, while he was still 2 blocks away….At 5.30pm, I see now the driver is in Simi Valley, CA  at an Amazon center location, 30 miles away from my house. I phone the customer service, who literally just says what I can read on my screen…. So not useful at all.The day after I go to this center in Simi Valley, CA where they tell me to go complain in Chatsworth, CA as they cannot help locally. Well ….the driver obviously stopped here and had the printer loaded in the van there. So why cannot they help ? Being now in Chatsworth , we check, and printer is tagged as ""missing"" in the system. We phone together Amazon customer service over the phone, same thing again, not useful at all, we are even told it is not missing and it will be delivered this same day for sure.Now today saturday 07/29/23, same status as 3 days ago. The information are not even updated on the tracking. I phone the customer service where I am being told to wait until the 11th of august (in 15 days) to ask for a solution if I have not been delivered in the meantime. After saying I didn’t agree , I did ask to speak to a supervisor, who finally told me literally "" I cannot do anything else and I will hang up"", that he did while I was continuing speaking.I phoned again 2 hours ago , after having selected ""cancel this delivery"" , and spoke to another lady to whom I explained the whole story. This lady, this time, was courteous but told me she cannot tell me anything about this sad situation and will escalate the issue….and I cannot even order another 1 at the same price that I ordered !Now if I check the delivery status, informations have magically changed :  I can read that I refused the delivery because the order was canceled before. What ??!!? So now Amazon is changing the story line ?To summarize , basically my printer was loaded in the van, the driver stopped 2 blocks away for a while and for any reason it did last, then he decides not to deliver me and goes back to the Amazon center 30 miles away. The van stays overnight and suddenly the printer is missing, but in the end it is me refusing delivery because the order was canceled !?!?Something is definitely wrong but it is being cover-up obviously. Leaving aside the fact I was hang-up by an Amazon associate representing the management, and all other associates telling me what I could read !As it is not an isolated case, aside from huge money losses (and in this case how is it handled with Epson…),  it says a lot about the ""Customer experience"" or ""Customer centricity""  mindset being practiced at Amazon:- customer being held hostage if the ordered item has suddenly disappeared- customer being hung-up if not satisfied- customer unsatisfied left unsatisfied- customer is not a priority, Amazon decides to hang-up as they don’t have any solution, and decides that you have to wait the period of time they decide- customer is being handled by low cost countries personal , just repeating what they learned and not customizing their answer to your own concern. In the end the service is more expensive, being paid for…..nothing except providing informations you already have on your screenObviously, Amazon is not set to handle expensive orders/ items that can suddenly disappear, and for which you can be held hostage for a while. I know now that I will prioritize Amazon for cheap items but not for pricier ones where I will go in a store, or order straight from more serious companies (bestbuy….).It was not like this in the past, so Amazon has taken definitely a wrong turn, probably being the result of short-term cash only oriented decisions. But this is another story….",3.0,769,0.9777105370343404,0.02228946296565959,39.740384533588646,Low Trust
Chris Clayton,GB,1.0,"for the third time in a month and second in two days my package has been "" delivered and handed to resident"". NO IT HASN""T!The problem is that I live in a small village most of which has the same postcode so SATNAV sends you to the centre of the village (a different street!) so I have set up detailed instructions on how to find me telling the driver to ignore SATNAV but that is ignored even though the tracking map I can access shows the right location. I am physicallly (NOT mentally Amazon!) so cannot wander around the village looking for misdelivered packages. I also pay a premium for Prime membership purely so I can get next day delivery which clearly I can't! Customer complaints then treat me like an idiot when I complain!",12.0,135,0.9777072329845009,0.022292767015499093,32.62894008941769,Low Trust
simonhaleross,GB,1.0,"Stop using Yodel!Whilst clearly you have dispatched my items within the agreed time, Yodel cannot stick to it. Use DPD or UK Royal Mail, even Hermes would be an improvement!!!!",7.0,30,0.9776206980192845,0.02237930198071547,31.45547659651194,Low Trust
Trish Flamant,CA,1.0,I was issued a refund for an item that broke after a couple of weeks of using it. I switched banks and I updated my payment method but was still issued a refund to my old account!! I was advised by the rep AND supervisor I needed to go to the bank myself and get the money! It doesn’t work like that here. I am battling cancer. I don’t need to be going and standing in line to argue with a bank I don’t bank with anymore. HORRIBLE CLIENT SERVICE!!,1.0,90,0.9776020783100935,0.022397921689906508,32.129430576923816,Low Trust
j A,US,1.0,"Bought this queen mattress, requested return because squeaky springs. Return slip was created for UPS, UPS refused to take an open box mattress. Called Amazon they created a new a return, for Thursday Jan 5Th. from 12 noon - 6 pm, to Pilot carrier.After waisting a whole day of work waiting, called Pilot they said we do not pickup mattress adding that amazon knows that. Called Amazon at 5:45 pm, I was transferred from agent to another, requested to talk to a supervisor, they refused to talk to me saying that the supervisor told them I have to wait for thirty days before I can return that mattress?!!!! I waited about an hour ...I asked for names to write a complain, I could not hear the line is bad.Stay away from buying any thing from Amazon, it is a very bad services. now I am stuck with credit card bill of around $1200, because Amazon also lost trace of my previous Lucid 12 inched Mattress I returned because it was the wrong size.I wish I can write on google as well, but google don't treat big corps like small business, one cannot write review ...?!",1.0,195,0.9775935190984543,0.022406480901545733,33.30764877867235,Low Trust
