CGAS,GB,1.0,"I placed an order on 06,01. I got an email on 13/01 telling me about the delay for my order. which stated : *If the order won't arrive by the time you need it, you can cancel the order or an individual item from your order by visiting Your Account, and viewing the order details. As long as the item hasn't entered the dispatch process,you'll be able to cancel it.*However, this was not true and it actually was impossible to cancel the order, either on my account or by contacting the supplier ( as per automated message on my account) who said that only Amazon could cancel it and also said that my payment was still pending , which is also untrue.I am now told by their advisors that it is not possible for them to cancel the order until it has been dispatched!!!!! I think I am just being fobbed off with random  excuses/explanations. This is ridiculous, makes no sense whatsoever and istotally unacceptable.This email also says: *We're sorry about the delay in getting your order to you, but I'm pleased to tell you that we're preparing it for dispatch now.**Within the next business day you should receive an e-mail from us confirming that the following items have been dispatched:*This ,too, is untrue as apparently they are still trying to locate the item and it has not been dispatched yet. But I do not want it  sent to me, I want it cancelled, as I have been saying since 13/01, and  my money refunded but according to their advisors this cannot be done until it has been dispatched.And apparently there is no way of getting this complaint escalated to a non existent complaint department as I a told the customer service is  also the complaint department . Resolver is not an option either as Amazon UK has decided not to accept complaints raised via Resolver.Absolutely disgusting customer serviceNEVER AGAIN",4.0,320,0.9750107562515725,0.02498924374842748,34.838918160500455,Low Trust
One That Travels,US,1.0,"Oh Where to Begin WHERE to begin?? Amazon has barred me from writing reviews because they felt that I was reviewing in return for discounted products or for free products. However, the reviews that I was writng, were very legitimate for discounts or not! The discounts DID NOT require reviews! My reviews have gone completely away from amazon.com why? Because they said that I have the broken their policy too many times and that they are removing all of my reviews. That is just the beginning.   I have emailed and called Amazon at least six times in the last year to discuss what actually happened because according to their ""computers"", I am doing something illegal. Really??? Anyways, all of my phone calls and all of my emails have always gone unanswered! The last time I tried was two weeks ago. Now, getting onto the business side of Amazon Prime, what a rip off! Definitely not worth $179. Amazon, you'll never get my money for Prime. Good luck!",8.0,167,0.9749827313654499,0.025017268634550116,33.12411076767815,Low Trust
Meg,GB,1.0,Dreadful Give them zero stars if I could!! Placed an order that said same day delivery by 10pm. Then said it was delayed until the 2nd. Then on the second it said my parcel was lost and to request a refund... funnily enough the refund button didn't do anything. Then told by seriously rude and unhelpful customer service to wait another 6 days for a parcel that's most likely been stolen by courier or not sent in the first place!!! Checked the sellers website they've put the price up on the exact same item so obviously trying to get people to re order and pay more. Will never use Amazon again deleting my account.,19.0,114,0.97493533367796,0.025064666322039963,32.53197700651142,Low Trust
B B P,GB,1.0,"Amazon seem to have lost their direction.Every order placed so far has either been, poor quality, faulty in one shape or form, or totally incorrect in size, description or actual product listing.A once has been superb Amazon I think has seen their day!Yes they may get the item to you quickly, but, is it any good?Easy answer is NO!Along with the fact that the prices are so false. After checking of suppliers online, the prices are actually inflated compared to other online retailers, that also includes P & P!Shame on Amazon and I for one will not be shopping with them. I will prefer to wait an extra day or two or even dare I say it, go back to the high street! Well as much as I can, as we have killed the high street, in thinking that it is better and cheaper shopping online….Namely Amazon!",3.0,147,0.9746619641747533,0.02533803582524674,32.91580812889554,Low Trust
