Ieva,GB,1.0,"I have ordered a couple of items for someone for their birthday well in advance, it say it was going to be delivered on the 3 days before the birthday. Closer the date, it was running late, so I contacted Amazon to find out when it will be delivered. They couldn't give me a definite answer. Then I checked the status on the birthday, it was still running late. Checked the status next day - 'item may be lost'. I had to contact Amazon AGAIN, who kept on telling me it was running late. I explained that's not what I see, they said they were seeing the item's different status. So it's not consistent! Because of that they gave me £5 promotional credit (which is nice but didn't help with the person getting a birthday gift on time). Now, I'm trying to purchase something to redeem £5 (apparently it's applied automatically), and it's not applying automatically, they are stating that £5 should be deducted from the item I have in my cart. I know it should, but it's not!!! They told me to still purchase the item full price and then contact them AGAIN with the order number. I've been back and forth with them for so long already and they are asking me to do that again. Instead, they could have offered one off gift card code or something but no, they want to make it more difficult. Also, suggested for someone to call me to talk about it. I explained that I was working and I couldn't take a phone call, but they insisted they call me! How unhelpful. The first customer assistant was unable to sort it out so I was transferred via chat to a different assistant. The second assistant confirmed that items sold by Amazon EU or Amazon US cannot be used with a promotional credit. The first assistant was adamant that the code SHOULD work. The second assistant suggested to help me find the same product to be shipped by Amazon, but instead of helping to find the original brand they found an alternative made by Amazon. It seems like they don't care about their customers and just want to benefit themselves even if they give promotional credits as a 'gesture of goodwill'. It's all fake and nothing genuine about their customer care and service. Very disappointed.",2.0,393,0.9732221710606608,0.02677782893933922,35.747192063904706,Low Trust
