PITZBURG,US,1.0,"Amazon treats their Prime members no differently and paying for Prime membership does not give you faster delivery service. A guaranteed window of delivery is NO GUARANTEE AT ALL! Customer service reps don't care and when a customer ends a chat, the customer service rep should not be reaching out to the customer--HARASSMENT!!!",2.0,53,0.969009866311443,0.030990133688556964,32.14401032996907,Low Trust
Matt Andrews,US,1.0,"I can't begin to express my anger towards Amazon. I'm absolutely appalled by the rude, offensive, belittling comments and lack of assistance. I bought three furniture pieces for my apartment in upstate New York. One was QLED 8K television, which was bought on May 5th. I received the item in practically a hollow box. Upon inspection, surprisingly, there were no noticeable signs of damage, so I decided to plug it into my wall. The second I did, I smelled an awful odor coming from the back of the set which smelled like something died inside. The television would not power on or respond to button presses. I decided to speak to Amazon personally, which I couldn't get in touch with a human for over an hour. When I finally got a hold of someone they had me on hold for another 30 minutes. At first, he was polite, but as I explained what happened, he would cut in and not let me get any other words in. He shouted MA'M!...MA'M!...MA'M!..then gave me an annoyed tone of why the television wasn't under warranty. If that wasn't enough, he would paraphrase me and use words ""power cord"" ""tv remote"" and others in a shrill voice clearly making fun of me because I'm a female. I told him if he would hold on the line I can put my boyfriend on, which suddenly ended the call prematurely. This is so unprofessional! I've reached out to Amazon customer service at least 4 times last and this month, which had I never received a reply. I can't return the television, and it has been in the living room the entirety of this ordeal! I have tried everything but it seems I'm on my own. I don't want to start a lawsuit against Amazon but I might not have a choice.",1.0,305,0.9686701043273488,0.03132989567265121,34.98769500797356,Low Trust
