Craig R.,US,1.0,"5 months of failed deliveries. This is ridiculous and yesterday was the final straw. I reside in a secure apartment community that has 24/7 call box access. Even a 2-year-old could figure it out! Look up the name, then key in 3 digit code and press the call button. Resident answers and presses 9 to open door. All of that info is in the delivery instructions. I even put the 3 digit code so they don't have to look me up. So what happens? Every time they show up when the office is closed they just drive off. They never even attempt to use the call boxes, NEVER! I complain every time and all the useless support staff does is put on their fake sincerity claiming they understand how upset I am. No, that's impossible. I spend a lot of money on Amazon. Over $3,000 in 2019 alone. Enough to make the cost of Prime worth it, but WTH good is it if it takes 2 or 3 delivery attempts every single time? It's basically paying them to screw me over. Yesterday was it, the last freaking straw! On Saturday my electric shaver broke. Now I could have gone to the mall or Walmart, but no, I chose to buy on Amazon and it was an Amazon sold item so next day (Sunday) delivery was guaranteed (that was manure)! So, what happens? As always the crappy delivery service shows up after 6 pm when the leasing office is closed and they just drive off, never even attempting to use the call boxes (there are two) that are in plain sight! As always I call and complain and get the same fake apologies and promises that it won't happen again. I'm even told that this time they will add instructions to call me prior to delivery if any issues. Well, the next day came and went with no delivery attempt and no phone call. Two damn days of dealing with a manual razor and useless people at Amazon logistics has me infuriated. Then they try to argue saying the driver said no access because the office is closed. I actually asked them if they were F-ing stupid because I have explained multiple times there is 24/7 access via call boxes. I demanded they explain how Dominos, Pizza Hut, Door Dash, Uber Eats and everyone else can deliver food with no issues, but a fracking damn near trillion-dollar company can't hire drivers willing to get off their lazy butts and use a call box? Of course no answer to that. Now I'm demanding they cancel the order and refund me, but they are trying to talk me into giving them another try. No, hell no, you are NOT getting a 3rd delivery attempt, just so the same a-hole can do another drive-by without trying. That was it. I was done. After getting it canceled I ended the call, went online and canceled Prime. I am not wasting another dime on a service that is impossible to receive. The extra 2% discount with Prime isn't worth it either as you need to spend at least $800 every month for that extra 2% to offset the cost of Prime. Free shipping you say? No that's nothing either because the standard shipping on in-stock items is never more than two days anyway. Well, 4-5 when you consider the moron drivers won't even try...",4.0,568,0.9546250503520087,0.04537494964799127,38.64003183461493,Low Trust
Diane Sala,US,1.0,"I had a Kindle fire that was never used.  No book was ever downloaded on it.  I bought it for my 88 year old dad at the time.  Deceased so I got it back recently. Maybe 9 years old. Still in the box it came in.  I got in touch with Amazon to see if I can use it (since mine died.)  Nope! No way even though I was able to give them all the information they required for ownership except an email address that my dad used 8 years ago and has not had an address for probably 6 years.  Send it in for a gift card of $5 and when they review the item, they will let you know about another gift card.  NOPE!  All I got was $5 and a 20% coupon.  I was lied to.  I asked for the unit back and was told - can't do it!  I am so angry that I was lied to and let Customer Service know it.  I was then credited for an different item I purchased last month and still have in my possession of $14.95!  Still angry!",1.0,189,0.9544431988881895,0.045556801111810485,34.397862489690354,Low Trust
