Julie-Anne Smith,GB,1.0,"Absolutely shocking experienceI stopped in all day for a delivery, followed the tracker and was told driver 1 stop away and location less than 100 yards or so away on the next road.....no delivery so  checked tracker again....it then says driver has a few more deliveries to do....still no delivery....tracker then updates to say delivery attempted. NO IT WAS NOT!.I then went through to Amazon customer services and was fobbed off with obvious scripted apology and advised driver would be instructed to re deliver today.I followed the tracker again to see delivery attempted again at 7.11, NO IT WAS NOT!!.Second contact in customer services advises that the re delivery was attempted 54km away from my address!The driver is obviously incapable of doing his job and telling the truth.The operative has now cancelled the order and refunded me.I worry for anyone ordering on their prime promotion day.My order was in reaction to one of the daily offer texts I get from Amazon....obviously too good to be true and they are incapable of fulfilling them",9.0,173,0.9351074052703137,0.06489259472968634,35.18517937193019,Low Trust
Stephen rekab,IE,1.0,"I was offered a FREE 7 day, NO OBLIGATION trial of Amazon PRIME as I landed at the check out webpage. I opted in: ""sure why not says I""However after a day or so, I had buyer's remorse and choose to cancel my Amazon Prime membership. What happened next was disappointing:My item went missing for 10 days without a notification from the seller - who had shipped it - or Amazon PRIME - who had lost it! Reaching out to Amazon online, I asked what had happened to my purchase. Having been compelled to call Amazon, after a long wait, I opted for a call back. A very nice lady offered me a full refund. FYI, this option was not displayed to me online. ""Great ! thanks, yes please. Let's do that"". Guess what happened next? She sends the money back into my credit card account  and withing a couple of hours of it happily resting in my account - don't I get an email next day saying the product was being delivered!  It arrives; I print the RETURNS LABELS and stick them to the unopened box. Then I noticed that the Package required a STAMP, which turned out to be €9.00 So I found myself being put in a position of PAYING for accepting a NO OBLIGATION FREE TRAIL OF AMAZON PRIME 24-48 HOUR SHIPPING - should I RETURN a refunded order. Mmmm!?!OR alternately I am tacitly being invited to injure my personal integrity if I don't post the (now) unwanted item back to the shop who in fact had sold and shipped it in good faith. It seems to me that it ought to be the manager responsible for the online Free AMAZON PRIME trail promotion- who should be the individual sanctioned for making an offer s/he never intended to honor in word as well as spirit.  Shame on you Sir or Madam, no doubt on a lower wrung of the Regional management ladder, on your shifting your lack of integrity from yourself and onto the shop or the guileless customer you have out witted today. Are you proud of your interpretation of fair procedure of a dispute between a shop, a customer and Amazon Prime?",19.0,368,0.9350574105980889,0.06494258940191111,37.3750038391365,Low Trust
Crystal Parrish,US,1.0,HORRIBLE COMPANY!!!! I don't get why everyone loves Amazon.  Items are always missing IF they even ever get delivered to begin with.  Impossible to get a refund or replacement sent.  Every time I've ordered from them I've always had an issue. Will be deleting my account.  Not worth the headache.,1.0,50,0.9350200579232502,0.06497994207674984,33.8098495996311,Low Trust
chandra Paredes,AU,1.0,"Non customer, I have received a text message from Amazon about a purchased a didn’t make, when I rang them to tell them I did not made the purchase and that they have the wrong number, they wanted to know my account details and full name. I DO NOT HAVE AN ACCOUNT WITH THEM!!! I hope no one has made the mistake and punched in my number by mistake because I have blocked them. Otherwise they are just trying to scum me. Please be aware! Terrible customer service, Indian people that can’t even speak proper English.",1.0,96,0.9348445897579504,0.06515541024204963,34.33460730402621,Low Trust
PD,GB,1.0,"I didn’t want to do this but it’s got to the point Where I feel something really has to be said or done now. What is it with amazon delivery drivers knocking on the door, but not waiting at all, they literally dump your parcel every single time on the floor in front of the door, knock and then run off back to their vans and drive off”!! 😡😡 what the hell”! So this is really caring about your costumers eh? I am always home the majority of the time and they never ever give me a chance to get to their door. We have cameras on the house and it clearly shows they just knock and run off 😯. They don’t wait at all for you to answer. How is this right !? I’ve always had my settings as leave in safe place but they never ever do this no more. Its lucky I’m in because I’m sure everyone else is at risk of having their parcels nicked seen as they r completely exposed to the public. Anyone can take your parcel. I have reported this whenever it asks for my feedback on how the driver did. But seems they all do it now and nothing ever gets done about it. Something should be done about this. It’s sick.",31.0,220,0.9346987577047048,0.06530124229529521,35.73281309625663,Low Trust
RL deWeever,NL,1.0,Amazon puts cheap carrier/delivery services and never complies with their dates there is always an excuse for any delays and they are at all INTERESTED in their customers. PITNEY BOWES IS THE WORST!!!,8.0,33,0.9345735841155097,0.06542641588449027,33.641483441448294,Low Trust
Miracles Happen,US,5.0,"I have been an Amazon/prime shopper for years and YEARS and then some.  A bazillion dollar company doesn't need little guy reviews. It will not make or break them at all.  When something is horrible, we all race to our puters to leave BAD reviews, I know, I am one of those people and I call em like I see em! FAST.  But when something is good, we often forget to give those shout outs.Amazon might as well be a family member for as often as I am ordering things and boxes showing up at my door.  Little things, BIG THINGS, VERY high dollar things, lots of low to mid dollar things, household things, and even food.Have I had counterfeit items. YES.  I have a have items not arrive, rarely but yes!  Have I gotten broken items, you betcha?  Have I gotten items not nearly as described! Uh huh.  Not that often but every single time I contacted customer service via chat for starters.  At first I would always get someone in India or the phillipines and I was thinking to myself ....oh Lawd, here we go, they are not going to understand me the loud-mouthed American, this will not have a happy ending, etc.  BOY WAS I WRONG and quick to misjudge.  These people are SO NICE and the way customer service SHOULD be!  They always, and usually through chat only, resolve whatever my problem is, be it a replacement, a refund and I REALLY feel that their apologies are sincere.(and I am cynical too)  In one case I did have to go through 3 reps to get resolution but that was the only time.  I have also spoken to their customer service on the phone and again, no matter who I speak to, no matter their race or country-problem gets resolved-FAST.I also am an online shopper of many other places.  Think along the lines of HSN, WALMART, CHEWY etc.  If I have a problem with one of those places, OMG its a hair pulling NIGHTMARE to get it fixed, be it a replacement or refund.So IMHO and from my years of experience with Amazon, I want to say THANK YOU for having the BEST CUSTOMER SERVICE on the PLANET!  Other companies need to learn from you.",1.0,378,0.9342762590044781,0.06572374099552192,157.52623191797576,High Trust
Megan,US,4.0,"I would give them a full 5 stars except for one thing that drives me absolutely nuts! The actual Amazon drivers never knock on the door.  When something is delivered via the post office or Fed Ex I always get a knock. However, whenever an actual Amazon van delivers something they never knock.  I wouldn't care except for the fact that people love to steal packages from the area I live. Why not knock??? You don't have to talk to the people. You're already taking a picture so just knock on the door!!!",2.0,93,0.9341508575755617,0.06584914242443829,124.33564276339801,High Trust
Sspencer,GB,1.0,"I was due an Amazon delivery today, at approx 5.30pm the tracking said 6 stops away, at 7.30 pm it was still showing 6 stops away but the tracking dot was going in the opposite directions further away than at 6.30, at exactly 10pm (latest delivery time) I got  message sorry  your delivery is late will be delivered tomorrow! If you dont receiv it you can come tomorrow and ask for a refund why would i order something if i wanted a refund the nxt day!!! The reason I pay prime membership is to get my orders when I want them, not when the delivery driver can be bothered, so I can ensure someone is at home to take delivery.Absolutely disgusted what's the point of paying prime.",25.0,127,0.9340096211773923,0.06599037882260772,34.72408428044614,Low Trust
