Scott Mine,US,2.0,"Do NOT trust ""2 day or 1 day shipping"" as advertised!As a Prime member, I've usually enjoyed shipping as advertised, but in late 2018, and now in 2019, too many times has Amazon broken their promise on shipping.  And I pay over $100.00 for this?  In short, when I put an item in the basket, it shows the day it's to be delivered.  Even more, once I place the order, I check to see if it's the same delivery date, and it shows the same.  But on the day of delivery, they'll wait until late night to show it's been ""delayed"" and it's then usually 2 or 3 more days scheduled to be delivered!!!!Would this be ""false advertising"" in the real world???",1.0,122,0.9271146877073584,0.07288531229264161,65.01274570436848,Medium Trust
Vinyl Norwegian,NO,1.0,Amazon is a scam company!I was dumb enough to use a free trail for Amazon benefits that also includes Prime Video. I also use two-factor authentication for my account. But 24 hour later and not even used the benefits yet and they claimed there was suspicious activity and they temporarily closed my account even though there had been no activity. And to get help they force me to either log in or call customer service. And it will cost alot to call from here. So had do cancel my credit card instead since I can't access my account to manage my subscription. This is quite insane! I will never ever recomend anyone using any service from Amazon!🤬 They actually try to scam people!🤬,3.0,123,0.9266462783820707,0.0733537216179293,35.04738322054873,Low Trust
Ray Foster,US,2.0,I have a prime account and yet I still have to watch commercials on the prime video! The delivery people for the goods I recieve Don't follow instructions ! They allow Market Fleecing like same item prices ranging from 5$ to 50$ or more ! I would like a more honest company ! ,1.0,53,0.9265871507000584,0.07341284929994163,64.2651461105383,Medium Trust
Chirag,IN,1.0,"Amazon actually proves that the Customer is no longer the king and that you're only there to give them profits. Here's a breakdown of what Amazon stands for today:1. Absolute Garbage Customer Support, IF at all you do manage to get in touch with one.2. The CS Rep has probably not even seen the face of elementary school since all they do is copy and paste replies from FAQs. I don't know what they're being paid for.3. 99% of the products you receive will be in a flimsy plastic wrapper with absolutely no padding at all and your item will be damaged for sure - All in the name of being Eco Friendly. But then you return and ask for a replacement and repeat, more such materials are wasted. So much for being Eco Friendly. In one instance, I literally had to return an item 8 times before I could get one in working order. Not so Eco friendly, just a diplomatic way of making more profits by saving on packaging costs!4. The CS Reps are powerless, they won't help you because they have no power and those that can do something won't get in touch with you, they're the so called back end and no matter what the rep tells you, no one is passing on your comments to the back end, believe me, I know. THE BIGGEST MISMATCH! It's hilarious!5. Apparently, 95% of the stuff sold on Amazon is low quality sourced from China, India and other third world countries and none of them have any kind of health and safety approvals whatsoever and almost everyone is a seller on Amazon selling whatever garbage they desire. And then you see cases of lead poisoning and other health related issues from using that plastic item you just bought from Amazon. Yes that's the culprit. Try to spend a little more and buy Branded stuff Made in a Developed country with checks and licensing authorities if you have a desire to live longer. If only Amazon was 'responsible' enough to do that for us.6. Packaging Standards are the WORST of any online retailer out there. Their frustration free packaging is a scam, it gives you a lot of frustration when you see broken items inside. There's NO bubble wrap or Foam peanuts or any sort of padding at all. Just the item thrown inside a flimsy polybag or a thin crushed box. I don't know who the wise guy is behind the packaging team but there are times when I receive an item as it is with shipping slip stuck directly on to it and there's no Amazon branded packing at all. Not even that low quality plastic bag. Imagine that!7. You actually end up wasting time and in turn money when you have to return, then reorder and then repeat and then speak to customer rep and then still get no resolution and apparently now their 10 day return is changing into 7 days replacement on some items, clever move. Instead of mending own ways, it's better to screw the customer, Bravo Amazon!8. In the end, it's your money. Either you can give it to support a retailer that keeps growing big and keeps screwing your happiness with no concern for your health, expectations, feedback and your hard earned money OR you can choose to boycott them and support a better company or another retailer instead that might be charging similar or maybe a little higher for the same item but will deliver it right the first time and will also stand behind it's products and be there for it's customers. 9. And since I've been fighting for my rightful money and asking for them to improve their packaging standards and had to constantly return items everytime due to damage or cheap quality, my account was BLACKLISTED by them and now they won't let me open another account or even let me get in touch with them. So much for being the world's largest online retailer. This is their sorry state. The choice is yours, the money is yours...",6.0,680,0.9258631318646521,0.07413686813534792,41.33443734956044,Low Trust
Edward,GB,1.0,"Delivery service needs to be returned to Royal Mail. The current service in my area run by Arrow is totally C.R.A.P. They were supposed to make a delivery by 8pm today 9th November, confirmed by Amazon and by tracking. It was dispatched from Amazon on 4th November, was conformed as being with Arrow. This afternoon I had a phone call telling me it would be delivered on Wednesday. My delivery is probably sitting in Arrows depot. Rubbish!!!!",2.0,77,0.9258359368030965,0.0741640631969035,34.57191600336733,Low Trust
Chandreia,US,1.0,"They need to teach their delivery people how to find addresses or at least to have a way to contact the customer if they are having trouble finding the delivery address. Why would I walk around looking for a package I wanted delivered? If I wanted to walk, I would've gone to Target, which is what I should have done. I'm not ordering anything else from them. Then they hold your money for 3 days? For what? I don't have my package!!! Take the money from the driver with ROCKS FOR BRAINS!",4.0,92,0.925752481704916,0.07424751829508403,34.74434450701443,Low Trust
