jeanette molloy,GB,1.0,"I placed an order and they asked for a phone number on my account. I used every number I had and couldn’t access my account. I phoned customer service in India and they couldn’t even understand my name despite spelling it I was raging and frustrated and hung up. I told  the next one I couldn’t access my account because of the phone number. She asked for THE phone number I sad I don’t have it, I was blowing a fuse by this time.  Asked  to speak to a manager as she obviously didn’t understand my situation. I couldn’t speak to anyone all she said was she couldn’t progress till I gave her a  phone  number. I’m in a rage by this time I hung up and closed my account. I’m owed £149.28 from a cancelled order sitting in my pending transactions.  My bank gave me the authorisation code to ask them to cancel the transaction from they’re end. This time on the phone to South Africans who refused to even consider tracing the authorisation code. Manager refused point blank and was almost aggressive with me. Used resolver and wrote the emails. Said the email address was unmanned. Gave me links down the usual route!Wrote to Amazon complaints and again the  email address again is unmanned! Gave me usual links.   Are Amazon hiding from  customers and can’t they employ possibly   Afghanistan’s to answer the emails without coming  in contact with any telephones? I want my money refunded and I will get it by any means!  I’m disgusted at this company and they should hire English speaking people. We pay them enough. Not people who speak foreign dialect  English!",12.0,278,0.920539968823461,0.07946003117653899,37.0913414354394,Low Trust
