Me,US,1.0,"Amazon's GC PROMO: 2% WHEN LOADED FROM DEBIT CARD (Since I can't attach any file here, to view the promo, go to Reload GC, then it will promt you to view the promo.) So I availed the above promo, reloaded GC from debit card on 2/25 with a small trial amount -before I put in more $.  But the 2% NEVER came which counters their claim/advertisement. On the same date 2/25 I used GC to purchase an item.  So there should have been some leftover, only to find out several days after- that the remaining money that was still there 2/25 after I bought the item suddenly disappeared! With an agent saying that it  went to a much earlier order made 2/22- which should NEVER have had happened coz at the time of that order, on 2/22, the items were FULLY paid on that same order day 2/22, so there shouldn't be ANY FLOATING UNPAID amount at all which would be charged days after on 2/25. Amazon CAN'T have any price change after I ordered & fully paid the purchase already on 2/22. So there are 2 ISSUES HERE: 1) MISSING 2% on the $ I put into the GC from my debit card as advertised. 2) MISSING money deducted WITHOUT my knowledge days after I ordered items.  BOTH of which should be put & returned to my GC, NOT in the form of promo credits. I REFUSE that Amazon will again FORCE me to just accept the missing 2% in the form of promo credits. No, I do not need those promo credits where I could only access & make use of by buying only certain Amazon items I'm NOT interested in buying at all! This is like conning me of my own money. Who gave Amazon the right to decide how it will be returned to me when my debit card's worth + the amount deducted from me are both good as cash, NOT good as promo credits being forced on me.  And it's a TOTAL FRAUD if Amazon's gonna force promo credits on me to pay me of the missing 2% because this CONTRADICTS their promo clearly saying that it should appear as 2% right there & then! All of Amazon's agents/managers are pathetically clueless of this promo & this is a VIOLATION of our trust when they post promos NONE of agents are able to help customers with coz they have ZERO product knowledge of it. Worse, I requested to be escalated to the correct dept, twice promised, made to wait for days, but none! A little bit of RESPECT of my time when I already wasted almost 4 hours now being passed on to around 10 agents and different departments & now reporting to this to Trustpilot to warn others of this 2% because all avenues failed in Amazon. This is so unfair & unacceptable.",4.0,480,0.9162589957499991,0.08374100425000086,39.571234172118665,Low Trust
Jessica,GB,2.0,"I rely on Amazon a lot for quick deliveries, and typically things go to plan, but when things go wrong the customer service options are very limited. I have a returns issues I need assistance with right now, and I have tried two email addresses which bounce back, the online call me function which doesn't recognize the +44 area code for the UK (?!?!), the chatbot which  just went quiet on me after saying ""I'll look into this and get back to you in a minute"" and the number the website told me to call which provided a recorded message redirecting me to the main website! For a tech company its pretty disappointing that nothing works!",16.0,116,0.915395552185393,0.08460444781460696,65.53140018097152,Medium Trust
Michelle A Finn,US,1.0,"Normally they're not horrible. But, after dealing with a seller who lied consistently for 2 weeks saying he shipped the product he did not ship and then telling me the day I need it though they forgot, so I had to go and buy one at the local store for six times the price. After dealing with that I contact Amazon customer service to write a review on the seller. After writing to separate reviews continually Amazon told me that my reviews were negative and therefore could not be published so I decided to chat with their customer service. You would figure that chatting with customer service would mean an actual person? Nope! Not only in that not an actual person but a computer system that doesn't even speak English properly! After getting the exact same paragraph multiple times with the exact same grammatical and spelling errors I decided screw it. And I tried to contact Amazon through email or phone. Nope! So I decided to try to contact the seller, nope! Basically I'm stuck. If you get a seller that super crappy, tough. Amazon is a figment of your imagination and actual people don't work there, it's little green Martian men that you can never get ahold of",1.0,209,0.9149263125434125,0.0850736874565875,36.59804780524665,Low Trust
