Janet,US,1.0,I purchased a Samsung S24 phone on Amazon for a family member because she requested it due to the $150 Amazon.com Promo Credit that was included with the phone. Their promo credit allows the buyer to spend $150 on items sold and shipped by Amazon. Seemed like a good deal for someone who wants to buy some extra accessories or other items.The instructions clearly said that the promo was applied automatically and that the buyer would receive an email after the phone gets delivered. The phone was delivered 2 days ago and still no Amazon promo credit. I spoken to 12 customer service agents and NONE of them knew wth they were talking about and gave non-sensical responses. They acted like the promo didn’t exist and asked me to send them links and screenshots to the phone even though they have my order and can see the product listing. I eventually gave up and my relative (who was already disappointed by this) asked for the phone to be returned. I went online to see if anyone else had this experience and I saw posts the past months where other buyers had the same problem. What a waste of time and why am I not surprised?!,173.0,205,0.9142467432908866,0.08575325670911338,36.587158068209455,Low Trust
