BigBenF,US,1.0,"Update - 7/12/23 - Amazon POOR Delivery.Amazon Driver launches a package on to my porch that is clearly marked as “Extremely Fragile” on ALL SIDES.Now my electronic device does not work right out of the package.This is what you will get for being a Amazon Prime Member.Amazon needs to get their act together.This company makes obtaining warranty requests from Amazon Seller’s extremely difficult after 30 days.If you send a Seller a request for a warranty claim or product issue, Amazon insists that you do not send personal information to the Seller such as email addresses, physical addresses & phone numbers.Amazon fulfills over 90% of orders so Seller’s don’t have your contact information. Only your money.Here is what you will get when sending a Amazon Seller a message:Please limit your text to less than 4000 characters. For your security, do not include any personal information including email addresses, physical addresses, phone numbers or credit card numbers in your message.So here is my question ???If I can’t give the Seller any of my personal information….how am I supposed to get warranty coverage for an item purchased on Amazon ??(Don’t bother contacting Amazon after 30 days for help either. They will simply tell you that the return window has closed and that there is nothing else that they can do.)You have to play a game with Amazon and send messages to Seller’s in a way that Amazon won’t intercept the message and it is undeliverable.I usually type everything out on paper and take a picture of it and use that to send a message to the Seller via Amazon messaging.Lastly, if you leave a Seller a honest and fair review and Amazon doesn’t like your honesty…..you will get a nasty red message and they also DO NOT reply for a explanation either. If you are in the mood for a extremely hard time, difficulties & terrible, bad customer service after 30 days of purchase….contact Amazon via chat or a phone call. You will get EXACTLY what you are looking for. A heart attack. I promise !!!What a waste of time ! 😠",88.0,349,0.906869785136977,0.09313021486302298,38.571261163790524,Low Trust
BebeC,GB,1.0,A few days ago a parcel was left (evening time) outside and it rained heavily overnight.  The packaging fell apart when lifted from the puddle!  Contents fortunately OK.  But was courier being unhelpful?  Our doorbell does work!!,29.0,37,0.9067842080878203,0.09321579191217966,35.07582044249625,Low Trust
TW,US,1.0,"My review is strictly about Amazon Delivery Services and how much they really SUCK!Never on time, when they say by 9PM they mean you'll get it shortly before 9PM.  The amazon delivery service shows up in cars, trucks, vans, uhaul vehicles, etc. so how the heck are we supposed to know these people are legit?  Most of the time they run up to front porch, throw package down at door, never ring doorbell, snap a pic, and off they run!. This past Friday, I'm standing in my driveway, the driver shows up with headphones in ears, scans packages after 10 minutes of digging thru vehicle, runs up to front porch (hello I'm RIGHT THERE IN YOUR LINE OF SIGHT!) drops packages, snaps a pic and runs off.  One of the packages was for a neighbor 3 houses down main street (i'm on a culdesac).  These guys are something else to say the least!  I'm 18 miles from a distribution center and anytime it says ""delivery by 9PM"" they do mean we are going to delivery to everyone else's known to mankind packages before we deliver your packages at 8:58PM after I've been waiting an entire day to receive.",3.0,198,0.9066810241172848,0.0933189758827152,36.88692467747844,Low Trust
