Rekka,US,1.0,"Absolutely disgusted with Amazon's customer service right now! This morning I received a package that I did not order (and have no record of ordering on either my Amazon account or my bank account), containing an item I did not want, and with absolutely no indication of who sent it. It was also sent to me under my legal name, which is not the name I list my Amazon account under.I tried to contact Amazon's customer service to figure out how this happened. I explained exactly why I was so upset: I am a young adult woman living alone. Receiving this sort of bizarre package, without warning, from an unknown sender, is extremely disturbing and terrifying. I had already contacted everyone I knew or had contact with who would have my address and legal name; none of them had any clue about the package, either. Amazon was absolutely ZERO help! They flatly refused to check who sent it to me, insisting that unless I was able to give them an EXACT NAME, there was nothing they could do because ""we can't access the account."" They insisted no one could and refused to escalate the complaint, either. I then asked how it was possible that some unknown stranger could gain access to my personal information to send me this item and they refused to explain that, either. They also refused to explain how I could leave a comment or complaint about the issue and refused to explain what the hell I was supposed to do with this item!I was already avoiding Amazon as much as possible due to their horrible business practices, the way they have undercut and destroyed local businesses, driven housing prices in Seattle through the roof, treated their warehouse employees like disposable goods, and bent over backwards to appease organizations like the CCP. This is just adding insult to injury!",2.0,312,0.8984648736555526,0.10153512634444739,38.57647589097447,Low Trust
