Sarah Kinch,GB,1.0,"Their delivery is so bad!  Honestly if I could give zero stars I would.  Every time I order from Amazon, I track the delivery & every single time the delivery person has marked it as ""Delivered, handed to customer"" when they haven't!  Not even bothering to try the doorbell or knock on a window, they just dump my packages behind a bin without any security or an attempt to hide them from the less law-abiding public looking for a freebie!  If my package isn't delivered at all then customer services are ridiculously useless.  You call & get a robot asking silly questions, you answer as it tells you to & it hangs up!  Utterly pointless.",2.0,115,0.894724829457071,0.10527517054292901,36.55371926747175,Low Trust
James g,GB,1.0,Fed up with prime deliveries are always late one order took 2 weeks to arrive when it should have been next day I ordered an item yesterday for same day delivery when it came to being delivered I got an email saying it was delayed and now have to wait for up to 3 days it takes the p!ss considering Amazon are happy to put the fees up and take your money for a service they clearly can’t provide and it is becoming regular with my orders I’m going to cancel my prime because it literally is just sh!t and you don’t get any compensation or anything for the inconvenience amazon have simply become greedy it’s become a crap company and I’m really p!ssed off with it now I’ve been a customer for years and this is how they treat their customers absolutely disgusting,85.0,144,0.8946290634640497,0.10537093653595031,36.8838020146831,Low Trust
RDe RCh,US,1.0,Pay for Prime but won't ship certain items to my location. What a waste of money!!!,1.0,16,0.8946036692149364,0.10539633078506361,35.44928933790713,Low Trust
Manickam Hellmuth,US,1.0,"I've been a pretty frequent amazon customer over at least the last two decades. The downfall started with a decision to purchase a macbook pro for around $3000. A large purchase, but I had confidence that if anything went wrong amazon would right things quickly. I received a one time passcode or OTP as they refer to it. I greeted the amazon delivery person, I gave him the passcode several times- he kept repeating it back incorrectly. I took the package and remarked to my girlfriend that man they make macs light these days. I opened the package to find an obviously used and abused macbook box. I opened the box with an ever increasing heart rate as I knew at this point my worst fears were about to be realized. It was EMPTY! My girlfriend rushed out the door to the driver who was just down the street. He stated you want to look in the back of my truck? Nothing I can do, call amazon support. Of course I called right away. I sat on hold for at least 30-40 mins. Amazon's first attempt at resolving the issue was to tell me there was nothing that could be done since I gave them the OTP- they stated I should call the police???!!!! When I refused and stated I had already wasted my day with this whole situation they put me on hold again for many minutes. They finally returned and refunded my order. This person refunded me with the most disgust I've ever experienced in my years of customer service. She quickly said bye, none of the usual thanks for being an amazon customer... Little did I know the issues would only continue from here. Later that evening I received an email stating my account had most likely been hacked and all my orders were cancelled. Next I came to find out that any order around $100+ would require a OTP- meaning they send you a passcode via email a couple hrs before your order arrives that you're forced to give to the delivery person- meaning you have to be present all day long if you actually want to receive your order. That's exactly the opposite of what amazon was designed to be. I called in multiple times to have this obstruction / inconvenience removed. One person from logistics stated maybe I should buy my macbook from apple like he did? I asked if he ever bought anything on amazon for $100+ he stated no. After talking to several more people from all over the world one person agreed to give me a partial refund of around $79 of the $139 I was so exhausted I agreed to it. I now realize that it makes no sense, given it's only almost April 1st and a prorated refund would be $100+??? This has been a pretty ridiculous experience to say the least. I repeated my grievances multiple times and I don't think one person understood once, much less did they try and correct it or provide any kind of customer service. PS I'm still waiting for my $79 refund... ",1.0,520,0.8945480207148034,0.10545197928519656,41.105464920513334,Low Trust
CC,GB,5.0,Excellent customer services who listen and have a good speed to answer.  Great prices and quick delivery along with a massive collection of products and sellers.  Good reviews of each item and a well structured/searchable site.  The list goes on!  Get involved if you havent already!,57.0,46,0.8945324052938483,0.10546759470615175,155.7893640314377,High Trust
