Alan Clarkson,US,1.0,"I think Amazon has gotten too big for their own britches. Too many mistakes, and they've forgotten the customers that brought this far. Their customer service is based on 'don't let the customer be right. We don't care what happened'.I've had a few botched deliveries lately. This last one, today, 5/29/2024, drove me to write this. I ordered a $95 knife (Spyderco Delica 4), on 5/27/2024. Amazon showed it would be delivered the next day. For the next 2 days, I was notified that there was a delay. I received it today. Kind of. I received a package. Not the knife I ordered and paid for. It was flat. I opened it. It was a piece of rubber in a plastic bag. No idea what it was for. So, I paid $95 for a knife, and received a 25 cent piece of rubber! I went through the return process. Amazon states that I'll receive a refund within 30 days, after they receive the return item. EPIC FAIL! AGAIN! For about the 5th time in 3 months. And, of course, they won't let you talk to a human. I'm getting real sick of this stupid stuff, their 'we don't care' attitude,  and lousy service!",1.0,203,0.8696986163849996,0.13030138361500043,38.79213031367206,Low Trust
