Mr.Tom,US,1.0,"I bought an baritone ukulele from Amazon, and when I received it, it had a warped neck .Customer Service would ""not"" help me, so they sent me to this so-called ""Amazon executive customer relations group"" in regards to my issue. This group ""TOTALLY"" did not care about who I was, and the money that I lost in regards to this issue. I actually write commercially licensed music, and there was a contracted deal with paid royalties in perpetuity that I needed this Baritone Ukulele for in regards to the song I was writing.. and again.. the ONLY THING that this so called upper tier so-called Amazon executive customer relations group would do is just tell me that I need to waste MORE OF MY TIME and send the baritone ukulele back to them.. THEN MAYBE they would refund my money! REALLY!?!?! This Amazon group was also VERY RUDE AND INSULTING to me in there over all tone and also lack of following up with my MANY email replies. No matter how much money that I LOST in regards to the contracted deal that I could not write this song for, because of receiving a defective instrument that Amazon is responsible FOR.. that did not matter to them.. AT ALL. The ironic thing, is that one of my own digital partners, is selling one of my song on Amazon... and I'm certainly going to tell them on how Amazon treats songwriters / composers.",10.0,242,0.860919231055527,0.13908076894447297,39.6685645268647,Low Trust
