Reese,US,1.0,"Amazon provided good customer service before before Covid-19. Now, it is virtually non-existent and they are allowing customers to be scammed by their 3rd party sellers & Amazon’s participation, in my opinion.  Tried to cancel an order (after seeing seller had 50% approval rating) less than 30 min after placing it. Amazon’s website directed me to 3rd party seller to cancel it thru auto chat (I couldn’t get a live body online chat or via telephone). Sent seller email asking them to cancel my order and they quickly responded back that I had to handle it on my end which I assumed meant on the Amazon site.  I sent email back to seller telling them Amazon sent me to them to cancel & Shocker, this time they waited over 24 hours to respond. I tried over and over to get a live body to speak with in an online chat or to call me but their system just circle jerked me and ultimately said no one was available or disconnected me from online chat forcing me to start over. 24 hours later I finally got an online chat with a live body only to be quoted policy(that Amazon & their seller hadn’t followed) & told the order hadn’t shipped and she would send email to seller. Asked for manager & he told me I wouldn’t be held financially accountable so not to worry.  Today I get a follow up phone call telling me the order shipped before Amazon got a response from the seller, asked for manager who just quoted me Amazon policies (ignoring that them & their seller not following their policies is what caused the issue. She ignored what I said and just kept quoting Amazon policies. She told me that the manager I previously spoke with should have done a better job of communicating because I could be held financially liable. I asked for her boss and she told me basically that she’s the top of the food chain available to me. Ethics & customer service no longer exist at Amazon!!!!",3.0,344,0.8607378265673408,0.13926217343265923,40.82177384269297,Low Trust
