None of your beeswax,US,1.0,"If I could give negative 5 stars I would. It’s not up to you amazon you dictate what I have on my phone. It’s not your job to tell me what I want. Guess what? I canceled my prime membership, music, noggin, and three other subscriptions I had through you. I will also be getting rid of my ring doorbell. GOODBYE! American patriots! Ditch these people who think they own you!",4.0,71,0.8490191292111807,0.15098087078881928,38.345454083467885,Low Trust
Cindy,US,1.0,"If you don't regularly use an amazon account. I HIGHLY recommend you go in and completely clear all your information off of amazon and then delete the account completely. Apparently they let hackers in to change how you can log in but they won't let you into your account unless you provide a gov't issued photo ID.A hacker in Portland, OR was able to access my amazon account. They then placed an order for 10 video games (easily resold) and used my saved card information. They then used the amazon deliver to a guy on a street corner service to avoid giving out an actual address. (I got this from the second person I talked to who wasn't supposed to tell me that much.)While the hackers were in my account they added a second log in requirement. This prevented ME from accessing my account until I proved to amazon that I was me with a photo ID. Amazon said to allow TWO DAYS for this to clear. During that time amazon said they were unable to secure my account from the hacker.The fourth amazon employee I spoke with (they kept switching countries and none of the employees were in the US) heard a few choice words from me and it actually took them less than an hour after I sent a copy of my driver's license.NOW, amazon was in my account and deleted the fraud order but would not allow me access until they gave me the run around for 24 hours!! So they were able to delete the information on the hacker's orders (more were in processing) BUT they refused to delete my personal information for my protection. So the hackers still have my full name, address and phone number.No fraud on my account was detected by them even tho an order for something I have never remotely ordered before was shipped to some where I have never shipped to before.Good-bye Amazon!!",1.0,323,0.8480333501583551,0.15196664984164487,41.22143961490894,Low Trust
