Paula Elvey,GB,1.0,"What an absolutely appalling experience I have received from Amazon over the last 10 days.  My ac was hacked and an item I did not order was sent to me (yes my address) and £70 vouchers given for my birthday were used to pay for it, alongside £9 from my business account (item was £79).  I duly returned the item after informing them of the situation with my ac.  Since then, the only communication is via Livechat.  Only one advisor (Jason, on Mon June 22nd) was polite and helpful, and today Fri June 26th Mark (1535 time) was particularly rude, unhelpful and ended up just ignoring me.  I have the screenshots on my phone.  Basically they have the item back unopened but will not refund me!  Will not transfer me to the relevant dept and will not do anything!! Apart from the security issue - what a terrible way to treat a customer, not give the item back and refuse to help.  I really enjoyed using my Amazon AC but unless I get someone to deal with this soon, I fear I may never use again. And that would be a shame as they were usually pretty good before.  Hopefully someone out there can help.",30.0,205,0.8367619972169115,0.16323800278308853,40.46139537190821,Low Trust
S L,GB,1.0,"I used to use Amazon for almost everything because I thought they are the best. They are expansive compared to Ali express. The same thing on Ali express is 6 quid and on Amazon it becomes 29.99 how is it possible.Had a delivery from Amazon US packed by Amazon themselves and then it came all opened and ripped apart no customs check was sticked onto the parcel so I’m pretty sure customs didn’t open the parcel. Tracking didn’t even give any useful information. (BTW they use fake tracking as I tried to type the tracking they give on the site to the delivery people. It says tracking not found) It stopped updating for a few days so I don’t even know where the parcel is. Contacted Amazon, they said they cannot do anything about it because the tracking doesn’t update to delivered and asked me to contact the shipping company myself... surely that is their job. The staff were very unhelpful as they keep saying ask the delivery people as we don’t know who it is... and we cannot chase after them ourselves, then quickly ended the chat... Sent them photos of the products and left a review.  Received a message from Amazon apparently my review is fake and misleading as they do not want any negative reviews on the products... worst company ever. I will be shopping with eBay and Ali express from now on. Shame on you!!!",6.0,239,0.8356568160422093,0.16434318395779068,40.89803412778297,Low Trust
Cristina Mano,GB,2.0,"PAYING PRIME to Amazon does not worth it!I purchased an item that should have arrived on the same day and Amazon registered that as "" Delivered in my letter box "". There was nothing in there! After contacting the customer service they kept saying that the item was delivered, when there wasn't. In the end they offered me a refund of it... this doesn't help at all, as I wanted the item! So, my question is, where is the money going on Prime if they cannot assure the delivery of these items?",3.0,92,0.8356401377010583,0.16435986229894173,69.24996170720732,Medium Trust
Cathy Plant,GB,1.0,"Received an email to say that parcels were handed to the resident. I am the resident, they were not!I have asked for evidence (this can't be provided as there isn't any!)Been told that must waste the time and resources of the police, how can I report a missing item that I have never even seen?There was no note through my door, Amazon won't entertain the idea that it could have been delivered to the wrong house. They have no photos of proof of delivery.Whenever I try to sort this out with so called customer services they cut me off!I shop very regularly on Amazon and am a prime member yet I'm being treated like a liar and a criminal.This is a disgraceful way to treat a loyal customer",2.0,128,0.8354691377516864,0.1645308622483136,39.66232550164731,Low Trust
