Rick Blessinger,US,1.0,Amazon has signed up both my fiancee and myself for services we were not intended to purchase as it states free. Amazon music and Amazon Prime. They are not to be trusted and should be boycotted. Have known many people they continue to scam. With this virus/economic downturn they continue to scam people. Spread the word ecspecially to the older generation and mentally slower and/or just trusting good hearted people. Amazon should be ashamed of yourself. Hear that Jeff Betos!!!,5.0,80,0.8217273517464481,0.17827264825355194,39.810996405947364,Low Trust
Linda M,US,1.0,"This was the final straw.  Nevermind, the late deliveries, forgive the items that don't show at all and omitting the three(3) out of five items that were damaged upon arrival; it was this last transaction that caused me to say enough. I'm finished Amazon!To 2K Furniture and Amazon,My name is Linda M, I am a customer. A customer! I'm contacting you yet again in reference to a Kitchen Buffet that I purchased in March. I have made at least five attempts to get this item back to 2K and have been requesting a refund for a month. I have believed that this should be a very simple process. To explain, a customer purchased an item, they're unsatisfied with the item, they make arrangements to return the item, the company which is reputable and has integrity will assist the purchaser in the return of the item via a return label or transport. The company provides the customer with a full refund of the purchase price. Contract done. I've never experienced a purchase, especially from Amazon, which I was required to pay for the shipping and handling 2 return item that does not satisfy the customer. These are the basics of customer service. Now allow me to further illustrate how easy this process can be resolved. I am requesting that 2K Furniture send me a return label and I am requesting that 2K make arrangements for the pick up by UPS, FedEx, US Postal Service, a truck of a friend that you know, to pick up this item. I do not think it acceptable that I incur any additional cost for your delivering a damaged product. To deliver an item in such terrible condition is unacceptable. Shame on you! Shame on you again! Is this really how you want to represent yourself. Do you really think that this is necessary for $260. Are you willing to sacrifice your reputation for $260. I want my money back. I believe I have been patient enough. I want a refund and a refund shouldn't cost me any more money or distress. If you do not respond to my satisfaction, I will have no other recourse but 2 investigate legal alternatives. I await your response. Thanking you for your cooperation in advance. Your loyal customer Linda M.",2.0,381,0.8216648119060871,0.1783351880939129,43.19045542264293,Low Trust
sandy,US,5.0,"I live in a small town in Washington state, this morning I order some items  off of Amazon, and tonight they arrived. This is so impressive to me. I was able to sit in the comfort of my own home, make a purchased and have it delivered the very same day. Everyone at Amazon is a hero to me, they operate seven days a week, 24 hours a day. Thank you to all of the employees world wide to make those of us at home lives better. Amazon is not a perfect company, but we don’t live in a perfect world. They are doing a great job! Their drivers are friendly and professional. I hope Amazon realizes how great their employees are and what a value they are to their company. They are the face of the company. Store fronts, drivers, pilots…they are making Amazon great! Be kind and appreciate this home delivery service!",5.0,154,0.8216532638028342,0.1783467361971658,160.64476249690262,High Trust
Heather,US,5.0,"I have been an Amazon customer for years and I just can't say enough about how awesome they are! I've used Amazon Prime (when I can afford it), Amazon Mom, and loved every part of it! Even when you have to pay shipping, generally its not too expensive, and you can find just about anything you could possibly want!",6.0,59,0.8212710344506804,0.1787289655493196,159.59825422250245,High Trust
Heather Gulling,US,1.0,What’s the point of “prime” anymore?!? 🤬😤 Continuously annoyed with delivery times and dates stating “shipped” “on way” and then for some phantom reason “sorry for delay…” blah blah blah. Amazon was great once upon a time. They’ve had their moment; as a customer being promised & paying annual fees for “such great expedited times” I’m completely over it!! 🚫,2.0,60,0.8212535706076124,0.1787464293923876,39.6103444645717,Low Trust
claire,GB,1.0,"Was given a fake email address to complain to also which went undelivered when I attempted to make a formal complaint before I take it to the ombudsman. .closed my Amazon Account, really wanted to just close Amazon Prime, yet again charged for amazon Prime when I do not want it.  Accidently closed account? Rang up to sort this out straight away,  Sent an email saying I had miss-used my account>  NO I have not and they can't even tell me why?? just sent out a generic email saying I had,  I rang them and was told in 24 hours you will have a response, 28 hours no so rang them again, no idea why my account is closed, have another 24 hours and lets see what else they can make up???? what a bunch of con people!!!  I wonder what the regulators make of all this from Amazon (Financial Ombudsman Service)  I was also told to open a 2nd account which is against company policy and regulations",39.0,168,0.8210627529337913,0.17893724706620873,40.83132673917695,Low Trust
