Eric Chavez,US,1.0,"Amazon RECIEVED my return on JUNE 7th at 7:40AM, today is JUNE 22nd @ 7:15AM....NO RETURN OF MY MONEY to my credit card!!! CUSTOMER SERVICE HAS NOT HELPED OUT with this.....They just keep going round and round....hard to understand MOST of their agents since ENGLISH is there SECOND language. ",2.0,49,0.8135837163723972,0.18641628362760276,39.87044962725787,Low Trust
Elizabeth Grant,US,5.0,I love shopping at Amazon.com! I have been an off and on member for over 10 years. It is truly my happy pla! I am of course a Prime member and have never had any shipment issues or delays and I order every week at least once or twice I purchse everything from makeup to leggings to jewelry to electronics and household items. I recently purchased a Phoera cosmetic bundle (CC Cream and foundation kit) and some makeup brushes with confidence due to their helpful customer reviews. It all arrived on time and in excellent condition (packaged well as to not have the products break in transit). I haven't had to return anything yet but I did have some questions regarding a return policy and customer service was helpful and pleasant. Before I look anywhere else I hop on Amazon.com and check out the price and product first! If nothing else they are sure to have helpful reviews and maybe a deal or two! Five Stars ⭐ ,2.0,167,0.8132815957723756,0.18671840422762442,161.20916754733187,High Trust
leona morgan,IE,1.0,"I ordered a phone and was delivered a book. I have been passed from pillar to post with customer service with different reps telling me to do different things. When I was eventually advised to return the incorrectly delivered item with a picture accompanying it for the refund to be processed (and the return form specifically said, return the incorrectly delivered item), the refund has not been processed and another customer service rep is advising that they need to send me a mail to gather further information - on top of the many mails that have already been sent on this matter!!! This is Amazon trying to frustrate customers out of having to pay for either their own mistake or fraud. I would strongly advise not ordering an  expensive item from Amazon that you can't afford to take a hit on if they don't deliver the correct item. Absolutely shocking customer service. I am a long loyal customer of Amazon (which my account shows if the customer service reps would be bothered to check it) and up to now we have had no issues with Amazon service but the treatment in this case has been woeful with customer service reps just trying to push the problem along without resolving it. I now don't even have the book they sent in error - so Amazon have my €511 for a phone they didn't deliver and they took back the book they sent in its stead so I have absolutely nothing to show for my 500!",1.0,254,0.8132464041534766,0.1867535958465234,42.186810470957695,Low Trust
Keith Glen,GB,1.0,"I had ordered three items from Amazon, all three were being delivered in one box! One was an expensive item. On delivery I opened the box to find only two items, the expensive one wasn’t there. I have contacted Amazon loads to try and resolve and they have refused saying it was delivered and was in the box at delivery! This item was not, they kept to a script and advised to inform police but the police will not record a crime as I am not the victim, the item was stolen from inside Amazon so they are the victim but they will NOT listen to me, I have even sent the email from the police saying all this and they are still saying I have to record it with them! Not getting a refund or the item so closing my account down and will NEVER use them again!",2.0,149,0.8129973911332138,0.1870026088667862,41.02147088080426,Low Trust
karen Miles,GB,1.0,"Christmas is currently ruined because of Amazon.  I had expected 3 packages today from Amazon.  When they hadn't arrived by 8pm I checked online, only to discover that they had been delivered and signed for by a completely different person in an entirely different location.  I then spent 2 hours trying to find out where my packages had been sent to.  Amazon couldn't contact the driver to re-deliver which is ridiculous!!!  I am so upset by the whole incident that I will no longer be using Amazon.",3.0,87,0.8129005482244989,0.18709945177550114,40.330855931455936,Low Trust
Evgenii,GB,1.0,"Never cooperate with Amazon. As a seller, you will be deceived. We, as the seller, sent the goods to the buyer, which were delivered to the address, for which there is evidence. However, the buyer stated that he had not received the goods and Amazon immediately refunded him the money. It turns out that the buyer simply stole a product worth 219 pounds from us and Amazon contributed to this. Amazon is the accomplices of scammers!!!",2.0,76,0.8127795131480033,0.18722048685199666,40.213520136206114,Low Trust
Stephanie,AU,1.0,"Absolutely terrible ""security"" process. Perhaps leaving a bad review might get some action from them.I bought an item on Amazon.de with my Australian bank card. At first it looked fine, it seemed my order went through. Then less than 24 hours later I got an email saying there was suspicious activity on my account (ie using my non-German card to buy from their German branch) and they cancelled order and asked me to verify my account by submitting proof of order or payment. I sent them a PDF of my order confirmation email but it was rejected. Then about 2 days after my original order, I got an email saying my order was approved and it's on it's way. Now first of all I do not appreciate the hassle it took to place a order. My friend tried to buy something on Amazon.de with a Chinese bank card and the same thing happened. This never happened on the Australian site.Second of all, it is really bad practise for Amazon to automatically deduct the cost from my bank card after initially cancelling my order. If you then decide to approve the order, you should have told me so, not take money from my account and tell me afterwards, that my order is on the way. What happens if I bought the same expensive item in the meantime from elsewhere?! This is very very bad practise! Buyers beware!!Secondly, I have since forgotten my password and cannot log in. When I try to log in, it keeps saying my password is incorrect (even though I think it is correct, if the machine thinks it is wrong, then perhaps it is wrong) and when I try to reset it, 1 of 2 things happen: Last week, it would repeatedly tell me to enter my email address, sends me an OTP One time password to that address, make me enter it, then when I do that, tells me to enter a capcha code and my email address again, then sends me a OTP to that address. Rinse and Repeat.Today, what is happening is, no matter whether I use the Australian or German site, the password recovery process ends in a dead end where it says:""Looking for Something? We're sorry. The Web address you entered is not a functioning page on our site. Go to Amazon.com.au's Home Page""From the home page you can try to log in again or reset your password using the method above.When I contacted customer service using the only other digital method I can, via twitter, they told me to make a call to their German branch, something I cannot do at the moment.I've been unable to log in for over a week and thus unable to change my delivery instructions or use or cancel any subscriptions I have.When I tried to contact them for help, their help site tells you to call them (which I can't do) or send a secure email message to them by, get this... logging in to your account.Absolutely terrible, will never use again, especially considering the winners here are the Amazon team, they also rip off sellers by charging a $1 fee just to list their item apart from other transaction/sales fees.Buy elsewhere, don't support the ripping off of sellers and their crappy system.",11.0,548,0.8125739260205203,0.18742607397947975,45.518247052871914,Low Trust
Jewels,US,1.0,"My account was hacked and someone was using my email account and writing terrible reviews under my name, I spoke to both departments because I now am not able to leave reviews and all reviews I have left have been removed. They said they would have their ""Team"" look into this and solve this issue for me! That's funny, what I did get was several emails telling me about their ""guidelines"" for reviews and fraudulent activity.And 1 very insulting email almost implying that my claims are false!I have since canceled my prime membership and will find an alternative company to order from. They are just getting to Big for there Pants!",8.0,111,0.8125601796311221,0.18743982036887785,40.6170835591057,Low Trust
Dr. Vieth,GB,1.0,"Despite advertising an ink cartridge from ubinki with 24 months guarantee in case of defect, there is no way to get in touch with the seller. Amazon claims there is, when in fact there is not - neither via their website, which keeps looping me into the Amazon chat bot, nor the actual email address I finally found on the box. After multiple chats, and over one hour on the phone with supposedly the highest supervisor in the customer service department, they tell me there is nothing they can do. The last person I spoke to is named Zahid. I know Amazon with better service - a disgrace!!!",5.0,108,0.8125189536045788,0.18748104639542118,40.58549371068525,Low Trust
Ai,GB,1.0,"I ordered something from amazon two days ago. As I'm with prime I got my order last night. The parcel turned up on time no damage but the delivery driver was abusive. He rang my door bell and he was still there when I answered the door and he just starting hollering at me from his van  and blaring his horn until I picked up my parcel, what I didnt know is that another parcel ( a present from a family member) was underneath in my name and he started blaring his horn even more until I noticed it and picked it up. It was pitch dark outside!  He kept shouting at me if it was mine and i said yes, I was polite the whole time even though he was being down right abusive for no reason. I have severe anxiety and hate confronting people but that made me on edge all night. Ive never had this happen to me before and i did not do anything to make this driver angry with me! I'm not ever ordering from amazon again so will be cancelling my prime account!",18.0,189,0.8124799690597666,0.1875200309402334,41.4960239811115,Low Trust
wurth51,US,5.0,"I have had my ups and downs with Amazon but most of the problems were with their 3rd party sellers. Amazon itself has stood behind every product and if it was incorrectly shipped or damaged they have gone above the norm to resolve any problems.  I know I can place and order, get in a reasonable time frame and best of all, I can return it - without ever having to get in my car.  Love it!!!",2.0,77,0.8121857649966242,0.1878142350033758,160.25442459369094,High Trust
Tami VanSickle,US,1.0,"Our account was frozen because we cancelled payment on items we thought fraudulent. After reviewing further, discovered that the purchases were valid just itemized. We contacted customer service to reopen our account and pay the items, but have gotten lost in a cycle of call customer service, wait for a specialist to call in 24-48 hours. No call. Call customer service, wait for a specialist to call in 24-48 hours. Have done it 3 times now....no call. Received an email asking for account verification and another payment method. Filled it out, three times now. Nothing. Latest email states that our amazon music will be cancelled if we don’t update our payment method within 3 days. Can’t update the payment info because the account states it locked when I try to login. Worst customer service ever!!!!",1.0,135,0.8121553650186537,0.1878446349813463,40.90653348771005,Low Trust
Anne Upshall,GB,1.0,Would have selected no stars but it wouldn’t let me. Terrible terrible service. I’m a prime customer and frequent buyer. Usually have deliveries to my home but needed something urgently for my dog and wanted to make sure I didn’t miss the delivery. Selected the closest Amazon locker to my home address. Received notifications it was delivered while I was out and felt thankful as would have missed it. Drove to locker location as soon as I could but there was no lockers. Just a big space and marks on the floor/wall as evidence that lockers were there once but not anymore. Security staff at the location confirmed that it didn’t exist anymore.  Trouble is tracking said it was delivered and I had been sent a barcode and draw number for it!!! Customer services couldn’t have been worse. Arguing with me that the item was there for collection and that I needed to collect it. I was passed through 6 agents. All bots I’m assuming as not answering my questions and repeating. Worst experience ever. Eventually spoke to a human who confirmed the lockers didn’t exist as were permanently closed but couldn’t explain why it was and still is an option for delivery on their site. The human told me I would have to wait a further 4 days for a refund and that was it. Cold hearted response. Could not give a toss that I needed the item today and I was so disappointed or that I had been around the houses trying to get one of the bots to help. Horrendous,3.0,263,0.8116505559516879,0.1883494440483121,42.36755633028997,Low Trust
its_ fitzer,IE,1.0,I ordered some lights and it has taken exactly 2 weeks to get LIGHTS!!!. I could of just went to a local hardware store and bought it but no this covid - 19 has to ruin it all I bet you amazon are making twice the amount of money they usually do.,1.0,52,0.811612794986282,0.18838720501371797,40.002646846311244,Low Trust
Truth,GB,1.0,"After being a Prime member since onset I cannot understand why the deliveries are now so bad it is laughable ... I have clear and concise delivery instructions, I have a notice on my door to re-iterate this yet time and time again they leave on my items on the door step where they are going missing or down the side of my building or at the back in the pouring rain - damaging the items.. I have contacted Amazon time and time again and still nothing is changing - there is simply 9 times out of 10 no care and it is not only inconveniencing me but must be costing Amazon a fortune and all because the delivery drivers do not follow instructions with regards to deliveries You can't even speak to someone in the UK to discuss it and when you do speak to someone they just read the script that the automated chat gives youWake up Amazon - sort your drivers out !!!",39.0,166,0.8115296499046422,0.18847035009535784,41.28554779080266,Low Trust
Kristina,GB,1.0,"Do not trust anyone working in this company…Delivery guys are doggy, stealing expensive items from your parcels and then once you try to report a problem, there is no one to help you…They all just trying to cover each others backs….you will be left without nothing!!!",8.0,46,0.811225784715386,0.18877421528461402,39.95469506036082,Low Trust
