Baz,GB,1.0,"So I received an unsolicited parcel to my address with a name on it not associated with my address or my account but with my correct address, hence it came to me. Try and get that over to their customers service reps.. The first rep seemed quite competent and said it would be investigated internally and to dispose or keep the items.I then get a generic email from customer services basically saying it was a gift and they would let the sender know my appreciation.WHAT!!! So I get back to online chat again trying to explain it was not a gift but probably a scam sometimes known as 'Brushing' from a fake account. I do not want it, nerver ordered it and certainly do not want you to give them my appreciation.  I then get given  a page to report an unwanted parcel with options to tick but as usual the option I want is not there. So I've now deleted my account as I cannot trust Amazon's security or being able to report suspicious activity.",19.0,176,0.7980144483046661,0.20198555169533394,42.07347836996019,Low Trust
Robert White,US,1.0,"I ordered items that stated a SPECIFIC delivery date and after the order, the delivery dates change.  I contacted customer service and they state that they are ESTIMATED dates.  It doesn’t say ANYTHING about estimated delivery.  It states if you order before “x” time, it will be delivered on a specific date.  I have been disconnected with customer service TWICE.  I’m sick and tired of the lack of accountability on Amazon’s part.  They deliver to the wrong address, deliver when they want, in spite of what their website states, their drivers will drive by your house multiple times before they actually deliver your package, their drivers park in the middle of the street and organize their trucks(police on my street have confronted the drivers multiple times), the drivers are on their phones while driving and delivering (which is disrespectful to the customer who is outside waiting for their package), the drivers blast their music as if they were teenagers trying to impress their peers. Amazon needs to get their vendors and drivers under control and build a professional image and take time to care about their customers.   Prime members do not receive prime benefits!!!!",1.0,194,0.7980039647608348,0.2019960352391652,42.27590944563745,Low Trust
Upset,US,1.0,"Twice in the last 6 months I never received my orders but they say delivered. Try to contact them but all I get is computer assistance! Computer assistance is NOT customer service.  Now, I have to wait up to 2 weeks to get my refund. I have cancelled my Prime membership because this company is not worth my money!!",1.0,59,0.7979246385730129,0.20207536142698712,40.765574016385806,Low Trust
Terri Hills,GB,1.0,"Fed-up with amazon. Every time you get a problem, you can NEVER, EVER email them. All you get is links that don't work - and when you think you've found an email address, it comes bouncing back with an auto-reply.How do they keep any customers at all??I am a PRIME customer and still can't find any way to communicate with these people. Sick of trying to talk to them on live-chat as well, because you have to go through the same saga over and over again. No cares at amazon.",148.0,90,0.7971233963647468,0.20287660363525317,41.15336467419115,Low Trust
Lizzie Wharton,GB,1.0,Waited for delivery then I was the next stop. I waited outside my apartment block to save them time. Then got a message to say unsuccessful delivery. Rang to complain they said driver said you were closed! Huh? It’s an apartment block. Just an excuse. Asked to complain they said oh we will but we can’t tell you the outcome but rest assured. I said I’m not rest assured I’m skeptical you will look into it if you can’t tell me why they didn’t stop. Muppets!! Service has really gone down.,3.0,91,0.7965438577742905,0.2034561422257095,41.193558653629836,Low Trust
Natalie Simpson,US,1.0,"I return items still get charged for them, this has happened more than once but other items in the SAME BOX getting returned I get $ back for?! Also I don't recommend prime before you try because I'm now 2 items out (not cheap items) I shouldn't be charged for something if it's returned!!! Nothing makes me more angry because I think we'll I should have kept the stupid thing at least I'd have something to show and you can write reviews but they don't accept them because they're not within their guidelines....please of course screwing people over are not within your guidelines",1.0,103,0.7964593311258107,0.2035406688741893,41.3323895850443,Low Trust
Nikki Walker,GB,1.0,"Abysmal customer service,called to rearrange a delivery of an item i have to receive and age verify and to ask if the courier could come earlier as im not in by 8pm to be told my account could not be verified and my address was wrong even though i order from amazon a lot and have for years!my billing address for that order came up as my daughters address for some reason but he still would not accept that address either!i offered to give him my card details,my dob and he had my email address but still he kept telling me my address is wrong and could not verify my account i told him i could tell him what i had ordered in the past 6 months and any other addresses i had sent things to because i know he was on my account,i asked to speak to somebody else and he refused to put me through to his manager or supervisor, it resulted with me hanging up on him and cancelling my order...disgusting customer service!",4.0,176,0.7962130330315526,0.20378696696844745,42.16354913361586,Low Trust
MRS.,DK,1.0,"Amazon keeps getting worse and worse! I’ve contacted them 11 times (only counting in the mails contacts) now regarding the same issue. I have items continuously claiming to be ‘on their way’ but nothing happens. No one is helping me getting a return or merely calling me. I just keep writing and writing! It’s turning into a scam company, holding your money, but no delivery of any packages.",81.0,68,0.7953370511557593,0.20466294884424074,40.99590683649134,Low Trust
Karlie Huff,US,1.0,"I recently ordered an electronic and a few other items from Amazon for Christmas presents.  When I hadn’t received any info regarding the purchase, I tried to look into it from my account.  I was locked out of my Amazon account for no apparent reason.  Despite having numerous security codes sent to my phone and email account, I couldn’t get passed the added security question, which I could not answer.  The security question was asking the expiration date on an old debit card that they had on file.  Not the last card I used, but one that was on file.  It was a card that I had canceled due to fraud almost a year ago.  I called customer service and told them that I just wanted to see about my most recent purchase.  I told them the credit card I used, , as well as the items purchased. All of this was to no avail.  The customer service rep would not unlock my account and she told me my order had been canceled.  She told me the credit card company canceled my order.  After a long wait on hold with the credit card company, I was told they had not declined my purchase, nor do they cancel people’s  orders.   I ended up ordering the electronic directly from Apple, which is what I should have done in the first place.  Low and behold, a few days later, I received a text that my amazon order was on the way!  Ugh!  Now I will have the headache of having to send it back when it arrives!  I’m so done with Amazon!",1.0,269,0.794948582848858,0.20505141715114195,43.2699572849267,Low Trust
Asif,CA,1.0,"Amazon non accountabilityAmazon, has been jerking me around for over three months. They don't hv phone support . I hv been waiting for 8 orders Never delivered. Charged me and they are not letting me post about it. There is no way to contact them about. I am thinking they are involve in this spamming and Fraud. There is no accountability for this company. Conversely, Amazon is destroying a lot businesses especially now. Shop anywhere but Amazon!!!",2.0,77,0.7949193056781727,0.2050806943218273,41.11774755961351,Low Trust
Julie Jones,US,1.0,"Over one hour on the ph, item caused damage and is unsafe.  First, I was told I'll get a $5 refund for $21 something item,  I didn't agree, she then said I'll get a full amount refund.   Then she says she can't allow it even after first manager approved,  she transferred me to a specialist.  Specialist Tells me absolutely no refund, I spoke to her manager, still no result.   Wants me to purchase a box and return the item.  Result; canceled prime membership,  I purchase a lot from Amazon, didn't appreciate the last manager's sarcasm,  saying I can't give you a refund on your time & I'm sorry they told you different information but can't help you.   I think I know that, but the inconvenience.  Left with a crappy item, that caused damage I have to pay for, and prime membership canceled.   Well done Amazon!!!  Let's not forget my other item is missing and no refund too 👏👏✌",1.0,158,0.7945901530308388,0.2054098469691612,42.04278623516585,Low Trust
customer,US,2.0,"As of today, I would rate Amazon a zero. I ordered a few items a few weeks ago and patiently waited for the packages to arrive. On the expected delivery day I discovered the driver delivered the packages to the wrong apartment!    I received the refund for the two less expensive items but I am still pending the refund on the two more expensive items. The customer service representative stated I should be refunded within 3 to 5 days. When that didn’t happen I called again and was once again given the same information.    I reached out again after one week only to be told by a third representative the refund was never initiated! The level of incompetence is ridiculous!",2.0,120,0.7943278829715898,0.20567211702841015,71.62965184132516,Medium Trust
