Kurush Sanjana,US,1.0,"Amazon is one of the biggest cheaters when it comes to giving monthly deals on items with Amazon Prime Credit Card through Chase. It states it will charge you monthly payments but instead charges the entire amount, how is that a benefit to the consumer? Stay away from them! Since they have grown they think they can cheat American consumers & get away with it. They have gotten worst by the day, its time to boycott Amazon!!",1.0,77,0.7889932910315486,0.21100670896845142,41.414048291944724,Low Trust
Alex T.,IT,1.0,"I have been a customer of Amazon for at least five years if not more. I bought dozens of items from these gentlemen for a few thousand euros in value. On March 3, 2023, I bought an inexpensive screwdriver drill (Amazon order number # 402-7269180-7579518) worth 54.99 euros (cheap). After a few days of use, one of the two rechargeable batteries stopped working. After having obtained the guarantee in chat from an Amazon operator that I could return an already used item, I requested and obtained the return, sending the item on June 6, 2023, even if the item only reached Amazon on June 19. On June 23 I receive the following email from Amazon:""Good morning,We are contacting you to inform you that we have processed your recent return of the article TEENO Cordless Screwdriver 21V, 2 Speed ​​Cordless Drill, 2 Lithium Batteries 1.5Ah, Fast Charge in 1 Hour, 20 Accessories Included (Drill an in the order n. 402-7269180-7579518.The item was returned in a condition that does not comply with our return policies. On this occasion, we have processed a refund for the order. However, if your returns continue to violate our policies, we may not issue further refunds or we may apply returns condition fees.To review our return policies, please see the About Our Returns Policy page:We will inform you if similar cases occur in the future.Account SpecialistAmazon. it""Aside from the semi-intimidating tone of the email, the email came to me with no reason why my returned item violated Amazon policies. The signature of whoever wrote the message is also missing and it doesn't seem correct to me. Perhaps it would be too much to ask for two specific words in the message?! And maybe even accompanying photos?! Why Amazon allows certain tones with its customers?! And why doesn't he document his motivations?Years and years of even very expensive purchases and now they send me threatening messages! What a disappointment...",14.0,321,0.7888660919875579,0.21113390801244214,44.15736842361706,Low Trust
Veronica Quinn,GB,1.0,"Oh Boy is this company dreadful.  Like so many reviews on here.. I ordered 3 items, one was a tablet.  In short I have waited 3 full days ( in the house as I needed to provide the delivery man with a code). Item was a no show.I too got the dreadful automated chat and requested several call backs, all very scripted could not tell me if my item had been despatched or window of delivery - shocking and then insulted me by offering £5 compensation !!!.  In short i have not received the tablet and was very disappointed in the generic email response .  I am now waiting on a refund for the tablet and also sending the remainder of the order back (keyboard and stylus pen), as they are no longer required.",2.0,134,0.7887717874654077,0.21122821253459234,42.064495315456476,Low Trust
Monera Ellsworth,US,4.0,"Love their prime features! I got a free trial and it was great! I'll consider getting it for good once I have more funds. My orders were all good quality but like other sites can depend on the seller and how reputable they are. Everything marked prime came in the 2 day window and was good quality. Some super cheap but more iffy from China sites seem like a scam but the products did come as described within a month, but took a while to get here! Give it a solid month for those type. For those in the US, give it a week or so for standard shipping... Overall positive experience with Amazon and will shop there again.",3.0,119,0.7885173541827051,0.21148264581729492,131.90896123085352,High Trust
Bobbie Dickie,GB,5.0,Amazon is amazing! I use Prime which has saved me significant postal charges. Information provided about the merchandise is good and Amazon keeps me informed about progress of my orders. I have never had a problem in the years that I have used Amazon. And prices on the site are keen.,79.0,51,0.7883352306272576,0.21166476937274237,161.1553080143466,High Trust
Alborz Parvizi,FR,5.0,"I buy 90% of my purchases online, and most of them are from Amazon.Love this company! they have almost everything and the customer service is the best. for anything you buy you have a month to try, even if you use it you can always send it back, the guarantee covers all the problems and if they can't fix it they give you a new one or refund you completely.I bought a beats headphone after two years the sound was not clear, Amazon took it back and gave me a new one, quickly!I currently order more than 250 items per year and never have been happier.Support this company to the end! need more companies like this in this world.",3.0,119,0.7879029688293318,0.21209703117066825,161.9396804985222,High Trust
Suzanne,GB,1.0,"Can I go lower than a 1 star rating? Absolutely appalling customer service from Amazon. Put through to the Philippines where they cant help you at all. Basically as a business we wanted to sell on Amazon. They have all my personal data, bank account, credit card details, bank statements, companies house information BUT I cant sell on the site and nobody can figure out why not! worse than useless. Now I have no idea where my personal data is stored and how it will be destroyed! 1 Dept after another and still no further forward. Poor poor poor!",3.0,99,0.7874306224786778,0.2125693775213222,41.738956817737446,Low Trust
Dani Ya,US,5.0,"Whether you're hanging on the coattails of someone else's Prime or using your own 30-day trial, Amazon is pretty awesome. I like that I can return things I impulsively bought and get refunded for it. Also, I love that I know what my friends are getting for me on my birthday and Christmas. Honestly, Amazon has also fed my addiction to books that I buy to look smart and not read (although I don't think it makes me look smart when all I buy are repeat volumes of Captain Underpants, but a copy of The Art of War balances it out I think). I'm currently waiting for a portable guitar. And before you say it, I know, all guitars are portable, but it's the one with like three frets and six-strings and you sort of just bring it around everywhere. Trust me, it's kind of cool. A lot of the things I've gotten from Amazon have been good. No complaints really. ALTHOUGH, the recent purchases I have (baring the portable guitar) been sad face qualities, so I returned it. And guess what? It was so easy! In any case, I think I have used Amazon to encourage my ""don't talk to people and stay in the darkness of your room"" ways. To be honest, I'm on my way to becoming a hermit and Amazon makes it possible. Thank you, Amazon! Cheers!",7.0,231,0.7870442617854054,0.21295573821459457,163.23892544129617,High Trust
Rob Leroy,US,1.0,"Don't like that they try to sneak in ways to get you to subscribe to Amazon prime,  Super annoying. Just let me order without that nonsense",156.0,26,0.787016131157181,0.21298386884281895,40.940836739953625,Low Trust
Al C,US,1.0,"Amazon is the worst company!  I order a bunch of items, they input the wrong code so my credit card declines. I chat with Amazon explaining all this and ask them to resend it, they agree.  Two days later my account gets flagged for unauthorized use and my orders are cancelled.  I immediately cancelled my Amazon accounts!  STAY AWAY, use Walmart instead!",2.0,62,0.7869079408910347,0.21309205910896534,41.350060050232344,Low Trust
Alan Bromyard,GB,1.0,"I was’t happy with the having to return a whole product when it was just one thing missing. I clink a like to ‘make a complaint’ and that takes you to a page that says ‘page doesn’t exist’ Called and got through to someone, she couldn’t help and put me through to someone. They said they are in Audible and cannot help. They put me through to someone who says Amazon doesn’t have a complaints department?! As a protested that I can’t believe they don’t have a complaints department and I was giving him my email address - he says the line is cutting out and cant hear me?! Come on!",1.0,111,0.7863606734416402,0.21363932655835982,41.9270588685798,Low Trust
H. Y.,US,1.0,"They keep promoting Amazon gift cards everywhere so I chose Amazon GC and I redeemed for $400 shopping cart. The Amazon instead of taking the redemption, charged to my credit card on file.I called them they said “Sorry”!!I told them that’s not enough, I need the charges to be reversed and instead redeem from my available GC since this was a mistake on your side. They said we can’t do that! Sorry The supervisor was a negative person and didn’t help and didn’t give me any option. First they accepted it was their system issue then they denied completely. I closed my Chase Amazon Prime credit card and from now I will minimize my use of Amazon to absolute minimum. Their prices are usually higher anyway and now this is their service.",1.0,132,0.785759264501466,0.21424073549853395,42.19268736382182,Low Trust
Sirin Arkhon,HU,1.0,"This was my complain I have send them: So. I have ordered a backpack early December, and it was said it will arrive around the 2nd or 3rd week of December. It would have been a Christmas gift, and you guys were really sure it will arrive, with all that advertising, spam emails and everything. ""Order up and you get your stuff before Christmas!"" So I did, waaaaay before the last chance to do this.Then I got an automatic email to rate my order, when it should have been arrived. But it did not. And I checked it, and it said, ""sorry, but Amazon is too busy in this season, you will get your stuff around 2-3 of January.""I was mad at first.Contacted the seller, who said, it's Amazon's fault, I should talk to them. Ok....So I have started to chat with the customer service. I talked to 5 different people. Or as I thought, but then I have realized they were AIs. Fkin AIs, who were not able to understand my problem, so they passed me to the next AI. Maybe the last one was a real person. I can't be sure at this point, because they all said the same lines over and over again.STOP USING Artificial Intelligence in customer service! It took tons of my time trying to tell what's my problem, and we didn't get any solution.At the end, since they didn't understand, I dropped it, and let it go. If it arrives in january, then it arrives in january, who cares anymore.But.I got an email today, when it should have arrived, Amazon said they will refund my order, because they couldn't deliver it.And why is that? NOBODY called the address, but that's why I GAVE THE PHONE NUMBER! Delivery companies ALWAYS calls or messages! ALWAYS, from whomewer I order from.ALWAYS.But I guess nobody were by the address, trying to deliver anything, so they were just stealing my money and time.Thanks for this roller coaster, I'm done with Amazon and will make sure to tell everybody that don't order from Amazon.Because delivering and customer service both sucks.I can just hope they will really send my money back at this point.",1.0,364,0.7854601677434276,0.21453983225657236,44.80999778220607,Low Trust
marcus gordon,GB,1.0,"I had been charged for both Student Prime and Prime, even though I had paid for Student Prime and their customer service team said they'd charge me £47.51 to upgrade my Student Prime to Prime, which would have been fine if that's what they actually did.Instead, they charged me the full amount for both Student Prime and Prime, and because they wrongly did that, I now don't have enough money in my bank account to pay the bill due today (30/08/2023). A situation that only exists because Amazon made a mistake, stealing money they weren't meant to take.I've now spent over two hours trying to get Amazon's customer service team tto pay attention to what I'm complaining about. Their third and sixth customer service person I was escalated to didn't even pretend to care about trying to solve the problem and ended the live chat without my consent.I tried to log three formal complaints, but they wouldn't log them or give me complaint reference numbersFormal complaint 1Stealing money out of my account they weren't entitled to and not returning that money in time to pay the bill it was in my account to pay for, affecting my credit rating and making it the first bill I've not been able to pay in 41 years of being alive.Formal complaint 2Their escalation team hanging up on me twice without bothering to try to solve the problem and without allowing me to log a formal complaint like I had requested.Formal complaint 3The sheer amount of my time and effort you've made me waste on the matter. Time I won't get backIt's a simple request. They took money they had no right to take and I need that mine returned today (30/08/2023) to pay for the bill it was in my account to pay. That was asking too much of a thief, apparently",157.0,309,0.7851130304098584,0.21488696959014164,44.210416903511565,Low Trust
