J Hawk,US,1.0,"I have been an Amazon Prime member for over 10 years.  I understand there may be a delay in shipping for some items, but when an item has left their facility that is 30 minutes from my house at 5:20 am, it should be to my house by the guaranteed delivery time of 9 pm.  I just spoke to Jeremy, who is apparently a manager or supervisor living in South Africa, and was told that the delay was due to COVID and he did not know where my package was.  He did tell me that it could be at the post office, or possibly even on the side of the road, he just didn't know!  What a joke!  Why do we pay for Prime when the guaranteed delivery time is not guaranteed and all customer service can say is that they are sorry, they don't know where the package is, there is nothing they can do, and the delay is definitely COVID related!",1.0,163,0.7785205745000631,0.22147942549993693,42.902350411284004,Low Trust
