Kalia Lor,US,2.0,"I was notified with a photo that my package was delivered into my apartment complex’s package concierge. When I got there, no locker was ready under my name and I had to ask the office manager to manually open the locker (the locker in which the Amazon driver had taken a photo of). The product ended up being for someone else within the complex. So, I called Amazon customer service.. and I was told my product was not “lost” and the neighbor with my package may return my package. Well, here’s the problem.. the reason we got a package concierge in the first place was due to package theft that was going around. The rep said he didn’t know what else he could do for me. First of all, he didn’t do anything; he basically said to wait on my neighbors to.. NO, it’s Amazon’s responsibility to make sure I receive my package, not my neighbors! If I don’t receive it and you can’t track it, then it is LOST. When I asked about the purpose of paying for Prime Membership just to get terrible quality and crappy service, he asked if I’ve ever had a problem with Amazon delivery. YES, MANY ACTUALLY! Why mark a product delivered if not delivered?!Gave a two star for the rep who gave me a discount.",2.0,222,0.7589812505794866,0.24101874942051338,74.54112255234928,Medium Trust
Clarky,FR,1.0,"Ordered a cpu for sons Christmas present and when it arrived it was an empty box!!. I was told I needed a crime number to get refunded of witch I got for them, for them to say its invalid.Expensive item stolen!!.I would give them a 0 star if I could, the customer service is atrocious, unhelpful and rude.I would advise people to be very wary of ordering things from amazon as if you take a look online we are not the only people to be ripped off, there are thousands and thousands daily with similar situations as ours.How they are getting away with taking people's money in this day and age is shocking.",2.0,113,0.7587523793566727,0.24124762064332728,43.329907672659914,Low Trust
Amanda Seeboeck,US,1.0,"I have been an amazon prime member for yrs, Fraudulent charges were made on my Amazon account at the end of April, so because I disputed the charges Amazon locked me out of my prime account,(to be expected), except they didn't stop there, no they decided to rob me of my thousands of dollars in movie and music purchases, and all of my Amazon devices when they also deemed it appropriate to lock me out of my prime movie and music accounts, not to mention none of my Amazon Alexas and echos will work due to all being registered to my account that had fraudulent activity... So then I called Amazon and confirmed I did not make those purchases dozens of times and here we are 4-5 months later and I'm still locked out of all my stuff and services that have already been bought and paid for??? Which is weird, I have never had the clerk from the grocery store come into my house and take all the food I just bought from my fridge, freezer, and pantry.... I have never had the manager of kohls show up at my house and confiscate the school clothes I just bought for my children.... I am not sure why Amazon thinks it is acceptable to remove access to movies and music that have already been PAID for... Or how they think it is appropriate to block the functionality of my devices that have already been PAID for with the understanding they would FUNCTION!!! I am beyond disgusted with treatment and handling of this whole situation.... I'm honestly not even sure it's legal.... It seems alot like theft to me... I honestly don't ever want to purchase anything from Amazon ever again after this and neither do family and friends... a full refund for ALL of my movies, music, and devices would be appreciated",1.0,312,0.7585531024151192,0.2414468975848808,45.572064452996145,Low Trust
