J Helfrich,US,1.0,"Trying to locate a Customer Service phone number on Amazon’s website is obviously an intentional roadblock constructed by Amazon.  When I finally uncovered a number, I was talking with someone, “Raheem”, in the third world, whose English was barely understandable.  Raheem gave incorrect information upon which I relied saying unauthorized charges would be reversed without cancellation to my wife’s Prime account.  Later, contrary to Raheem’s assurances, we discovered her Prime account had been cancelled.  Totally bad experience!  When I later, again, called Amazon Customer Service, I was informed that the incorrect Amex credit card had been used for two years to pay for Prime - disgusted now with Amazon!   Moreover, after 5 years of Prime membership, I am throughly done! I have NO confidence in the company’s competence and/or it’s integrity.",3.0,131,0.7455687860647161,0.2544312139352839,44.19099423574344,Low Trust
Pawel,GB,1.0,"Used to love Amazon and spent thousands with them - not any more! Time to support local shops again! Amazon has a habit of overpricing, was looking for a graphics card to finish my computer - had no choice but to pay almost £200 more than retail value (item sold and dispatched by Amazon) I get it , these are hard to get at the moment but it's still a cheeky move! Especially when other smaller retailers stick to suggested pricing. On top of that their drivers think it's ok to leave parcels in the communal areas and don't bother to come upstairs. Amazon also don't like negative product/service reviews and refuse to publish them on their website. Amazon you have become a real stinker and I'm not going near you again. Cheers - awaiting my prime membership refund.",11.0,139,0.7445146212780441,0.25548537872195587,44.33343887440402,Low Trust
Melanie C,CA,1.0,"Worst customer service experience! I placed an order on September 25th 2022 and one of the items was set to arrive only on October 11th. That day I looked up my order to obtain tracking information and noticed my order was cancelled, claiming that I refused delivery. I live by myself, work from home and there was no attempted delivery. I called Amazon and spoke to an agent who said she would follow up with me the next day. The one time I stepped away from my phone is when she called and missed the call. I called them back and spoke to another agent who said they are trained to return the call 30 minutes later, so instead of explaining my story again, I said I would just wait for her to call back. She never called back. I called Amazon again and spoke to a 3rd agent who put me on hold for 25 minutes and then the line dropped. She also never called back. I waited a couple days and still nothing. So this morning I told my story to a 4th agent and she tells me she is going to escalate this to management and couldn’t tell me much of anything. I told her my only request is that I do not want the same delivery company to be used for any future deliveries going forward and I will not be making any Amazon purchases going forward until that is confirmed. She then tells me the delivery company has to mess up at least 3 times for them to consider this. By this point I’m irate and I’m not interested in possibly going through this experience again a 2nd or 3rd time and request to escalate the call. This is where my experience gets even worse. The manager was completely uncaring, no empathy, unfriendly and expressed very little concern when I said that I would cancel my prime membership and close my account if my request wasn’t granted after all the hoops I had to jump with them. It was so triggering to me and I asked to speak with someone higher than him and he flat out said no. Did I curse and express how I felt about his “help”, yes. Should I have stayed calm? Yes but honestly I was just disappointed and upset by his lack of care and I disconnected the call. I immediately went on the chat customer service to report my experience and the agent right away was empathetic and kind and helpful and filled out a carrier deprioritization form. Why could a manager from the leadership team give me that same treatment?! And the kicker is that I received an email from that manager threatening to cancel my account because of MY Behaviour. UNREAL!",1.0,465,0.7444306153546332,0.2555693846453668,47.99439744314888,Low Trust
