Andrienne Vasquez,GB,1.0,"Amazon deliveries are either thrown over a ten foot fence , thrown in my kitchen window onto my cooker - whilst it’s on ! Clear instructions are on my account which are not followed . Recently a large parcel was wedged under my front door effectively locking me in ! I only have 1 door so had to climb out the window ! I have continued to raise complaints but they are ignored .",16.0,74,0.7377348737434213,0.2622651262565787,43.94331800660347,Low Trust
Guy Person,GB,1.0,"very dishonest and scummy company but always get away with it. The way they treat their workers, abysmal customer service which lie from the back of their teeth, the cons and scam-worthy products which you can’t return because Amazon protects sellers against criticism. And a personal experience where I bought a very expensive item, had to return it because Hermes Delivery service did what they always do… destroy your parcels… and so I had to send it back. But when I did, Amazon told me that Hermes (who had recollected it) had lost it during transit. Amazon refused to refund me for 3 weeks. But after implying I would take further action if I had to, they gave me a partial refund…….. Prime ALSO sucks because the guaranteed next day delivery isn’t always next day…. Just the “oops we’re running late! We’ll deliver you item tomorrow!”  … a dilemma of which could also repeat the day after.. The delivery drivers rarely knock and toss your parcel on the driveway and scoot off.  As for Amazon Fresh… isn’t even AVAILABLE for my area which sucks…and for Prime Video, you have to pay ADDITIONAL costs for other shows on top of Prime if they aren’t included… that is just ridiculous how is that considered acceptable!?? Needless to say I gave up on Amazon altogether.",16.0,222,0.7373239638282237,0.26267603617177626,45.62398688991243,Low Trust
Desirae “Rosincore” Baker,US,1.0,Phone case never got here talked with customer service the latest it would be here was the 25th I ordered it on the 19th and I have prime and still nothing. They need to get stuff together. If it was me on prime I'd quit it but it's my mom's account. I don't like being lied to by customer service !! USPS doesn't even deliver on christmas!!,1.0,67,0.7372841677767951,0.26271583222320494,43.88733395552368,Low Trust
Judy FISHER,US,5.0,"I've been with Amazon for several Years now, I must say I am seeing the Prices rising! I haven't ever had a real problem with Amazon.I will say I have talked with some Customer Service Rep.. Whom I can not Understand & I do try!Other than that,I must say They have always tried to help Me.I feel Even if They don't have Answers They will go & Get The answer from Someone higher Up.I don't like The cost Raising every Year However,I appreciate their service  & will continue To pay for the renewal !",1.0,94,0.7364371888397722,0.26356281116022784,164.23254325010336,High Trust
Dena Jenks,US,2.0,"Amazon customer service has gotten worse. Their drivers have, on several occasions, indicated that a package was delivered, even going so far as to take a picture, only to discover they lied about having made the delivery. I have gone through the very painful process of contacting them, only to get no resolution. The most recent incident began April 14, 2020. I ordered birthday gifts for my great grandson in Houston area, whose birthday was May 6, 2020. Amazon indicated the package (with picture) was delivered on April 17, 2020. I ordered birthday gifts early because I was unsure how fast deliveries could be made during Covid-19. Some items were delivered on 4/17/20, but my granddaughter just told me today that one large package didn't arrive until YESTERDAY, May 6th, on his actual birthday. I discovered this today when I called my granddaughter to ask how Jasai's 2nd birthday went and if he liked his gifts. That's when I was told the driver knocked on her door to give her the package.You might say, ""Well done! It arrived ON his birthday!"" However, as I have said to Amazon customer service, when the drivers lie about when packages are delivered, it could create a problem if the item was NEVER delivered. It has happened to me recently, with the USPS. Amazon indicated that the item was delivered and yet my friend in Chicago has yet to receive the item. Dealing with the postal service is just as infuriating as dealing with Amazon's customer service. Your package never arrives and your are out of the price of your purchases. Amazon seems to go out of their way to make it near impossible to get customer service. I'm writing here because when I attempted to chat with Amazon's customer service, I was switched to something called Just Answer. For the price of a dollar (which they claim is refunded) you then wait for the system to match you with a lawyer (yes, that's right, a lawyer!) who will then call you or email you the answer to your question.Has anyone any advice on how I can do an end run around the Amazon obstacle course. I've tried their chat, they no longer answer their phones, I'm at a loss.",7.0,376,0.7363664453826444,0.2636335546173556,77.3992884992357,High Trust
Mrs Ellis,CY,1.0,I can’t believe I have spoken to 5 customer services in relation to appalling service I have received from Amazon.What has happened to this company …????It has gone down big time…Shambles of a company … will think twice before I use Amazon again… it’s  a massive 👎😧 0/10 From me.,121.0,50,0.7353844881548027,0.26461551184519727,43.79162808805347,Low Trust
