Raul Butuc,GB,1.0,"As a Prime customer, I have been experiencing a very critical issue with a high-value order being misdelivered, without signature to a fake name (or at least not anyone in my building). I have spent over 20 hours talking to customer support, their managers and their managers' managers throughout the last 3 weeks. Every conversation is going in circles; their chain of communication is virtually non-existent; let's say their CS representative Mr. X doesn't know what their CS representative Mr. Y said, so you have to explain everything from the beginning every single time, even when being transferred! The best part is when you get conflicting responses from different customer service reps... (sarcasm intended) - such as: we have a delivery signature / we don't have a delivery signature - which then obviously takes extra time to figure out. Some of the managers even had the audacity to close the conversation after I caught them contradicting themselves!! Please stay away from this company. I will be taking legal action against them based on these events and they will pay for everything wrong they've done.",8.0,184,0.7297766204493006,0.2702233795506994,45.57510616205544,Low Trust
Ralph Cramdon,US,1.0,"Their customer service SUCKS!!! I cannot believe that it is so bad in today's day and age with the money they bring in. Also, they are always looking for new ways to charge you for things. If Amazon has to ""cry poverty"" I simply do not know what the world is coming to. I would suggest any alternative to buying anything from them. It seems I do not have a choice but to use them. I am looking for an alternative. When I find one I will pleasantly tell them to go ""go away"" themselves.",6.0,95,0.7296759510530765,0.2703240489469235,44.58182218935403,Low Trust
