Night Shade,GB,1.0,"I have been an Amazon customer for 10 years. I cannot believe how rude these people were to me today. I paid for Huyu subscription for £4.99 and it said Prime Video was included. I purchased this on the 28th of November. I have just been paid from work today then all of a sudden I was charged £7.99 then when I spoke to them to ask for a refund. A lady said she couldn't see the transaction I said you just charged me how can you not see it? She then transferred me to another incompetent person and he was saying he couldn't see it and how I should contact my bank to get the money back. I said instead of that I can take a picture that the money has been taken he ignored me and kept asking the same questions and repeating himself. Then I asked to speak to his manager he said I have a supervisor I said to him did you just hear what I said I said? MANAGER. He replied well we class a supervisor the same as a manager. The supervisor was beyond rude to the point I never want to buy anything on Amazon again for anything. He said that in the past we have made exceptions for you and that how I have accidentally purchased Amazon Prime when I checked out of paying for an item. I thought you cheeky idiot. I told him I already paid for Prime Video so why am I being charged again? How can I accidentally purchase something? These people must have thought I was stupid. I am so disgusted with the lies and disrespect of these people. The supervisor was saying he will make an exception and refund Huyu and Amazon Prime but in the future, we will not refund you if this happens again. I said to him as far as I'm concerned don't go on like you guys are holier than thou since you want to bring up the past things I bought on Amazon once in 2015 you charged me £79.99 without my authorization so don't even go there. I said to him you weren't there when I was refunded Amazon Prime in the past so don't go on like it was my fault. I am so done with Amazon and they don't deserve me as a customer. I will be buying from eBay as someone else said their customer services are much nicer. I have never had this problem with their team. Adios Amazon you're not worth it. I will never waste my hard earned money on there again!!!",20.0,438,0.7296033895224368,0.27039661047756325,48.43289838703016,Low Trust
Alex P,GB,1.0,"I ordered an electrical item (for over £300). When the courier arrived it was a completely different item (garden shed). Amazon wouldn’t sort the error just told me to cancel and reorder. Went to reorder and the price had gone up £20 (scam much?!) Amazon offered to compensate, but the compensation wasn’t eligible for use on the item ordered! I reordered as requested and the courier has now failed to deliver two days in a row citing “technical errors”. I tried speaking to them on live chat and each time their staff say they can’t help and tell you to contact the courier, then they close the chat without warning. Now I am over £300 out of pocket, haven’t received the item and they are refusing to cancel or refund. Thank God I bought on credit card and can cancel the payment with my bank! Avoid Amazon at all costs.",2.0,150,0.7290886502206386,0.2709113497793614,45.22812497634889,Low Trust
Mark Price,GB,1.0,"Where do I start, Amazon, I buy hundreds of items off Amazon as a buyer for the company I work for and usually they are okish. However lately they have become a nightmare! I could run you through the brash emails the hanging up of the phone or the weird decisions they seem to be making but whats the point you will all have your own versions of that to relate to. What I will say is that Amazon has become so big the tail is wagging the dog! Items dont arrive, refunds dont arrive, returns do arrive but then are deemed to be wrong by Amazon so further charges are applied to accounts. Do yourself a favour and shop about, there are better and even cheaper options out there its a little more work but when you get to the point of spending thousands a year Amazon should be your last choice not your first!",7.0,156,0.7286809705189841,0.27131902948101594,45.31581126092685,Low Trust
Deborah Wardle,GB,1.0,"Beware of amazon a-z guarantee!!!Amazon has unscrupulous sellers on and does not protect buyer. Recently purchased items unfit for use asked to return, told full refund and no need to return. Then refund cancelled now I am£50 out of pocket and a-z guarantee says not entitled to anything.",1.0,48,0.7285035745012175,0.2714964254987825,44.11323967090098,Low Trust
Rebecca Collins,GE,1.0,"They have had ""technical difficulties"" with their chat seemingly forever - every time I try to chat, not just today. I need to communicate with them about the items I ordered and cannot. I cannot call as am in another country. And when I click on the item I ordered it says ""cannot deliver to your location"", yet when I ordered it, it did say it can be delivered to my location. They need to fix all of this!!!",1.0,79,0.7283707528223701,0.27162924717762993,44.467609302235395,Low Trust
Alan,GB,1.0,"I have been a customer with Amazon UK since 2005 and just recently I purchased Car/Van Tyre Vulcanising Cement from an Amazon seller (Ma-Man) but what I received was bicycle puncture repair glue which believe me isn't the same thing!  I questioned this with Amazon Customer Services and wrote a Negative Review for the product and the same in the Sellers Feedback.  I later accidentally received an email from Amazon which was obviously intended for the seller (Ma-Man),... ""I've read the review and I understand your concerns......""  both of my reviews were subsequently removed and my account has since been closed! Amazon obviously care more about protecting their sellers than they do their customers.  Don't be fooled, all they want is your money!",9.0,123,0.7281654721175336,0.2718345278824664,44.97142353377559,Low Trust
Stephanie Stanhope,US,1.0,I made an order was billed by Amazon on March 12th. I was to receive the item by March 17th to March 20th! I have yet to this date not received the item nor my refund I asked for many times. I was told by Amazon if I disputed the charge my account would be locked yet I can't seem to get my money back from them! This is the excuse... it's a third party seller so I have to wait 2 days here 2 days there ... I've now waited the 48 hours and still can't get my money back. Amazon is a joke. I will dispute and don't care about there account!,2.0,114,0.7280007640718242,0.27199923592817576,44.87870548681821,Low Trust
Alzbeta Homolkova,US,1.0,"I got onto chat to ask a simple question. Why have my groceries been delivered to the lobby instead  of my door recently (can we change it back to my door?) and is it possible to use less bags (since they're always half empty?  Simple right? Nope. First live agent answer I got was ""Sorry for the inconvenience. We can offer you a $5 promo."" ...Uhh but what about my questions? I couldn't get an answer! Just kept getting copy and paste information about how deliveries work. I had to ask if they were really a live agent because it was like they weren't reading anything I wrote. And then he just left the chat. Just like that and I got another guy. Same deal. I finally got kind of an answer but it was like pulling teeth. I was still talking to him when HE just left.  Then I got a girl and I told her that my question is answered but I am very frustrated with the customer service and just wanted to express that, to which she replied by asking if I can help her with the order #. If she read it she would know it's not about the order anymore!! lol ...she could've just said ""Hey, I'm sorry for the bad experience. I will note your feedback"" and I would have been good with that but nope, once again it was like she didn't even read my message. I got off the  chat and was so frustrated I could cry ...and it all could've been solved in like 2 min if the first guy would've said:  ""Yes, we're sorry about that. The driver must have gotten it wrong. To ensure this won't happen again, you can write this down in your delivery instructions so they don't miss it again."" . I'm still not even sure if that applies for the bags question but I was pretty done by the end.",3.0,325,0.7277767300217676,0.27222326997823243,47.25670472157007,Low Trust
Julie,GB,1.0,"I purchased 6 items 5 of which were next day delivery for prime members. I specifically chose the items because they were next day. Did they honour their promise and deliver them? No, they have said they will deliver 4 days late on 9/3/23. I am finding this more and more, Amazon’s service is going down and down, The reason I usually buy almost everything but food on Amazon is because they deliver the next day so it’s not worth going to the shop but they rarely deliver next day these days. It’s false advertising. I am not impressed and when you ring amazon, despite the billions they earn in profits, they still go for cheap foreign labour for customer services, you can barely understand what they say because of their accents. 👎👎👎 Rubbish!!",111.0,134,0.7268572102679401,0.27314278973205985,45.16022417532986,Low Trust
Michele,US,1.0,"I ordered a keepsake box for a gift for Christmas, needing it by 12/19/19. Promised delivery by Amazon Prime was 12/18. I got a message at 6:00 tonight that it won't arrive today, but on 12/21/19. When I contacted customer service after 45 minutes, they kept saying sorry, but nothing they can do, it would arrive between 12/19 and 12/21. I explained that it would be too late. They said they can refund my money for the purchase since it won't arrive in time. Thinking this was their customer service offer, I accepted that resolution, thinking it was still going to be delivered at some point. I went into my orders to check on another item, and I saw they cancelled that order!! When I went back to customer service to find out about it, they said I asked to cancel the order and there is nothing they can do. Now, it can't even be reversed and I would have to start al over. This company has gone way down hill and do not care anymore about keeping customers.  Prime isn't worth it AT ALL!  The customer service reps are rude and keep passing you off on someone else.",1.0,199,0.7265443326875936,0.27345566731240645,45.90497629887887,Low Trust
Richard Magnuson,US,1.0,"Amazon has the worst CEO on earth.  I used to buy from Amazon weekly.  NO MORE!!! CEO Bezos and employees of Amazon have given millions of dollars to Democrats.  Led by Bezos, he and company employees have not been open and fair to both political parties and they should realize that half of their clientele is Republican.  I’m not giving Amazon my money any longer.  Along with “big tech” and Bezos’s (fake news) Washington Post, they will push their agenda on the Conservatives. Bezos and Amazon elites should have stayed out of the election as they depend on people like me to make their billions.  Such a business depending on all Americans to survive, should have kept their money and opinions out of politics.",4.0,124,0.7262945955498584,0.2737054044501416,45.07618441207522,Low Trust
