Mrs Margaret Ross,GB,1.0,"I noticed the Amazon Prime van was parked in one of the disabled bay spaces outside my sheltered housing accommodation. He had taken up 1 and 1/2 of the only 2 disabled bays for the building which has 27 flats. I was unable to park my car due to the limited space that was left. I was entering my building as he was exiting. I asked him if he was aware that he'd parked in disabled bay to which he replied"" So what,there's worse things to complain about!"" I told him how inconsiderate this was as I couldn't park my car in the space he had left me. Also there was other spaces he could have parked his van.His reply"" Well tell folk in your building not to order stuff then"" I asked for his name as I was not happy with his attitude, very unprofessional. He wouldn't give me his name. He walked away and made fun of me saying "" Ooh go ahead and report me then spekky!"" This happened at 1pm on Saturday 14th October 23. I feel this kind of attitude towards an elderly disabled person is totally unacceptable.  Does Amazon not do a Customer Service training course for these drivers? If not its about time they did! I am absolutely furious with this driver moreso when other drivers have been very courteous and professional towards every service user who depend on Amazon for their needs. I'd like to think that this review would be taken seriously and dealt with appropriately.",4.0,255,0.7215130333084397,0.27848696669156026,46.7846960631254,Low Trust
