Estela Jennings,US,1.0,"Hey Amazon, Hire New Delivery Drivers No point in paying for Prime if they can't even deliver your packages on time, or deliver them at all. I have had several instances of this. Amazon said ""package will be delivered today"" meanwhile it was sitting in a processing center in India. Amazon is terrible at making estimates apparently.  Most recently, the delivery driver just gave up on finding my address and took it back to the processing center. They provided a ""nonexistent"" tracking number as well.  I live next to a college campus and it is very easy to find where I live. And finally, when packages ARE delivered, they don't bother to double check WHICH APARTMENT to deliver it to, so they send it to either apartment either directly on the left or directly on the right. I don't want to be that person digging through the neighbor's mail to find my stuff!!! It is NOT HARD to double check where a package is supposed to be going, you'd think that would be the most basic job requirement is to know how to read.",1.0,184,0.7074627892443923,0.2925372107556077,46.69079772230085,Low Trust
